{"abstract":"Refleksioner over dimensioner ved kritisk tænkning fra mere \"blød\" kritisk tænkning til \"hård\", hvor fokus er på et kritiske samfundsmæssige - at tænke i alternative samfund. Og videre interviews med nordiske didaktikere","author_count":3,"contributors":["Damgård Jørgensen, Mette","Jakobsen, Carsten Linding","Hansen, Mogens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-751350"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["samfundsvidenskabelige fag"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["POLIS - tidsskrift for samfundsfagsdidaktik"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kritisk tænkning i samfundsfag fagdidaktiske problemstillinger i en skandinavisk kontekst","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/POLIS/article/view/143055","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-751350","ids":["via-0b382c53-fe0f-47be-ac16-d6cb4b374bbb"],"keyword":["samfundsvidenskabelige fag"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5DA64912303F7C3C07B0451740E26AC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/POLIS/article/view/143055","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL University College"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Forsk.center for professionsstudier","VIA, Uddannelser, Læreruddannelsen, HF og FIF-kurser, Lærerudd. Aarhus C samf. og kunstneriske fag"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["POLIS - tidsskrift for samfundsfagsdidaktik"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"damgårdjørgensenpau","last":"Damgård Jørgensen","name":"Damgård Jørgensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Linding","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"0f41513c-767f-4d2d-9ae8-e4f6f8155a8c","name":"Jakobsen, Carsten Linding","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Mogens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["25972774"],"issn_org":["25972766"],"issue":"7","journal":"POLIS - Tidsskrift for samfundsfagsdidaktik","pages":"119-148","publisher":"Columbus","status":"p","title":"POLIS - Tidsskrift for samfundsfagsdidaktik","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","UCL University College","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-0b382c53-fe0f-47be-ac16-d6cb4b374bbb"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Kritisk tænkning i samfundsfag : fagdidaktiske problemstillinger i en skandinavisk kontekst","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-751350","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Ghrelin is an appetite-stimulating hormone secreted from the gastric mucosa in the fasting state, and secretion decreases in response to food intake. After sleeve gastrectomy (SG), plasma concentrations of ghrelin decrease markedly. Whether this affects appetite and glucose tolerance postoperatively is unknown. We investigated the effects of ghrelin infusion on appetite and glucose tolerance in individuals with obesity before and 3 mo after SG. Twelve participants scheduled for SG were included. Before and 3 mo after surgery, a mixed-meal test followed by an ad libitum meal test was performed with concomitant infusions of acyl-ghrelin (1 pmol/kg/min) or placebo. Infusions began 60 min before meal intake to reach a steady state before the mixed-meal and were continued throughout the study day. Two additional experimental days with 0.25 pmol/kg/min and 10 pmol/kg/min of acyl-ghrelin infusions were conducted 3 mo after surgery. Both before and after SG, postprandial glucose concentrations increased dose dependently during ghrelin infusions compared with placebo. Ghrelin infusions inhibited basal and postprandial insulin secretion rates, resulting in lowered measures of β-cell function, but no effect on insulin sensitivity was seen. Ad libitum meal intake was unaffected by the administration of ghrelin. In conclusion, ghrelin infusion increases postprandial plasma glucose concentrations and impairs β-cell function before and after SG but has no effect on ad libitum meal intake. We speculate that the lower concentration of ghrelin after SG may impact glucose metabolism following this procedure.NEW & NOTEWORTHY Ghrelin's effect on glucose tolerance and food intake following sleeve gastrectomy (SG) was evaluated. Acyl-ghrelin was infused during a mixed-meal and ad libitum meals before and 3 mo after surgery. Postprandial glucose concentrations increased during ghrelin infusions, both before and after surgery, while insulin production was inhibited. However, ad libitum meal intake did not differ during ghrelin administration compared with placebo. The decreased ghrelin concentration following SG may contribute to the glycemic control after surgery.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hedbäck, Nora","Dichman, Marie Louise","Hindsø, Morten","Dirksen, Carsten","Jørgensen, Nils Brun","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine Nyvold","Kristiansen, Viggo B.","Rehfeld, Jens F.","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Svane, Maria Saur","Madsbad, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760186"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Appetite","Food intake","Ghrelin","Glucose tolerance","Sleeve gastrectomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of ghrelin on glucose tolerance gut hormones appetite and food intake after sleeve gastrectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpendo.00177.2024","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-760186","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11427089","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85203419458","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39082900","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9deba85a-6da7-43e7-9c97-fac68c85b3a0"],"keyword":["appetite","food intake","ghrelin","glucose tolerance","sleeve gastrectomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76B142C08702583EF09C469C912FA9E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407151366/hedb_ck_et_al_2024_effect_of_ghrelin_on_glucose_tolerance_gut_hormones_appetite_and_food_intake_after_sleeve_gastrectomy_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpendo.00177.2024","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nora","key":"hedbäckpau","last":"Hedbäck","name":"Hedbäck, Nora","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marie Louise","key":"dichmanpau","last":"Dichman","name":"Dichman, Marie Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"hindsøpau","last":"Hindsø","name":"Hindsø, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","locid":"2504d7c9-ee3f-4990-9c1b-10be728b298c","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils Brun","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils Brun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kirstine Nyvold","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"a1de842f-aeb0-4687-bcc1-a5478f6f6bf0","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine Nyvold","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Viggo B.","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Viggo B.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens F.","key":"rehfeldpau","last":"Rehfeld","name":"Rehfeld, Jens F.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Saur","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Maria Saur","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39082900"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpendo.00177.2024","issn":["01931849","15221555"],"issn_org":["01931849"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"American journal of physiology. Endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203419458"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9deba85a-6da7-43e7-9c97-fac68c85b3a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of ghrelin on glucose tolerance, gut hormones, appetite, and food intake after sleeve gastrectomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760186","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"En podwalk gennem kunsthistorien på jagt efter værker af Lene Adler Petersen skabt til det offentlige rum","author_count":3,"contributors":["Anderberg, Birgitte","Neimann Clement, Anne","Jørgensen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779767"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tabula rosa lene adler petersen","src":["kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://artmatter.dk/journal/podcast-tabula-rosa/","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Statens Kunstfond Aage og Johanne Louis-Hansens Fond"],"id":"S01-000.00-779767","ids":["kum-ba806684-1b88-4ce0-973f-1a4782726b78"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C9A820354C7695F78586BD008D49FB17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://soundcloud.com/kunsten-nu/tabula-rosa-lene-adler-petersen?utm_source=clipboard&utm_medium=text&utm_campaign=social_sharing","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://artmatter.dk/journal/podcast-tabula-rosa/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, SMK National Gallery of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"anderbergoth","last":"Anderberg","locid":"3cbef47b-d882-43ad-b64e-0f77ff0d0853","name":"Anderberg, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0002-9612-9516","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"neimannclementppu","last":"Neimann Clement","name":"Neimann Clement, Anne","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"jørgensenppu","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"SoundCloud","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-ba806684-1b88-4ce0-973f-1a4782726b78"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Tabula Rosa : Lene Adler Petersen","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779767","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: About one third of patients with depression are in a condition that can be termed as “difficult-to-treat”. Some evidence suggests that difficult-to-treat depression is associated with a higher frequency of childhood trauma and comorbid personality disorders or accentuated features. However, the condition is understudied, and the effects of psychotherapy for difficult-to-treat depression are currently uncertain. The aim of this trial is to investigate the beneficial and harmful effects of 30 sessions of individual schema therapy versus treatment as usual for difficult-to-treat depression in the Danish secondary, public mental health sector. Methods: In this randomized, multi-centre, parallel-group, superiority clinical trial, 129 outpatients with difficult-to-treat depression will be randomized (1:1) to 30 sessions of individual schema therapy or treatment as usual; in this context mainly group-based, short-term cognitive behaviour or psychodynamic therapy. The primary outcome is the change from baseline in depressive symptoms 12 months after randomization, measured on the observer-rated 6-item Hamilton Rating Scale for Depression. The secondary outcomes are health-related quality of life assessed with the European Quality of Life 5 Dimensions 5 Level Version, functional impairment assessed with the Work and Social Adjustment Scale, psychological wellbeing assessed with the WHO-5 Well-being Index, and negative effects of treatment assessed with the Negative Effects Questionnaire. Exploratory outcomes are improvement on patient self-defined outcomes, personal recovery, anxiety symptoms, anger reactions, metacognitive beliefs about anger, and perseverative negative thinking. Outcomes will be assessed at 6, 12, and 24 months after randomization; the 12-month time-point being the primary time-point of interest. Outcome assessors performing the depression-rating, data managers, statisticians, the data safety and monitoring committee, and conclusion makers for the outcome article will be blinded to treatment allocation and results. To assess cost-effectiveness of the intervention, a health economic analysis will be performed. Discussion: This trial will provide evidence on the beneficial and harmful effects, as well as the cost-effectiveness of schema therapy versus treatment as usual for outpatients with difficult-to-treat depression. The results can potentially improve treatment for a large and understudied patient group. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT05833087. Registered on 15th April 2023 (approved without prompts for revision on 27th April 2023).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Arendt, Ida-Marie Terese Pereira","Gondan, Matthias","Juul, Sophie","Hastrup, Lene Halling","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Bach, Bo","Videbech, Poul","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","Møller, Stine Bjerrum"],"cuid":["S02-098.72-785421"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Arendt, Ida-Marie Terese Pereira"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Innsbruck"],"keyword":["Childhood trauma","Chronic depression","Cognitive Behavioral Therapy methods","Depression diagnosis","Depressive personality disorder","Difficult to treat depression","Humans","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Outpatients","Persistent depressive disorder","Psychotherapy","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Schema therapy","Treatment Outcome","Treatment refractory depression","Treatment resistant depression"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"schema therapy versus treatment as usual for outpatients with difficult to treat depression study protocol for a parallel group randomized clinical trial depre st","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-024-08079-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.72-785421","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11022394","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38627837","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85190680365","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-14bdcdcb-d780-4777-9ee8-7a0dc8f9fd37","sdu-09efdf9e-329b-4203-bfb3-3616dcf3d5f3"],"keyword":["Childhood trauma","Chronic depression","Cognitive Behavioral Therapy/methods","Depression/diagnosis","Depressive personality disorder","Difficult-to-treat depression","Humans","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Outpatients","Persistent depressive disorder","Psychotherapy","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Randomized controlled trial","Schema therapy","Treatment Outcome","Treatment refractory depression","Treatment-resistant depression"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-20CCF245879AC08C8E27D8DBA927BB52"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-024-08079-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/420931236/s13063_024_08079_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/259624267/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, Clinical Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Mental Health Services in the Region of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Region Hovedstadens Psykiatri","Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Psykiatrien Region Sjælland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Marie T.P.","key":"arendtpau","last":"Arendt","locid":"a3868389-3a2d-4d26-ad3e-9335f0c1b08b","name":"Arendt, Ida-Marie Terese Pereira","name_org":"Arendt, Ida Marie T.P.","orcid":"0000-0002-0889-4526","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"gondanpau","last":"Gondan","name":"Gondan, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sophie","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Sophie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Halling","key":"hastruppau","last":"Hastrup","locid":"123c37f8-a704-4f87-b3cf-aad5b59bf6f9","name":"Hastrup, Lene Halling","orcid":"0000-0002-6194-1336","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lene","key":"hallinghastruppau","last":"Halling Hastrup","name":"Halling Hastrup, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 3","first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthøjpau","last":"Hjorthøj","locid":"d4b636e3-7c21-48a0-b812-de219ca78a9e","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Bo","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"3b5fc215-c054-4541-ac5a-029e3c36d85d","name":"Bach, Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-2102-7873","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"videbechpau","last":"Videbech","name":"Videbech, Poul","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Martin Balslev","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"dfc70acd-d15d-44f9-891e-6a7646d1727d","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Bjerrum","key":"moellerpau","last":"Moeller","locid":"54bd623a-c96e-4d6b-ad07-c083a883109c","name":"Møller, Stine Bjerrum","name_org":"Moeller, Stine Bjerrum","orcid":"0000-0002-5019-8065","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38627837"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-024-08079-9","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"journal":"Trials","paperid":"266","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190680365"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-14bdcdcb-d780-4777-9ee8-7a0dc8f9fd37","sdu-09efdf9e-329b-4203-bfb3-3616dcf3d5f3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Schema therapy versus treatment as usual for outpatients with difficult-to-treat depression : Study protocol for a parallel group randomized clinical trial (DEPRE-ST)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.72-785421","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Overweight and obesity are linked to increased hospitalization and mortality in COVID-19 patients. This study aimed to characterize induced immune responses and deep immune cell profiles stratified by BMI in hospitalized COVID-19 patients. Methods and results: This observational multicenter cohort pilot study included 122 adult patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19 in Denmark, stratified by BMI (normal weight, overweight, obese). Inflammation was assessed using TruCulture® and immune cell profiles by flow cytometry with a customized antibody panel (DuraClone®). Patients with obesity had a more pro-inflammatory phenotype with increased TNF-α, IL-8, IL-17, and IL-10 levels post-T cell stimulation, and altered B cell profiles. Patients with obesity showed higher concentrations of naïve, transitional, and non-isotype switched memory B cells, and plasmablasts compared to normal weight patients and healthy controls. Conclusions: Obesity in hospitalized COVID-19 patients may correlate with elevated pro-inflammatory cytokines, anti-inflammatory IL-10, and increased B cell subset activation, highlighting the need for further studies.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Sejdic, Adin","Hartling, Hans Jakob","Gitz Holler, Jon","Klingen Gjærde, Lars","Matovu Dungu, Arnold","Engel Møller, Maria Elizabeth","Svanberg Teglgaard, Rebecca","Utoft Niemann, Carsten Utoft","Brooks, Patrick Terrence","Mogensen, Trine H.","Weis, Nina","Podlekareva, Daria","Baum Jørgensen, Marie Louise","Gang, Anne Ortved","Stampe Hersby, Ditte","Hald, Annemette","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Lebech, Anne Mette","Helleberg, Marie","Lundgren, Jens","Træholt Franck, Kristina","Fischer, Thea K.","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Marquart, Hanne Vibeke","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Lindegaard, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-755996"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sejdic, Adin"],"keyword":["Adaptive Immunity","B cells","BMI","Covid 19","Cytokines","Inflammation","Innate immunity","Obesity","SARS CoV 2","T cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep immune cell phenotyping and induced immune cell responses at admission stratified by bmi in patients hospitalized with covid 000000000019 an observational multicenter cohort pilot study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clim.2024.110336","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-755996","identifier":[{"id":"85201002798","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39117044","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3c8bffd1-be9c-4d93-b9c6-c1d62fbc6a72","ku-29033ce1-e64c-46e4-97f6-14b3d8111d3e"],"keyword":["Adaptive immunity","B cells","BMI","COVID-19","Cytokines","Inflammation","Innate immunity","Obesity","SARS-CoV-2","T cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F0E2B410A0B1A162FD88F2AA8A8F9929"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402066288/1_s2.0_S1521661624004455_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clim.2024.110336","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Med