{"abstract":"The trial aimed to examine the effect of eight weeks preoperative low-load blood flow restricted resistance training (BFR-RT) on physical function, lower limb strength, and patient-reported outcomes in knee OA patients 3 and 12 months after total knee arthroplasty (TKA) compared with preoperative usual care. An assessor blinded randomized controlled trial (RCT) was conducted. Eighty-six patients scheduled for TKA who were allocated to 8 weeks BFR-RT on the affected leg 3x/week or preoperative usual care involving no exercise (CON). Primary outcome: 30-s sit to stand (30STS). Secondary outcomes: Timed Up&Go, 40-m walk test (40mWT), knee range of motion (ROM) 1-repetition maximum (1RM) leg press and knee extensor strength, maximal isometric contraction (MVIC) for the knee extensors and flexors, Knee injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score (KOOS), and Euroqol 5-dimensions (EQ-5D-L5) questionnaire. Data were collected at baseline (12 weeks pre-surgery), ~3 days pre-surgery, 3 and 12 months postoperatively. Intention-to-treat analysis revealed no significant between-group differences in the change from baseline to 3 and 12 months postoperatively on 30STS, TUG, or 40mFWT. Significant between-group differences were observed at 3 but not 12 months postoperatively for the corresponding changes in 1RM leg press strength, 1RM knee extensor strength, and MVIC knee extensor favoring BFR-RT. No between-group differences were observed for the delta changes from baseline in knee ROM, KOOS subscales or EQ-5D-L5 at any postoperative time points. These findings suggest that preoperative BFR-RT offered no superior effects compared with usual preoperative care on postoperative physical function or patient-reported outcomes. Preoperative BFR-RT produced amplified gains in lower limb muscle strength at 3 months postoperatively. Trial Registration: NCT04081493.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Stian Langgård","Aagaard, Per","Bohn, Marie Bagger","Hansen, Peter","Hansen, Per Moller","Holm, Carsten","Mortensen, Louise","Garval, Mette","Reimer, Lisa Cecilie Urup","Mechlenburg, Inger"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-768007"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Stian Langgård"],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee rehabilitation","Blood Flow Restriction Therapy","Female","Humans","Lower Extremity blood supply","Male","Middle Aged","Muscle Strength physiology","Occlusion training","Osteoarthritis Knee surgery","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Physical function","Postoperative Period","Prehabilitation","Preoperative Exercise","Range of Motion Articular","Resistance Training methods","exercise medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of blood flow restriction exercise prior to total knee arthroplasty on postoperative physical function lower limb strength and patient reported outcomes a randomized controlled trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14750","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by grants from the Health Research Foundation of Central Denmark Region, Aase & Ejnar Danielsens Foundation, Nis-Hanssens Mindes legat, The Family Hede Nielsen Foundation, Brother's Hartmann Foundation, Augustinus Foundation, William Demant Foundation, The Danish Association of Physiotherapy Foundation. The funders of the study had no role in study design, data collection, data analysis, data interpretation, or conclusions of this trial."],"id":"S02-100.00-768007","identifier":[{"id":"39461901","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85207572917","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f36cc4bf-6b9a-451f-a5c1-83b1c56ffddd","sdu-318b95fd-b21b-438c-8639-e77ba7c9b416"],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/rehabilitation","Blood Flow Restriction Therapy","Female","Humans","Lower Extremity/blood supply","Male","Middle Aged","Muscle Strength/physiology","Osteoarthritis, Knee/surgery","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Postoperative Period","Preoperative Exercise","Range of Motion, Articular","Resistance Training/methods","exercise medicine","occlusion training","physical function","prehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-814838AF227FB41DA702650292779621"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275836301/Scandinavian_Med_Sci_Sports_-_2024_-_J_rgensen_-_The_Effect_of_Blood_Flow_Restriction_Exercise_Prior_to_Total_Knee.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.14750","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Ortopædkirurgi, Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3n