//local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785467","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Article 110 TFEU prohibits Member States (MS) from imposing discriminatory or protective internal taxation on products from other MS. The provision is closely linked to and must be understood in connection with: the prohibition of internal customs duties in Article 30 TFEU (➔ Article 30 TFEU para 3–5); the principle of the free movement of goods in Articles 26 and 28 TFEU; and the prohibition in Article 34 TFEU of quantitative restrictions between MS and all charges having equivalent effect (➔ Article 34 TFEU para 4 et seqq.). These provisions aim to ensure the free movement of goods between MS under normal conditions of competition. The function of Article 110 TFEU is to prevent MS circumventing these provisions by imposing internal taxation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","Terkilsen, Lars Kjærgård"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-220463"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["EU ret","Interne afgifter"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["KPMG Acor Tax"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"article 000000000110 discriminatory and protective internal taxation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-220463","ids":["au-9ff77728-d7a4-4866-877b-a88e7e50b309"],"keyword":["EU-ret","Interne afgifter","TEUF 110"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-90449948EE8017FFE24CC96A4940F9E4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["KPMG Acor Tax"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Willemoes","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"69969451-0c6e-42f9-bbbc-ee6c03b2464f","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","orcid":"0000-0001-5880-7294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Kjærgård","key":"terkilsenpau","last":"Terkilsen","name":"Terkilsen, Lars Kjærgård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/16559_2022_41","pages":"1-20","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Springer Commentaries on International and European Law"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9ff77728-d7a4-4866-877b-a88e7e50b309"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Article 110 [Discriminatory and Protective Internal Taxation]","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220463","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Traditional conceptions of personality disorder (PD) view severe identity disturbance as a defining characteristic of borderline personality disorder (BPD). In the alternative DSM-5 model for PDs (AMPD) and in the outlined substantial changes to PD diagnostics in ICD-11, disturbances in self and identity are elevated from a specific diagnostic criterion for BPD to a defining criterion for PD in general. In line with Kernberg’s theory of personality organization (PO), it is expected that although identity disturbance may be characteristic of most or all PDs, severe identity diffusion is a more pronounced and defining characteristic of BPD and possibly other PDs organized on a borderline level (BPO). Here, we examined the level of identity disturbance in SCID-diagnosed patients with BPD, narcissistic PD (NPD), avoidant PD (AVPD), comorbid BPD with NPD and AVDP, as well as other specified PD (PD-OT). We found that measures of identity diffusion were higher in BPD and NPD patients compared with patients diagnosed with AVPD. Hierarchical multiple regression analyses showed that number of SCID criteria met for BPD and NPD predicted level of identity diffusion when gender, age and general symptomatology were controlled for, whereas number of SCID criteria met for AVPD did not. The presented data support severe identity diffusion as a prominent characteristic of BPD with possible implications for how we should differentiate BPD from other PDs. The findings are discussed in relation to Kernberg’s model and the AMPD.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten René","Rasmussen, Anne Scharling","Bøye, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-668345"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Carsten René"],"keyword":["Borderline personality disorder","Identity disturbance","identity diffusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"level of identity diffusion in patients with borderline narcissistic avoidant and other specified personality disorder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85152904999","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-668345","identifier":[{"id":"85152904999","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-816289d9-3ac9-4e4d-a80f-212114598eb3"],"keyword":["borderline personality disorder","identity diffusion","identity disturbance","personality disorder assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-734C222D8735BA62F84FF3B5E70B8CBC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Scharling","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"b7723e07-5e65-4a2d-a159-5b963d34e1b8","name":"Rasmussen, Anne Scharling","orcid":"0000-0002-7853-9271","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bøyepau","last":"Bøye","locid":"c816211a-6dc5-4594-ba92-a5d3aa050cde","name":"Bøye, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19012276.2023.2197561","issn":["09008772","19040016"],"issn_org":["19012276"],"issue":"3","journal":"Nordic Psychology","pages":"302-316","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Nordic Psychology","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152904999"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-816289d9-3ac9-4e4d-a80f-212114598eb3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Level of identity diffusion in patients with borderline, narcissistic, avoidant and other specified personality disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-668345","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Shame is an essential affect in many patients with borderline personality disorder (BPD) and can be associated with most of the BPD diagnostic criteria. Severe shame is a highly aversive emotion with concomitant beliefs about the self as deeply inferior, insignificant, disgusting, and unloved. Shame and how it is manifested in the subjective experience and behavior in people diagnosed with BPD is remarkably under-researched, and our knowledge of the phenomenology of shame in BPD needs to be improved. Severe shame is often less accessible and available to conscious awareness, making it difficult to access via questionnaires and self-report measures. Therefore, this study is based on semi-structured interviews with 21 women Structural clinical interview for DSM-5 disorders' diagnosed with BPD. All interviews were analyzed using the interpretive phenomenological approach. Based on the analysis, the participants' descriptions of how severe shame manifests itself in their subjective experience and behavior are classified into 10 themes: the self is deeply flawed and unlovable; self-hatred/self-contempt; eye contact is awkward and shameful; shameful over being mentally ill; shameful identity diffusion; hiding behind façade/social roles; pleasing others/performing to avoid shame; self-destructive behavior to mitigate shame; sex associated with shame; and shame during the therapy session. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2024 APA, all rights reserved).","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten René","Bøye, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-727999"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Borderline Personality Disorder psychology","Borderline personality disorder","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Phenomenology","Qualitative Research","Qualitative study","Self Concept","Sexual Behavior","Shame","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i am ashamed that i exist i feel like apologizing for existing the phenomenology of shame in patients with borderline personality disorder a qualitative study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1037/per0000655","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-727999","identifier":[{"id":"85189183917","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38330356","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9a26c8e4-965a-4dac-abe7-8a145cb1c885"],"keyword":["Adult","Borderline Personality Disorder/psychology","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Qualitative Research","Self Concept","Young Adult","borderline personality disorder","phenomenology","qualitative study","sexual behavior","shame"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CFB1677F921061AAEF5F22705C68F87C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/370343666/I_am_ashamed_that_I_exist._I_feel_like_apologizing_for_existing_Accepted_manuscript_2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1037/per0000655","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten R.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","name_org":"Jørgensen, Carsten R.","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bøyepau","last":"Bøye","locid":"c816211a-6dc5-4594-ba92-a5d3aa050cde","name":"Bøye, Rikke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38330356"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1037/per0000655","issn":["19492715","19492723"],"issn_org":["19492715"],"issue":"3","journal":"Personality Disorders: Theory, Research, and Treatment","pages":"181-192","publisher":"American Psychological Association","status":"p","title":"Personality Disorders: Theory, Research, and Treatment","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189183917"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9a26c8e4-965a-4dac-abe7-8a145cb1c885"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"\"I am ashamed that I exist. I feel like apologizing for existing\" : The phenomenology of shame in patients with borderline personality disorder: A qualitative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-727999","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The barley powdery mildew fungus, Blumeria hordei (Bh), secretes hundreds of candidate secreted effector proteins (CSEPs) to facilitate pathogen infection and colonization. One of these, CSEP0008, is directly recognized by the barley nucleotide-binding leucine-rich-repeat (NLR) receptor MLA1 and therefore is designated AVRA1. Here, we show that AVRA1 and the sequence-unrelated Bh effector BEC1016 (CSEP0491) suppress immunity in barley. We used yeast two-hybrid next-generation interaction screens (Y2H-NGIS), followed by binary Y2H and in planta protein–protein interactions studies, and identified a common barley target of AVRA1 and BEC1016, the endoplasmic reticulum (ER)-localized J-domain protein HvERdj3B. Silencing of this ER quality control (ERQC) protein increased Bh penetration. HvERdj3B is ER luminal, and we showed using split GFP that AVRA1 and BEC1016 translocate into the ER signal peptide-independently. Overexpression of the two effectors impeded trafficking of a vacuolar marker through the ER; silencing of HvERdj3B also exhibited this same cellular phenotype, coinciding with the effectors targeting this ERQC component. Together, these results suggest that the barley innate immunity, preventing Bh entry into epidermal cells, requires ERQC. Here, the J-domain protein HvERdj3B appears to be essential and can be regulated by AVRA1 and BEC1016. Plant disease resistance often occurs upon direct or indirect recognition of pathogen effectors by host NLR receptors. Previous work has shown that AVRA1 is directly recognized in the cytosol by the immune receptor MLA1. We speculate that the AVRA1 J-domain target being inside the ER, where it is inapproachable by NLRs, has forced the plant to evolve this challenging direct recognition.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Li, Zizhang","Velásquez-Zapata, Valeria","Elmore, J. Mitch","Li, Xuan","Xie, Wenjun","Deb, Sohini","Tian, Xiao","Banerjee, Sagnik","Jørgensen, Hans Jørgen Lyngs","Pedersen, Carsten","Wise, Roger P.","Thordal-Christensen, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-740057"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Corn Insects and Crop Genetics Research Unit","Iowa State University"],"keyword":["Barley","ER quality control","ERdj3b","Immunity","Pathogen effectors","Powdery mildew","signal peptide independent ER uptake","yeast two hybrid next generation interaction screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"powdery mildew effectors avr sub a000000000001 sub and bec000000001016 target the er j domain protein i hv i erdj000000000003b required for immunity in barley","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/mpp.13463","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-740057","identifier":[{"id":"38695677","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001215977500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC11064805","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85192035338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f0a949b6-aee9-44b2-9a0f-b92d966f8f3a"],"keyword":["ER quality control","ERdj3b","barley","immunity","pathogen effectors","powdery mildew","signal peptide-independent ER-uptake","yeast two-hybrid next-generation interaction screening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1276F9DF28BF37BEFA2B2ABB27AE5D8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/mpp.13463","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391744157/Molecular_Plant_Pathology_2024_Li_Powdery_mildew_effectors_AVRA1_and_BEC1016_target_the_ER_J_domain_protein_HvERdj3B.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"iowa state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Iowa State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"corn insects and crop genetics research unit","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Corn Insects and Crop Genetics Research Unit","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zizhang","key":"lizizhangpau","last":"Li","locid":"a470deab-a3da-4c0f-a882-83026248cbad","name":"Li, Zizhang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Valeria","key":"velásquezzapatavaleriapau","last":"Velásquez-Zapata","name":"Velásquez-Zapata, Valeria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"J. Mitch","key":"elmorejmitchpau","last":"Elmore","name":"Elmore, J. Mitch","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuan","key":"lixuanpau","last":"Li","locid":"2b8054a3-f72e-4c23-9da5-c547c75ebb07","name":"Li, Xuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wenjun","key":"xiewenjunpau","last":"Xie","locid":"2575d7cd-b9f4-4383-a34f-d1d98c7284a8","name":"Xie, Wenjun","orcid":"0000-0001-8101-5519","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sohini","key":"debsohinipau","last":"Deb","locid":"c57688f1-092a-44ad-b4d9-7d0965c8e0e8","name":"Deb, Sohini","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao","key":"tianxiaopau","last":"Tian","locid":"6c7da93d-bf14-404b-8b6f-a78f913c7e22","name":"Tian, Xiao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sagnik","key":"banerjeesagnikpau","last":"Banerjee","name":"Banerjee, Sagnik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans J.L.","key":"jørgensenhansjørgenlyngspau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1b3f39b0-a166-4a0c-96ea-e6c3dd0de338","name":"Jørgensen, Hans Jørgen Lyngs","name_org":"Jørgensen, Hans J.L.","orcid":"0000-0002-5902-6550","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"pedersencarstenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7750ab11-4cc4-4421-8073-4a339254a400","name":"Pedersen, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0002-9520-2232","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Roger P.","key":"wiserogerppau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Roger P.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"thordalchristensenhanspau","last":"Thordal-Christensen","locid":"3e904207-07a2-412e-969f-3272f1fe12c5","name":"Thordal-Christensen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0001-8813-0157","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38695677"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/mpp.13463","issn":["13643703","14646722"],"issn_org":["14646722"],"issue":"5","journal":"Molecular Plant Pathology","paperid":"e13463","status":"p","title":"Molecular Plant Pathology","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192035338"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f0a949b6-aee9-44b2-9a0f-b92d966f8f3a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Powdery mildew effectors AVR<sub>A1</sub> and BEC1016 target the ER J-domain protein <i>Hv</i>ERdj3B required for immunity in barley","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-740057","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
