{"abstract":"Article 111 TFEU is the counterpart to Article 110 TFEU. It concerns exports of products to other MS whereas Article 110 TFEU concerns imports from other MS (➔ Article 110 TFEU para 1–4). Article 111 TFEU is aimed at preventing MS from using the repayment of internal taxes to distort competition in the internal market, by repaying more than what was initially levied. Thus, Article 111 TFEU is linked not only to the rules on the free movement of goods, but also to the State aid rules in Article 107 TFEU (➔ Article 107 TFEU).","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","Terkilsen, Lars Kjærgård"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-181629"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["EU ret","Forbud","Interne afgifter"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"article 000000000111 tax repayments for exported products","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-181629","ids":["au-5bb53519-326a-4159-b36c-bb72bf5c2bda"],"keyword":["EU-ret","Interne afgifter","TEUF 111","forbud","udførsel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-705C22E2C57CD2A39B1B06AE40B4E6A0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Willemoes","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"69969451-0c6e-42f9-bbbc-ee6c03b2464f","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","orcid":"0000-0001-5880-7294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Kjærgård","key":"terkilsenpau","last":"Terkilsen","locid":"724e3cb7-a63d-4e67-9695-ade9fb90b111","name":"Terkilsen, Lars Kjærgård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/16559_2022_42","pages":"1-2","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer International Publishing","status":"p","title":"Springer Commentaries on International and European Law"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5bb53519-326a-4159-b36c-bb72bf5c2bda"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Article 111 [Tax Repayments for Exported Products]","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-181629","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In the case of charges other than1 turnover taxes, excise duties and other forms of indirect taxation, remissions and repayments in respect of exports to other Member States may not be granted and countervailing charges in respect of imports from Member States may not be imposed3 unless the measures contemplated have been previously approved for a limited period4 by the Council2 on a proposal from the Commission.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","Terkilsen, Lars Kjærgård"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-216504"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["EU ret"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"article 000000000112 approval of reimbursements","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-216504","ids":["au-99053434-fb46-4337-aecd-ad6dc1240028"],"keyword":["EU-ret","EUTK 112","Godtgørelse af afgifter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-194AF3AC4A860D160313B0AE03B45281"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Willemoes","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"69969451-0c6e-42f9-bbbc-ee6c03b2464f","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten Willemoes","orcid":"0000-0001-5880-7294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Kjærgård","key":"terkilsenpau","last":"Terkilsen","locid":"724e3cb7-a63d-4e67