{"abstract":"Background: Vaccine breakthrough SARS-CoV-2 infections are common and of clinical and public health concern. However, little is known about the immunological characteristics of patients hospitalized due to these infections. We aimed to investigate and compare immune cell subpopulations and induced immune responses in vaccinated and non-vaccinated patients hospitalized with severe COVID-19. Methods: A nested case-control study on adults (≥ 18 years) who received at least two doses of a mRNA-COVID-19 vaccine and were hospitalized with SARS-CoV-2 breakthrough infections and severe COVID-19 between January 7, 2021, and February 1, 2022, were eligible for inclusion. Age- and sex-matched non-vaccinated controls were identified. Immunophenotyping was performed using a custom-designed 10-color flow cytometry prefabricated freeze-dried antibody panel (DuraClone, Beckman Coulter (BC), Brea, Calif). TruCulture (Myriad RBM, Austin, USA) was used to assess induced immune response in whole blood, revealing different critical signaling pathways as a proxy for immune function. All samples were obtained within 48 hours of admission. Results: In total, 20 hospitalized patients with severe COVID-19 and a breakthrough SARS-CoV-2 infection were included, ten vaccinated and ten non-vaccinated patients. Vaccinated patients had lower concentrations of CD19 B cells (p = 0.035), naïve CD4 T cells (p = 0.015), a higher proportion of γδ1 T cells (p = 0.019), and higher unstimulated immune cell release of IL-10 (p = 0.015). Conclusion: We observed immunological differences between vaccinated and non-vaccinated patients hospitalized due to severe COVID-19 that indicate that vaccinated patients had lower B cell concentrations, lower concentrations of CD4 naïve T cells, a skewed gamma-delta V1/V2 ratio, and an exaggerated IL-10 response at admission. These results could indicate a suboptimal immune response involved in SARS-CoV-2 breakthrough infections that cause severe COVID-19 in vaccinated adults. However, the sample size was small, and further research is needed to confirm these results.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Sejdic, Adin","Hartling, Hans Jakob","Holler, Jon Gitz","Klingen Gjærde, Lars","Lindegaard, Birgitte","Dungu, Arnold Matovu","Gnesin, Filip","Møller, Maria Elizabeth Engel","Teglgaard, Rebecca Svanberg","Niemann, Carsten Utoft","Brooks, Patrick Terrence","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Franck, Kristina Træholt","Fischer, Thea K.","Marquart, Hanne Vibeke","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747565"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cytokines","Inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immune cell populations and induced immune responses at admission in patients hospitalized with vaccine breakthrough sars cov 000000000002 infections","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2024.1360843","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747565","identifier":[{"id":"38903511","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11188326","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85196264601","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1b19bb04-3dd8-4f8c-84fc-a7f9a873b268"],"keyword":["cytokines","immune cell populations","inflammation","mRNA vaccine against SARS-CoV2","vaccine breakthrough infection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D3E72B5AF60312DB825496B3DF582FD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2024.1360843","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395995088/fimmu_15_1360843.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Adin","key":"sejdicpau","last":"Sejdic","locid":"743c05e9-0a74-49b7-aca7-f3ddbb4d8742","name":"Sejdic, Adin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hans Jakob","key":"hartlingpau","last":"Hartling","name":"Hartling, Hans Jakob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jon Gitz","key":"hollerpau","last":"Holler","name":"Holler, Jon Gitz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"klingengjærdepau","last":"Klingen Gjærde","name":"Klingen Gjærde, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Birgitte","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"f8c3a235-1f94-4c1d-afe3-c6c7f9b31002","name":"Lindegaard, Birgitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Arnold Matovu","key":"dungupau","last":"Dungu","name":"Dungu, Arnold Matovu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Filip","key":"gnesinpau","last":"Gnesin","name":"Gnesin, Filip","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria Elizabeth Engel","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Maria Elizabeth Engel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rebecca Svanberg","key":"teglgaardpau","last":"Teglgaard","name":"Teglgaard, Rebecca Svanberg","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Carsten Utoft","key":"niemannpau","last":"Niemann","locid":"c34cbf81-3f48-4443-8481-b428de733daa","name":"Niemann, Carsten Utoft","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Patrick Terrence","key":"brookspau","last":"Brooks","name":"Brooks, Patrick Terrence","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kristina Træholt","key":"franckpau","last":"Franck","name":"Franck, Kristina Træholt","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Thea K.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"97c4bf8d-8bd1-470b-8e0b-91eb4faf7703","name":"Fischer, Thea K.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Hanne Vibeke","key":"marquartpau","last":"Marquart","locid":"9b5af5d9-9f83-4dd4-a91c-140cd128fb8c","name":"Marquart, Hanne Vibeke","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Zitta Barrella","key":"harboepau","last":"Harboe","locid":"2b596a33-5659-4236-b5ea-c0991866af44","name":"Harboe, Zitta Barrella","orcid":"0000-0001-5552-0095","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38903511"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fimmu.2024.1360843","issn":["16643224"],"journal":"Frontiers in Immunology","paperid":"1360843","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Immunology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196264601"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1b19bb04-3dd8-4f8c-84fc-a7f9a873b268"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Immune cell populations and induced immune responses at admission in patients hospitalized with vaccine breakthrough SARS-CoV-2 infections","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747565","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This book discusses the pivotal role of shame in a wide range of mental disorders and as a driving force in societal polarization and escalating conflicts between nations and population groups. Exploring the phenomenology of one of the most vulnerable and painful of human emotions, shame, Jørgensen dives deep into its many facets and the ways in which it manifests in mental illnesses and everyday life. Delving into an in-depth discussion of the differentiation between the moral and ethical feelings of guilt and shame, he presses the need to distinguish between constructive and destructive feelings of shame. He examines how shame permeates societal and cultural expectations, on both individual and collective levels. Solution-centric in its approach, the author not only discusses the destructive feelings of shame particularly common among individuals with more severe mental disorders, but also offers specific advice to therapists on how to deal with it. The book will be an essential read for psychoanalysts, psychotherapists, philosophers, and anyone wanting to understand the power of shame in our lives.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786918"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding and working with shame psychotherapeutic cultural and philosophical perspectives","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85210830574","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-786918","identifier":[{"id":"85210830574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2883a3bd-3230-4c9d-a679-d18d27285a94"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mr