,"title":"Kulturen i dansk psykiatri må forandres","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-676034","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Postprandial hypoglycemia is a complication of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB), but the effects of postprandial exercise and meal glycemic index (GI) on postprandial glucose and glucoregulatory hormone responses are unknown. Ten RYGB-operated and 10 age and weight-matched unoperated women completed four test days in random order ingesting mixed meals with high GI (HGI, GI = 93) or low GI (LGI, GI = 54), but matched on energy and macronutrient content. Ten minutes after meal completion, participants rested or cycled for 30 min at 70% of maximum oxygen uptake (V̇o2max). Blood was collected for 4 h. Postprandial exercise did not lower plasma nadir glucose in RYGB after HGI (HGI/rest 3.7 ± 0.5 vs. HGI/Ex 4.1 ± 0.4 mmol/L, P = 0.070). Replacing HGI with LGI meals raised glucose nadir in RYGB (LGI/rest 4.1 ± 0.5 mmol/L, P = 0.034) and reduced glucose excursions (Δpeak-nadir) but less so in RYGB (-14% [95% CI: -27; -1]) compared with controls (-33% [-51; -14]). Insulin responses mirrored glucose concentrations. Glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) responses were greater in RYGB versus controls, and higher with HGI versus LGI. Glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) responses were greater after HGI versus LGI in both groups. Postexercise glucagon responses were lower in RYGB than controls, and noradrenaline responses tended to be lower in RYGB, whereas adrenaline responses were similar between groups. In conclusion, moderate intensity cycling shortly after meal intake did not increase the risk of postprandial hypoglycemia after RYGB. The low GI meal increased nadir glucose and reduced glucose excursions compared with the high GI meal. RYGB participants had lower postexercise glucagon responses compared with controls.NEW & NOTEWORTHY We investigate the effect of moderate exercise after a high or a low glycemic index meal on nadir glucose and glucoregulatory hormones in gastric bypass-operated individuals and in matched unoperated controls. Cycling shortly after meal intake did not increase the risk of hypoglycemia in operated individuals. The low glycemic index meal increased glucose nadir and reduced excursions compared with the high glycemic index meal. Operated individuals had lower postexercise glucagon responses compared with controls.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ternhamar, Tummas","Møller, Andreas","Martinussen, Christoffer","Svane, Maria S.","Hindsø, Morten","Jørgensen, Nils B.","Dirksen, Carsten","Jensen, Jens-Erik Beck","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Kiens, Bente","Madsbad, Sten","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702329"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exercise","Glycemic Index","Mixed meal test","Postprandial hypoglycemia","Roux en Y gastric bypass"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of postprandial exercise and meal glycemic index on plasma glucose and glucoregulatory hormone responses after roux en y gastric bypass","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407603789/The_effects_of_postprandial_exercise.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-702329","identifier":[{"id":"85174752182","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37755455","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ccc41f82-2e89-4d8a-845e-21257eb86b47"],"keyword":["Roux-en-Y gastric bypass","exercise","glycemic index","mixed meal test","postprandial hypoglycemia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6FD71191EF74F18D62B51B2789C8D92A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407603789/The_effects_of_postprandial_exercise.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tummas","key":"ternhamarpau","last":"Ternhamar","name":"Ternhamar, Tummas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","name":"Martinussen, Christoffer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria S.","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Maria S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"hindsøpau","last":"Hindsø","name":"Hindsø, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils B.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Erik Beck","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d1f25271-f70a-4e26-a035-