{"abstract":"Background Collaborative care (CC) and consultation liaison (CL) are two conceptual models aiming to improve mental healthcare in primary care. The effects of these models have not been compared in a Danish setting. Aims To examine the effects of CC versus CL for persons with anxiety and depression in Danish general practices (trial registration: NCT03113175 and NCT03113201). Method Two randomised parallel superiority trials for anxiety disorders and depression were carried out in 2018-2019. In the CC-group, care managers collaborated with general practitioners (GPs) to provide evidence-based treatment according to structured treatment plans. They followed up and provided psychoeducation and/or cognitive-behavioural therapy. The GPs initiated pharmacological treatment if indicated, and a psychiatrist provided supervision. In the CL-group, the intervention consisted of the GP's usual treatment. However, the psychiatrist and care manager could be consulted. Primary outcomes were depression symptoms (Beck Depression Inventory-II, BDI-II) in the depression trial and anxiety symptoms (Beck Anxiety Inventory, BAI) in the anxiety trial at 6-month follow-up. Results In total, 302 participants with anxiety disorders and 389 participants with depression were included. A significant difference in BDI-II score was found in the depression trial, with larger symptom reductions in the CC-group (CC: 12.7, 95% CI 11.4-14.0; CL: 17.5, 95% CI 16.2-18.9; Cohen's d = -0.50, P ≤ 0.001). There was a significant difference in BAI in the anxiety trial (CC: 14.9, 95% CI 13.5-16.3; CL: 17.9, 95% CI 16.5-19.3; Cohen's d = -0.34, P ≤ 0.001), with larger symptom reductions in the CC-group. Conclusions Collaborative care was an effective model to improve outcomes for persons with depression and anxiety disorders.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Curth, Nadja Kehler","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Brinck-Claussen, Ursula","Jorgensen, Kirstine Bro","Rosendal, Susanne","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Nordentoft, Merete","Eplov, Lene Falgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-696510"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anxiety disorders","Depressive disorders","Primary care","Randomised controlled trial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of collaborative care versus consultation liaison for anxiety disorders and depression in denmark two randomised controlled trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1192/bjp.2023.77","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-696510","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10895499","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37395101","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164906705","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-de4aeb88-a94c-4d0a-99cd-15c4f862d368"],"keyword":["Anxiety disorders","cognitive-behavioural therapies","depressive disorders","primary care","randomised controlled trial"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0580E734872058B237A5E8FF47AC9EBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1192/bjp.2023.77","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/368204830/the_effects_of_collaborative_care_versus_consultation_liaison_for_anxiety_disorders_and_depression_in_denmark_two_randomised_controlled_trials.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nadja Kehler","key":"curthpau","last":"Curth","name":"Curth, Nadja Kehler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthojpau","last":"Hjorthoj","locid":"d4b636e3-7c21-48a0-b812-de219ca78a9e","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","name_org":"Hjorthoj, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ursula","key":"brinckclaussenpau","last":"Brinck-Claussen","name":"Brinck-Claussen, Ursula","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine Bro","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, Kirstine Bro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne","key":"rosendalpau","last":"Rosendal","name":"Rosendal, Susanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Bo","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Anders Bo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37395101"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1192/bjp.2023.77","issn":["00071250","09605371"],"issn_org":["00071250"],"issue":"3","journal":"British Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"430-437","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"223"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164906705"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-de4aeb88-a94c-4d0a-99cd-15c4f862d368"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of collaborative care versus consultation liaison for anxiety disorders and depression in Denmark : Two randomised controlled trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-696510","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: A better understanding of factors that influence functioning may improve the identification of patients with distal radius fractures (DRFs) who need hand therapy. The purpose of this scoping review was to provide a comprehensive overview of factors that have been evaluated for their influence on hand functioning following volar plate fixation of DRFs. MATERIAL AND METHODS: 6 databases were searched from 2005 to 2021 for publications regarding surgical treatment for a DRF with a volar locking plate. Included studies evaluated demographic, perioperative, and postoperative factors within the 6 weeks post-surgery for their influence on functioning at least 3 months post-surgery. Functioning was assessed with patient-reported outcome measures. The factors were categorized into themes and mapped to the International Classification of Functioning, Disability and Health (ICF). RESULTS: 148 studies were included. 708 factors were categorized into 39 themes (e.g. pain) and mapped to the ICF components. The themes were primarily mapped to \"body functions and structures\" (n = 26) and rarely to \"activities and participation\" (n = 5). Fracture type (n = 40), age (n = 38), and sex (n = 22) were the most frequently evaluated factors. CONCLUSION: This scoping review identified an extensive number of factors evaluated within 6 weeks after surgery for their influence on functioning at least 3 months after volar plate fixation of a DRF and the existing research has primarily evaluated factors related to \"body functions and structures,\" with limited focus on factors related to \"activities and participation.\"","author_count":11,"contributors":["Boel, Susanne","Vinther, Anders","Hansen, Alice Ørts","Juhl, Carsten Bogh","Landgren, Marcus","Schøler Jacobsen, Nicolaj","Paulsen, Camilla P.","Thomas Jørgensen, Claus","Kristensen, Hanne Kaae"],"cuid":["S03-098.11-735523"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Boel, Susanne"],"keyword":["Functioning","ICF","Radius Fractures"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Danish Health Authority"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors influencing functioning after volar locking plate fixation of distal radius fractures a scoping review of 000000000148 studies","src":["ku","sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2023.13431","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.11-735523","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10253938","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37293983","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85163181282","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7b110610-eab0-4c65-94ae-b03a00fecd93","sdu-f03e3899-c511-426c-9058-2ed7219facc2","ucl-e1ec9599-0d2f-458c-bcca-ae101e204a61"],"keyword":["Functioning","ICF","Radius Fractures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-64F5E151249ACCDCA5729631CC51D4FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391314614/document.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/232916849/document.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2023.13431","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU Uni