5","publisher":"Miljøstyreslen","repno":"Pesticides Research, No. 207","series":"Pesticides Research","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","pj-bluetech aps (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bac05e25-ab45-4adc-8530-097a5233b23b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ancient root macropores and fractures in glacial till and their contribution to pesticide vulnerability of groundwater in low- and high-ground agricultural landscape : Pestpore2","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732236","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose: With the introduction of hybrid magnetic resonance linacs (MR-linac), improved imaging has enabled daily treatment adaptation. However, the use of gadolinium based contrast agents (GBCAs) is desired to further improve MR image contrast. GBCAs are in the form of a non-toxic metalorganic gadolinium complex, but toxic un-chelated aqueous gadolinium(III), Gd3+(aq), can be released in patients if the organic ligand is degraded by the radiation. In this study, T-1 relaxation measurements were performed to study the effect of radiation on three GBCAs. Materials and methods: GBCAs, gadoteric acid, gadobutrol and gadoxectic acid were investigated in a concentration range of 10-100 mM. Measurements were performed on a 500 MHz nuclear MR (NMR) spectrometer with a high-resolution inversion recovery sequence to determine T-1. Samples were irradiated with 7 MV photons on an MR-linac to a total dose of 100 Gy. The lower detection limit of Gd3+(aq) was established by estimating the overall measurement uncertainty and comparing to corresponding changes in R1 when replacing chelated Gd3+ with gadolinium nitrate at predefined percentages. Results: The overall measurement uncertainty was estimated to +/- 0.0053 ms(-1), corresponding to Gd3+(aq) detection levels 1%-1.5% or 1-4.5 micro molar at clinical GBCA dosage. No detectable differences in R-1 were observed between irradiated and non-irradiated samples for any GBCA. Conclusions: This study did not find any measurable degradation of GBCAs due to irradiation with high-energy X-rays, however, in-vivo investigations are needed to provide the clinical basis for safe use of contrast agents in a radiotherapy workflow.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mahmood, Faisal","Nielsen, Ulla Gro","Jorgensen, Christian Brandt","Brink, Carsten","Thomsen, Henrik S","Hansen, Rasmus Hvass"],"cuid":["S02-095.36-040757"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Mahmood, Faisal"],"keyword":["Gadolinium based contrast agent","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","NMR relaxometry","Radiation","Radiotherapy","Safety","Toxicity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety of gadolinium based contrast agents in magnetic resonance imaging guided radiotherapy an investigation of chelate stability using relaxometry","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.phro.2022.02.015","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Authors are thankful to Benny Clifford Buthler, Department of Oncology, Odense University Hospital, for construction of the phantom for NMR tube irradiation, and colleagues at the Laboratory of Radiation Physics, Odense University Hospital, for technical assistance. This work was supported by a grant from Danish Cancer Society (Grant no. R231-A13852). Faisal Mahmood and Carsten Brink acknowledge support from MANTRA (New MAgNetic resonance Technology for Response Adapted radiotherapy), a Frontline research center based at Odense University Hospital, Denmark, and AgeCare (Academy of Geriatric Cancer Research), an international research collaboration based at Odense University Hospital, Denmark."],"id":"S02-095.36-040757","identifier":[{"id":"85125281043","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8885577","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000804745500003","type":"wos"},{"id":"35243039","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-203e599c-7af3-46e0-a353-abaa4ee4d7dd","sdu-d9e8bcda-c8dc-4c0a-871c-c9e954339cfa"],"keyword":["Gadolinium based contrast agent","Magnetic resonance imaging","NMR relaxometry","RADIATION","Radiotherapy","Safety","Toxicity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AF0755CA1B04F71C9000B87EDD3455CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/315759512/1_s2.0_S2405631622000203_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.phro.2022.02.015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/199864740/1_s2.0_S2405631622000203_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Faisal","key":"mahmoodpau","last":"Mahmood","locid":"a29cdf63-9a6e-411f-9491-078a1942861e","name":"Mahmood, Faisal","orcid":"0000-0002-7270-7967","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Gro","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"564677e7-90aa-4240-bb0e-002f5dfc1d5c","name":"Nielsen, Ulla Gro","orcid":"0000-0002-2336-3061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Brandt","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"46f4577d-f9cb-4d0d-a632-485effd5c3e7","name":"Jørgensen, Christian Brandt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"brinkpau","last":"Brink","locid":"1392b95d-bbe7-4a00-bc48-aa402170385e","name":"Brink, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3906-1962","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik S.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c1b9dc28-6145-43cc-a1e7-c8a93ab22ec7","name":"Thomsen, Henrik S","name_org":"Thomsen, Henrik S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Hvass","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Rasmus Hvass","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35243039"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.phro.2022.02.015","issn":["24056316"],"journal":"Physics and Imaging in Radiation Oncology","pages":"96-100","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Physics and Imaging in Radiation Oncology","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125281043"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-203e599c-7af3-46e0-a353-abaa4ee4d7dd","sdu-d9e8bcda-c8dc-4c0a-871c-c9e954339cfa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Safety of gadolinium based contrast agents in magnetic resonance imaging-guided radiotherapy - An investigation of chelate stability using relaxometry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.36-040757","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Neuromodulation is a rapidly expanding therapeutic option considered within neuropsychiatry, pain and rehabilitation therapy. Combining electrostimulation with feedback from fMRI can provide information about the mechanisms underlying the therapeutic effects, but so far, such studies have been hampered by the lack of technology to conduct safe and accurate experiments. Here we present a system for fMRI compatible electrical stimulation, and the first proof-of-concept neuroimaging data with deep brain stimulation (DBS) in pigs obtained with the device. New method: The system consists of two modules, placed in the control and scanner room, connected by optical fiber. The system also connects to the MRI scanner to timely initiate the stimulation sequence at start of scan. We evaluated the system in four pigs with DBS in the subthalamic nucleus (STN) while we acquired BOLD responses in the STN and neocortex. Results: We found that the system delivered robust electrical stimuli to the implanted electrode in sync with the preprogrammed fMRI sequence. All pigs displayed a DBS-STN induced neocortical BOLD response, but none in the STN. Comparisons with existing method: The system solves three major problems related to electric stimuli and fMRI examinations, namely preventing distortion of the fMRI signal, enabling communication that synchronize the experimental conditions, and surmounting the safety hazards caused by interference with the MRI scanner. Conclusions: The fMRI compatible electrical stimulator circumvents previous problems related to electroceuticals and fMRI. The system allows flexible modifications for fMRI designs and stimulation parameters, and can be customized to electroceutical applications beyond DBS.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Louise Møller","Baandrup, Anders Ohlhues","Mandeville, Joseph","Glud, Andreas Nørgaard","Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","Weikop, Pia","Jespersen, Bo","Hansen, Adam Espe","Thomsen, Carsten","Knudsen, Gitte Moos"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023628"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Louise Møller"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Deep brain stimulation","Electroceutical therapy","Optic fiber","RF Noise Spectrum","Radiofrequency emission","fMRI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an fmri compatible system for targeted electrical stimulation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jneumeth.2022.109659","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023628","identifier":[{"id":"85133610121","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35772608","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9681ca13-e3c5-42f5-8ce5-59890b9efec4","ku-6c668d2d-a6b3-494a-b32d-6840788f302e"],"keyword":["Deep brain stimulation","Electroceutical therapy","Optic fiber","RF Noise Spectrum","Radiofrequency emission","fMRI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2D13BD5D95C71F1D5496496EEE57155D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jneumeth.2022.109659","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/342163155/An_fMRI-compatible_system_for_targeted_electrical_stimulation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321837433/1_s2.0_S0165027022001868_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurosurgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Møller","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"8ce07f7e-b4be-4885-a96b-702a7a0d9f6e","name":"Jørgensen, Louise Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Ohlhues","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","name":"Baandrup, Anders Ohlhues","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph","key":"mandevillepau","last":"Mandeville","name":"Mandeville, Joseph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas Nørgaard","key":"gludpau","last":"Glud","locid":"7c293aba-b85e-4919-ac45-c7fe82208804","name":"Glud, Andreas Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3339-6120","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Christian Hedemann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f442e934-3b4d-4fc2-91dc-93621be94d60","name":"Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-7405","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"weikoppau","last":"Weikop","locid":"03dfc781-ac58-469d-a16a-12067a22f8fc","name":"Weikop, Pia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bo","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","name":"Jespersen, Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam Espe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"3df25ea7-9eb3-4b95-9aca-5171b7d5870f","name":"Thomsen, Carsten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gitte Moos","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f02aee9e-69cf-491a-9765-ff062f734db8","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Moos","orcid":"0000-0003-1508-6866","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35772608"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jneumeth.2022.109659","issn":["01650270","1872678X"],"issn_org":["01650270"],"journal":"Journal of Neuroscience Methods","paperid":"109659","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neuroscience Methods","volume":"378"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133610121"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9681ca13-e3c5-42f5-8ce5-59890b9efec4","ku-6c668d2d-a6b3-494a-b32d-6840788f302e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An fMRI-compatible system for targeted electrical stimulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-023628","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Difficult-to-treat-depression (DTD) is a clinical challenge. The interventions that are well-established for DTD are not suitable or effective for all the patients. Therefore, more treatment options are highly warranted. We formulated an evidence-based guideline concerning six interventions not well-established for DTD in Denmark. Methods: Selected review questions were formulated according to the PICO principle with specific definitions of the patient population (P), the intervention (I), the comparison (C), and the outcomes of interest (O), and systematic literature searches were performed stepwise for each review question to identify relevant systematic reviews/meta-analyses, and randomized controlled trials. The Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development and Evaluation (GRADE) system was used to assess the methodological quality of the included studies. Clinical recommendations were formulated based on the evidence, the risk-benefit ratio, and perceived patient preferences. Results: We found sufficient evidence for a weak recommendation of repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS) and cognitive behavioural analysis system of psychotherapy (CBASP). The use of bright light therapy in DTD was not sufficiently supported by the evidence, but should be considered as good clinical practice. The interventions should be considered in addition to ongoing antidepressant treatment. We did not find sufficient evidence to recommend intravenous ketamine/esketamine, rumination-focused psychotherapy, or cognitive remediation to patients with DTD. Conclusion: The evidence supported two of the six reviewed interventions, however it was generally weak which emphasizes the need for more good quality studies. This guideline does not cover all treatment options and should be regarded as a supplement to relevant DTD-guidelines.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Moeller, Stine Bjerrum","Gbyl, Krzysztof","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Andreasen, Maike","Austin, Stephen F.","Buchholtz, Poul Erik","Fønss, Line","Hjerrild, Simon","Hogervorst, Lise","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","Ladegaard, Nicolai","Martiny, Klaus","Meile, Jonas","Packness, Aake","Sigaard, Karen Rodriguez","Straarup, Krista","Straszek, Sune P. V.","Soerensen, Claus Havregaard","Welcher, Birgitte","Videbech, Poul"],"cuid":["S04-086.84-012038"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Moeller, Stine Bjerrum","Møller, Stine Bjerrum"],"keyword":["Affective disorders","Antidepressive Agents therapeutic use","Clinical guideline","Cognitive behavioral therapy","Depression therapy","Humans","Persistent depressive disorder","Psychotherapy","Treatment resistant depression","refractory depression"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unknown external organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treatment of difficult to treat depression clinical guideline for selected interventions","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08039488.2021.1952303","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financed by the Danish Health Authority (DHA). The current guideline was developed in a collaboration between the Capital Region Mental Health Centre (CR-MHC) and the Danish Psychiatric Association."],"id":"S04-086.84-012038","identifier":[{"id":"85113797239","type":"scopus"}