tle":"En højesterets dom om valutaspekulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-272359","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The Danish national health registers were used to investigate the economic burden of obesity, associated costs of comorbidities and a breakdown into direct and indirect costs. Methods: The study population comprised all Danish adult citizens registered with a hospital diagnosis of obesity in the Danish National Patient Register between 2002 and 2018. Cases were matched with five controls via the Danish Civil Registration System. We estimated the difference in total healthcare costs and indirect costs between cases and controls and the difference in healthcare resource utilization. In a sub-analysis, we estimated total healthcare costs for persons who had been registered with one or more of 11 predefined comorbidities. Results: People with obesity experienced a statistically significant twofold increase in average direct healthcare costs per year (EUR 5,934), compared with controls (EUR 2,788) and had statistically significantly higher indirect costs compared to controls. Total healthcare costs for people with obesity and one or more of the 11 comorbidities were 91.7%–342.8% higher than total healthcare costs of the population with obesity but none of the 11 comorbidities. Conclusion: Obesity was associated with an increase in both direct and indirect costs. The presence of comorbidities was associated with additional healthcare costs. Key points: Obesity is associated with an increase in direct and indirect costs in Denmark. Comorbidities are associated with additional healthcare costs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Spanggaard, Maria","Bøgelund, Mette","Dirksen, Carsten","Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","Madsbad, Steen","Panton, Ulrik Haagen","Pedersen, Mikkel H.","Reitzel, Signe Baattrup","Johansen, Pierre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455357"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Burden of disease","Cost of Illness","Obesity","Real world evidence","Register based study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the substantial costs to society associated with obesity a danish register based study based on 000000002002 000000002018 data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14737167.2022.2053676","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-455357","identifier":[{"id":"85127332903","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35297718","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-67b3b828-f3c0-448f-9219-963095704158"],"keyword":["Burden of disease","cost of illness","obesity","real-world evidence","register-based study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBFE9684CCAF1028D79F7A79F19B32EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313646734/The.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14737167.2022.2053676","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Incentive"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk Scandinavia"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"spanggaardpau","last":"Spanggaard","name":"Spanggaard, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"bøgelundpau","last":"Bøgelund","name":"Bøgelund, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","locid":"2504d7c9-ee3f-4990-9c1b-10be728b298c","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Nils Bruun","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"a7e601a6-3ad6-46d0-9a6a-b8956c0af321","name":"Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Steen","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","name":"Madsbad, Steen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Ulrik Haagen","key":"pantonpau","last":"Panton","name":"Panton, Ulrik Haagen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel H.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Mikkel H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe Baattrup","key":"reitzelpau","last":"Reitzel","name":"Reitzel, Signe Baattrup","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Pierre","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Pierre","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35297718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/14737167.2022.2053676","issn":["14737167","17448379"],"issn_org":["14737167"],"issue":"5","journal":"Expert Review of Pharmacoeconomics & Outcomes Research","pages":"823-833","status":"p","title":"Expert Review of Pharmacoeconomics & Outcomes Research","title_org":"Expert Review of Pharmacoeconomics and Outcomes Research","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127332903"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Novo Nordisk","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","incentive"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-67b3b828-f3c0-448f-9219-963095704158"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The substantial costs to society associated with obesity–a Danish register-based study based on 2002-2018 data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455357","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Peptide receptor radionuclide therapy (PRRT) relies on α-and β-emitting radionuclides bound to a peptide that commonly targets somatostatin receptors (SSTRs) for the localized killing of tumors through ionizing radiation. A Lutetium-177 (177Lu)-based probe linked to the somatostatin analog octreotate ([177Lu]Lu-DOTA-TATE) is approved for the treatment of certain SSTR-expressing tumors and has been shown to improve survival. However, a limiting factor of PRRT is the potential toxicity derived from the high doses needed to kill the tumor. This could be circumvented by combining PRRT with other treatments for an enhanced anti-tumor effect. Photothermal therapy (PTT) relies on nanoparticle-induced hyperthermia for cancer treatment and could be a useful add-on to PRRT. Here, we investigate a strategy combining [177Lu]Lu-DOTA-TATE PRRT and nanoshell (NS)-based PTT for the treatment of SSTR-expressing small-cell lung tumors in mice. Our results showed that the combination treatment improved survival compared to PRRT alone, but only when PTT was performed one day after [177Lu]Lu-DOTA-TATE injection (one of the timepoints examined), showcasing the effect of treatment timing in relation to outcome. Furthermore, the combination treatment was well-tolerated in the mice. This indicates that strategies involving NS-based PTT as an add-on to PRRT could be promising and should be investigated further.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Simón, Marina","Jørgensen, Jesper Tranekjær","Khare, Harshvardhan A.","Christensen, Camilla","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458180"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer","Photothermal therapy PTT","peptide receptor radionuclide therapy PRRT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combination of sup 000000000177 sup lu lu dota tate targeted radionuclide therapy and photothermal therapy as a promising approach for cancer treatment in vivo studies in a human xenograft mouse model","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pharmaceutics14061284","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-458180","identifier":[{"id":"85132576048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9227845","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35745856","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6c65e5b0-f5e0-476e-bd68-bafa611b1f96"],"keyword":["[177Lu]Lu-DOTA-TATE","cancer","nanoshells (NS)","peptide receptor radionuclide therapy (PRRT)","photothermal therapy (PTT)","somatostatin receptor (SSTR)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-873CDCE527CF9F85955C14D8C3DD3AF8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pharmaceutics14061284","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/314068605/Combination_of_177Lu_Lu_DOTA_TATE_Targeted_Radionuclide.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Minerva Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marina","key":"simónpau","last":"Simón","locid":"6d845210-1808-405b-9e62-3e12b06829a8","name":"Simón, Marina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tranekjær","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"192b41b5-cee6-4e1e-87f3-e74d782502c9","name":"Jørgensen, Jesper Tranekjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Harshvardhan A.","key":"kharepau","last":"Khare","locid":"50b9e645-be48-4208-86ad-ba917cf99db9","name":"Khare, Harshvardhan A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"9492a2fe-f5a8-49cf-ba8e-0d1e1069fffc","name":"Christensen, Camilla","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Carsten Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aefb223a-8c5c-41c6-9e69-fade0a04bf90","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35745856"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/pharmaceutics14061284","issn":["19994923"],"issue":"6","journal":"Pharmaceutics","pages":"1-16","paperid":"1284","status":"p","title":"Pharmaceutics","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132576048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","minerva imaging"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6c65e5b0-f5e0-476e-bd68-bafa611b1f96"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combination of [<sup>177</sup>Lu]Lu-DOTA-TATE Targeted Radionuclide Therapy and Photothermal Therapy as a Promising Approach for Cancer Treatment : In Vivo Studies in a Human Xenograft Mouse Model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458180","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and aims: The metabolic consequences after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB) and sleeve gastrectomy (SG) are often studied using a liquid mixed meal. However, liquid meals may not be representative of the patients' everyday diet. We therefore examined postprandial glucose and gut hormone responses using mixed meals differing only with respect to meal texture. Methods: Twelve RYGB-operated, 12 SG-operated, and 12 unoperated individuals (controls) were enrolled in the study. Participants were matched on age, sex, and body mass index. In randomized order, each participant underwent a liquid and a solid 4-h mixed meal test on separate days. The meals were isocaloric (309 kcal), and with identical macronutrient composition (47 E% carbohydrate, 18 E% protein, 32 E% fat, and 3 E% dietary fibers). The liquid meal was blended to create a smooth liquid texture while the other meal retained its solid components. Results: Postprandial glucose concentrations (peak and incremental area under curve, iAUC) did not differ between the two meal textures in any group. In the control group, peak C-peptide was higher after the liquid meal compared with the solid meal (p = 0.04), whereas iAUCs of C-peptide were similar between the two meals in all groups. Peak of glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) was higher after the liquid meal compared with the solid meal in RYGB- and SG-operated individuals (RYGB p = 0.02; SG p < 0.01), but iAUC of GLP-1 did not differ between meal textures within any group. Peak of glucose-dependent insulin tropic polypeptide (GIP) was higher after the liquid meal in the SG and control groups (SG p = 0.02; controls p < 0.01), but iAUCs of GIP were equal between meals. There were no differences in total AUC of ghrelin between the liquid and solid meals within any of the groups. Conclusion: A liquid and a solid meal with identical macronutrient composition result in similar postprandial glucose responses, both in operated and unoperated individuals. Small differences were observed for the postprandial peaks of C-peptide, GLP-1, and GIP concentrations. Overall, a liquid meal is suitable for evaluating glucose tolerance, β-cell function, and gut hormones responses, both after RYGB and SG and in unoperated individuals. Clinical Trial Registration: [www.clinicaltrials.gov], identifier [NCT04082923].","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hedbäck, Nora","Hindsø, Morten","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","Linddal, Adelaide K","Jørgensen, Nils B.","Dirksen, Carsten","Møller, Andreas","Kristiansen, Viggo B.","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Svane, Maria S.","Madsbad, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461886"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of meal texture on postprandial glucose excursions and gut hormones after roux en y gastric bypass and sleeve gastrectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnut.2022.889710","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461886","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9100791","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35571890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85132615471","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000796443300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-728f0836-9d03-4bc9-89b4-d687c64d840b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-89411776BEFC59D568E010B05E44F27A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/310510045/fnut_09_889710.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnut.2022.889710","version":"Published Version"