{"abstract":"Affect integration is defined as the capacity to comprehend emotional experiences as meaningful and to convert this knowledge into well-adjusted motivation, communication and behavior. Thus, affect integration is considered essential for personal adjustment and well-being, and it has been operationalized through the Affect Integration Inventory. However, the validity of this questionnaire has been examined only in non-clinical respondents. Therefore, the purpose of this study was to investigate the psychometric properties of the questionnaire in a sample of patients with personality disorders (n = 87). The internal structure and consistency were addressed using Cronbach's alpha and confirmatory factor analysis. To determine aspects of convergent and discriminant validity, the correlations between the scores on the questionnaire and the scores on content-related questionnaires and scales were examined. Finally, scores from the clinical respondents and existing data from a previously collected non-clinical sample (n = 157) were compared to evaluate the external validity. The overall results demonstrated satisfactory internal consistency, a consistent factor structure, and systematic patterns of convergent and discriminant validity. Additionally, the findings indicated that the instrument clearly differentiated the clinical sample from the non-clinical sample.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Christina","Solbakken, Ole André","Licht, Rasmus W","Christensen, Ann-Eva","Jørgensen, Carsten René","Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007966"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Christina"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Affect Integration Inventory","Affect consciousness","Affect integration","Cross Sectional Studies","Emotional dysfunction","Humans","Personality Disorders diagnosis","Personality Inventory","Personality disorder","Psychometrics","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of the affect integration inventory in a sample of patients with personality disorders a cross sectional study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actpsy.2022.103554","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007966","identifier":[{"id":"85125697468","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35276544","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a4e2de6e-f2ca-4462-8a5c-da1aaf8c7ff4","au-d18e9db2-6f40-46c0-a14e-cb1ce67ff399"],"keyword":["Affect Integration Inventory","Affect consciousness","Affect integration","Cross-Sectional Studies","Emotional dysfunction","Humans","Personality Disorders/diagnosis","Personality Inventory","Personality disorder","Psychometrics","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EBE253D0535C1D45FED7999280FCF425"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actpsy.2022.103554","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/474992778/1_s2.0_S0001691822000695_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Psychiatry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"9f676fc7-28d7-462f-b271-84ed8e836389","name":"Frederiksen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole André","key":"solbakkenpau","last":"Solbakken","name":"Solbakken, Ole André","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus W.","key":"lichtpau","last":"Licht","locid":"bf0037e5-e6f9-48b0-91bf-bfd4ec420fb8","name":"Licht, Rasmus W","name_org":"Licht, Rasmus W.","orcid":"0000-0001-8095-3490","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Eva","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"6b85a6be-dd8d-4396-ba07-8786573bae99","name":"Christensen, Ann-Eva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gry Kjaersdam","key":"telléuspau","last":"Telléus","locid":"156daec5-475f-48d0-aee8-4bfcf2cb7941","name":"Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam","name_org":"Telléus, Gry Kjaersdam","orcid":"0000-0003-2329-3988","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35276544"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.actpsy.2022.103554","issn":["00016918","18736297"],"issn_org":["00016918"],"journal":"Acta Psychologica","paperid":"103554","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Acta Psychologica","volume":"225"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125697468"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a4e2de6e-f2ca-4462-8a5c-da1aaf8c7ff4","au-d18e9db2-6f40-46c0-a14e-cb1ce67ff399"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Validation of the Affect Integration Inventory in a sample of patients with personality disorders : A cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-007966","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Identity diffusion is one of the defining characteristics of borderline personality disorder (BPD). Given its central importance in the formal diagnostic criteria for personality disorders, identity diffusion is remarkably under-researched. In particular, our knowledge of the phenomenology of identity diffusion needs to be improved. This study is based on semistructured interviews with 16 younger women SCID-5-diagnosed with BPD. All interviews were analyzed using the interpretative phenomenological analysis approach. On the basis of this analysis, the patients' descriptions of how identity diffusion manifests itself in their subjective experience are classified into nine categories: disintegrated self-image; using various façades to stabilize the self; painful feelings of the self as broken; feeling that the self does not fit in; inner emptiness; “I don't know what I want”; great need for attention from others to stabilize identity; feeling unable to handle interpersonal relationships; and using sex to distract the self and regulate painful self-states.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten René","Bøye, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-254525"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Borderline personality disorder","Identity disturbance","Patient perspective","Phenomenology","Qualitative study","Sexual Behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does it feel to have a disturbed identity the phenomenology of identity diffusion in patients with borderline personality disorder a qualitative study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/355920130/How_Does_It_Feel_to_Have_a_Disturbed_Identity_Published_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-254525","identifier":[{"id":"34124947","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85123969001","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-db584362-d489-4edb-9f43-40f35f6708d6"],"keyword":["Borderline personality disorder","Identity disturbance","Patient perspective","Phenomenology","Qualitative study","Sexual behavior"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B716FBF9B3E2F18BCA4608AF40186555"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/355920130/How_Does_It_Feel_to_Have_a_Disturbed_Identity_Published_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bøyepau","last":"Bøye","locid":"c816211a-6dc5-4594-ba92-a5d3aa050cde","name":"Bøye, Rikke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34124947"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1521/pedi_2021_35_526","issn":["0885579X","19432763"],"issn_org":["0885579X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Personality Disorders","pages":"40-69","publisher":"Guilford Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Personality Disorders","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123969001"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-db584362-d489-4edb-9f43-40f35f6708d6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How Does It Feel to Have a Disturbed Identity? The Phenomenology of Identity Diffusion in Patients With Borderline Personality Disorder : A Qualitative Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254525","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Fluid therapy in patients with suspected infection is controversial, and it is not known whether fluid treatment administered in the prehospital setting is beneficial. In the absence of evidence-based guidelines for prehospital fluid therapy for patients with suspected infection, Emergency Medical Services (EMS) personnel are challenged on when and how to initiate such therapy. This study aimed to assess EMS personnel’s decision-making in prehospital fluid therapy, including triggers for initiating fluid and fluid volumes, as well as the need for education and evidence-based guidelines on prehospital fluid therapy in patients with suspected infection. Methods: An online survey concerning fluid administration in prehospital patients with suspected infection was distributed to all EMS personnel in the Central Denmark Region, including ambulance clinicians and prehospital critical care anaesthesiologists (PCCA). The survey consisted of sections concerning academic knowledge, statements about fluid administration, triggers to evaluate patient needs for intravenous fluid, and clinical scenarios. Results: In total, 468/807 (58%) ambulance clinicians and 106/151 (70%) PCCA responded to the survey. Of the respondents, 73% (n = 341) of the ambulance clinicians and 100% (n = 106) of the PCCA felt confident about administering fluids to prehospital patients with infections. However, both groups primarily based their fluid-related decisions on “clinical intuition”. Ambulance clinicians named the most frequently faced challenges in fluid therapy as “Unsure whether the patient needs fluid” and “Unsure about the volume of fluid the patient needs”. The five most frequently used triggers for evaluating fluid needs were blood pressure, history taking, skin turgor, capillary refill time, and shock index, the last of which only applied to ambulance clinicians. In the scenarios, the majority administered 500 ml to a normotensive woman with suspected sepsis and 1000 ml to a woman with suspected sepsis-related hypotension. Moreover, 97% (n = 250) of the ambulance clinicians strongly agreed or agreed that they were interested in more education about fluid therapy in patients with suspected infection. Conclusion: The majority of ambulance clinicians and PCCA based their fluid administration on “clinical intuition”. They faced challenges deciding on fluid volumes and individual fluid needs. Thus, they were eager to learn more and requested research and evidence-based guidelines.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Marie Egebjerg","Jensen, Arne Sylvester","Meilandt, Carsten","Jørgensen, Kristian Winther","Væggemose, Ulla","Bach, Allan","Kirkegaard, Hans","Pedersen, Marie Kristine Jessen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255546"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Marie Kristine Jessen"],"keyword":["Emergency Medical Services","Fluid administration","Guideline","Sepsis","Survey"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prehospital fluid therapy in patients with suspected infection a survey of ambulance personnel s practice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-022-01025-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255546","identifier":[{"id":"35642066","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85131008505","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9158174","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-dd21a211-326b-412a-80da-4e15706d5b07"],"keyword":["Emergency Medical Services","Fluid administration","Guideline","Sepsis","Survey","Suspected infection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7467994496850AA42BBEC6072CBC2868"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-022-01025-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Research Center for Emergency Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Central Denmark Region"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Egebjerg","key":"jensenmarieegebjergpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1ace90ab-cc6b-4560-8398-3febe8937700","name":"Jensen, Marie Egebjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne Sylvester","key":"jensenarnesylvesterpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Arne Sylvester","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"meilandtcarstenpau","last":"Meilandt","name":"Meilandt, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Winther","key":"jørgensenkristianwintherpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Kristian Winther","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla","key":"væggemoseullapau","last":"Væggemose","locid":"837849e6-ed87-4ab9-922f-dca49efcf9c8","name":"Væggemose, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0003-1389-6777","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"bachallanpau","last":"Bach","locid":"7cf56010-168d-43e6-96ee-78dd09999be2","name":"Bach, Allan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"kirkegaardhanspau","last":"Kirkegaard","locid":"911be177-8ade-45ff-93ef-6f631e537119","name":"Kirkegaard, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Kristine","key":"pedersenmariekristinejessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"b0074398-927b-41e6-a59a-4d6fd79f3fdb","name":"Pedersen, Marie Kristine Jessen","name_org":"Jessen, Marie Kristine","orcid":"0000-0001-9445-7690","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35642066"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13049-022-01025-1","issn":["17577241"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","paperid":"38","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131008505"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dd21a211-326b-412a-80da-4e15706d5b07"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prehospital fluid therapy in patients with suspected infection : a survey of ambulance personnel’s practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255546","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) patients with unmutated immunoglobulin heavy chain (IgHV) are at risk of early disease progression compared to patients with mutated IgHV. As a preventive strategy, we treated 19 previously untreated CLL patients with unmutated IgHV in a phase 1/2 trial (clinicaltrials.gov, NCT03939234) exploring the efficacy and toxicity of a therapeutic cancer vaccine containing peptides derived from programmed death ligand 1 (PD-L1) and ligand 2 (PD-L2), hoping to restore immunological control of the disease. According to the International Workshop on Chronic lymphocytic Leukemia (iwCLL) response criteria, no patients obtained a response; however, during follow-up, one patient had complete normalization of the peripheral lymphocyte count and remained in biochemical remission after a follow-up time of 15 months. At the end of treatment, one patient had progressed, and 17 patients had stable disease. During follow-up with a median time of 23.5 months since inclusion, seven patients had progressed, and eight patients had stable disease. The median time to first treatment (TTFT) from diagnosis was 90.3 months with a median follow-up time of 50.1 months. This apparent favorable outcome in TTFT needs to be investigated in a randomized setting, as our population may have been biased. More than 80% of patients obtained vaccine-specific immune responses, confirming the immunogenicity of the vaccine. The vaccine was generally well tolerated with only grade I–II adverse events. Although there were some signs of clinical effects, the vaccine seems to be insufficient as monotherapy in CLL, possibly due to a high tumor burden. The efficacy of the vaccine should preferably be tested in combination with novel targeted therapies or as a consolidating treatment.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Klausen, Uffe","Grauslund, Jacob Handlos","Jørgensen, Nicolai Grønne Dahlager","Ahmad, Shamaila Munir","Jonassen, Merete","Weis-Banke, Stine Emilie","Martinenaite, Evelina","Pedersen, Lone Bredo","Lisle, Thomas Landkildehus","Gang, Anne Ortved","Enggaard, Lisbeth","Hansen, Morten","Holmström, Morten Orebo","Met, Özcan","Svane, Inge Marie","Niemann, Carsten Utoft","Pedersen, Lars Møller","Andersen, Mads Hald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438864"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer vaccine","Immunotherapy","PD L1","PD L2","chronic lymphocytic leukemia CLL"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anti pd l000000000001 pd l000000000002 therapeutic vaccination in untreated chronic lymphocytic leukemia patients with unmutated ighv","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fonc.2022.1023015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438864","identifier":[{"id":"36483037","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9723164","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85143346823","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4c25c248-0a16-45e0-8dd5-b18b589b9258"],"keyword":["PD-L1","PD-L2","cancer vaccine","chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL)","immunotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A7E0858D1F068851CF1873B3E41E6C19"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fonc.2022.1023015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/330394720/fonc_12_1023015.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3