{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Women experiencing greater trochanteric pain syndrome (GTPS) report high levels of pain and reduced quality of life. Exploring how they manage GTPS in a daily life context can provide important knowledge about individual coping strategies. Education, extracorporeal shockwave therapy (ESWT) and exercise have good group level evidence for efficacy in clinical trials and are increasingly used in routine care for patients with GTPS. Exploring women's experiences of such treatment may help understand the mechanisms underpinning these positive results and inform treatment strategies. We therefore aimed to explore how women with GTPS experience and manage their daily life, and their experience of the combined treatment of education, ESWT and exercises. METHODS: This qualitative study was nested within a cohort study based in a hospital outpatient clinic and a physiotherapy clinic in Denmark assessing the combined treatment of education, ESWT and exercises. Data was collected from eleven women using in-person, individual, semi-structured interviews which were audio recorded. Transcripts were coded and analysed using an inductive thematic analysis approach. FINDINGS: Five themes were identified: (1) Daily life was controlled and structured by pain; (2) The condition was acknowledged and taken seriously by treating professionals; (3) The participants´ experiences of the intervention-information is key; (4) Improved capability and autonomy in pain management and (5) The women´s perspectives on improving and expanding the intervention. Learning how to manage pain was experienced as the most important element of the program to the women to be able to minimize pain and manage daily life. CONCLUSION: Exploration of how women with greater trochanteric pain syndrome experienced and managed daily hip pain, and how they experienced and adapted to treatment are important novel findings that will inform clinical practice. This new knowledge may be used to inform an individualized patient education, treatment and evaluation strategy for women with the painful and debilitating condition of GTPS.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Andreasen, Jane","Fearon, Angela","Morissey, Dylan","Hjørnholm, Laura Hvidaa","Kristinsson, Jens","Jorgensen, Jens Erik","Mølgaard, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063874"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Andreasen, Jane"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barts Health NHS Trust","Canberra Hospital","Queen Mary University of London","University of Canberra"],"keyword":["Bursitis","Cohort Studies","Female","Humans","Pain","Qualitative Research","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Sofiendal Aalborg Sundhedsteam"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i feel i have been taken seriously women s experience of greater trochanteric pain syndrome treatment a nested qualitative study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0278197","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-063874","identifier":[{"id":"85142939905","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36441745","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2fb09c16-62a0-4524-aa6b-3a240f29bdbc"],"keyword":["Bursitis","Cohort Studies","Female","Humans","Pain","Qualitative Research","Quality of Life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3970ECF928B4EA5FE32FD0DE0B530CDA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/503286366/journal.pone.0278197.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0278197","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Physiotherapy and Occupational Therapy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Public Health and Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"canberra hospital","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Canberra Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of canberra","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Canberra","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"barts health nhs trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Barts Health NHS Trust","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Sofiendal Aalborg Sundhedsteam"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"afdfbe5c-39d0-4504-a751-4e3e2b5b0b6c","name":"Andreasen, Jane","orcid":"0000-0001-8000-1553","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Angela","key":"fearonpau","last":"Fearon","name":"Fearon, Angela","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Dylan","key":"morisseypau","last":"Morissey","name":"Morissey, Dylan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Hvidaa","key":"hjørnholmpau","last":"Hjørnholm","locid":"40b8985d-d6a7-43e8-acc2-8cbe21a32af0","name":"Hjørnholm, Laura Hvidaa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kristinssonpau","last":"Kristinsson","locid":"d279d9c4-5f5e-4d78-a617-a3bde3352dbf","name":"Kristinsson, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Erik","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, Jens Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten M","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"e49f2521-d695-41bf-b1c2-595166292dfd","name":"Mølgaard, Carsten","name_org":"Mølgaard, Carsten M","orcid":"0000-0002-7427-8078","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36441745"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0278197","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"11","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0278197","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142939905"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2fb09c16-62a0-4524-aa6b-3a240f29bdbc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"I feel I have been taken seriously\" Women's experience of greater trochanteric pain syndrome treatment-A nested qualitative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063874","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Neurotensin (NT) is released from enteroendocrine cells and lowers food intake in rodents. We evaluated postprandial NT secretion in humans after surgeries associated with accelerated small intestinal nutrient delivery, and after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB) when glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) signalling and dipeptidyl peptidase 4 (DPP-4) were inhibited, and during pharmacological treatments influencing entero-pancreatic functions. METHODS: We measured NT concentrations in plasma from meal studies: (I) after truncal vagotomy with pyloroplasty (TVP), cardia resection +TVP (CTVP), and matched controls (n = 10); (II) after RYGB, sleeve gastrectomy (SG), and in matched controls (n = 12); (III) after RYGB (n = 11) with antagonism of GLP-1 signalling using exendin(9-39) and DPP-4 inhibition using sitagliptin; (IV) after RYGB (n = 11) during a run-in period and subsequent treatment with, sitagliptin, liraglutide (GLP-1 receptor agonist), verapamil (calcium antagonist), acarbose (alpha glucosidase inhibitor), and pasireotide (somatostatin analogue), respectively. RESULTS: (I) NT secretion was similar after TVP/CTVP (p = 0.9), but increased vs. controls (p < 0.0001). (II) NT secretion was increased after RYGB vs. SG and controls (p < 0.0001). NT responses were similar in SG and controls (p = 0.3), but early postprandial NT concentrations were higher after SG (p < 0.05). (III) Exendin (9-39) and sitagliptin did not change NT responses vs placebo (p > 0.2), but responses were lower during sitagliptin vs. exendin(9-39) (p = 0.03). (IV) Pasireotide suppressed NT secretion (p = 0.004). Sitagliptin tended to lower NT secretion (p = 0.08). Liraglutide, verapamil, and acarbose had no effect (p > 0.9). CONCLUSION: Neurotensin secretion is increased after surgeries associated with accelerated gastric emptying and lowered by pasireotide.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Svane, Maria S.","Øhrstrøm, Caroline C","Plamboeck, Astrid","Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","Dirksen, Carsten","Martinussen, Christoffer","Vilsbøll, Tina","Hartmann, Bolette","Deacon, Carolyn F.","Kristiansen, Viggo B.","Knop, Filip K.","Svendsen, Lars Bo","Madsbad, Sten","Holst, Jens Juul","Veedfald, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412682"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neurotensin secretion after roux en y gastric bypass sleeve gastrectomy and truncal vagotomy with pyloroplasty","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-412682","identifier":[{"id":"34378827","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000683790100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85112106834","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2047e009-0958-4a88-8e51-4b8bde2043a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F0332AB8111D1EBC2C1DF136AD9D0A2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria S.","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"4cc109fb-b416-4327-a1bd-c980486fa717","name":"Svane, Maria S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Caroline C","key":"øhrstrømpau","last":"Øhrstrøm","name":"Øhrstrøm, Caroline C","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Astrid","key":"plamboeckpau","last":"Plamboeck","locid"