{"abstract":"Circulating fragments of type III collagen, measured by PRO-C3, has shown promising results as a tumor fibrosis biomarker. However, the fibrotic tumor microenvironment consists of many other collagens with diverse functions and unexplored biomarker potential. One example hereof is type XXII collagen (COL22). In this study, we investigated the biomarker potential of COL22 by measuring this in serum. An ELISA, named PRO-C22, was developed and measured in two serum cohorts consisting of patients with various solid tumors (n = 220) and healthy subjects (n = 33) (Cohort 1), and patients with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) (n = 34), and healthy subjects (n = 20) (Cohort 2). In Cohort 1, PRO-C22 was elevated in the serum from patients with solid tumors, compared to healthy subjects (p < 0.01 to p < 0.0001), and the diagnostic accuracy (AUROC) ranged from 0.87 to 0.98, p < 0.0001. In Cohort 2, the high levels of PRO-C22, in patients with PDAC, were predictive of a worse overall survival (HR = 4.52, 95% CI 1.90–10.7, p = 0.0006) and this remained significant after adjusting for PRO-C3 (HR = 4.27, 95% CI 1.24–10.4, p = 0.0013). In conclusion, PRO-C22 has diagnostic biomarker potential in various solid tumor types and prognostic biomarker potential in PDAC. Furthermore, PRO-C22 complemented PRO-C3 in predicting mortality, suggesting an additive prognostic value when quantifying different collagens.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Madsen, Emilie A.","Thorlacius-Ussing, Jeppe","Nissen, Neel I.","Jensen, Christina","Chen, Inna M.","Johansen, Julia S.","Diab, Hadi M.H.","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Hansen, Carsten P.","Karsdal, Morten A.","Willumsen, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501269"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collagens","ECM","Non invasive biomarker","PDAC","Tumor fibrosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"type xxii collagen complements fibrillar collagens in the serological assessment of tumor fibrosis and the outcome in pancreatic cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells11233763","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-501269","identifier":[{"id":"85143623674","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36497023","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9738409","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b4894528-d4fe-4186-8089-b85a48918558"],"keyword":["ECM","PDAC","collagens","non-invasive biomarker","tumor fibrosis","type XXII collagen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-27DC0540DF693F4FF7EDDCCBBD59FAD9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/329571784/cells_11_03763_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells11233763","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Emilie A.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"271c4fbf-ab6c-4b25-aa5d-ca332a3a8925","name":"Madsen, Emilie A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jeppe","key":"thorlaciusussingpau","last":"Thorlacius-Ussing","name":"Thorlacius-Ussing, Jeppe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Neel I.","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","name":"Nissen, Neel I.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Inna M.","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Inna M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julia S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hadi M.H.","key":"diabpau","last":"Diab","locid":"02e20038-d5c8-4685-951f-6c6da91d9735","name":"Diab, Hadi M.H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars N.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","name_org":"Jørgensen, Lars N.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten P.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Carsten P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten A.","key":"karsdalpau","last":"Karsdal","name":"Karsdal, Morten A.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicholas","key":"willumsenpau","last":"Willumsen","name":"Willumsen, Nicholas","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36497023"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cells11233763","issn":["20734409"],"issue":"23","journal":"Cells","paperid":"3763","status":"p","title":"Cells","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143623674"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b4894528-d4fe-4186-8089-b85a48918558"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Type XXII Collagen Complements Fibrillar Collagens in the Serological Assessment of Tumor Fibrosis and the Outcome in Pancreatic Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-501269","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"About half of all Danish cancer patients are 70 years or older at diagnosis. The incidence is expected to increase further over the coming years because of an increasing longevity. Therefore, this review recommends that the Danish health care system develops and implement models to ensure optimal care for older adults with cancer. We are still in need of knowledge about the optimal treatment, rehabilitation, palliation and care for older adults with cancer. We encourage the Danish health authorities to formulate a national strategy for this area.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Ewertz, Marianne","Ehmsen, Sidse","Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","Dieperink, Karin Brochstedt","Pfeiffer, Per","Hansen, Olfred","Brink, Carsten","Hjelmborg, Jacob","Hvidt, Niels Christian","Abildgaard, Niels","Lund, Lars","Frederiksen, Henrik","Ryg, Jesper","Ditzel, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-595904"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ditzel, Henrik"],"keyword":["Aged","Delivery of Health Care","Humans","Incidence","Neoplasms therapy","Palliative care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udfordringer ved kræftbehandling til ældre","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/264744884/v04210325_web.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-595904","identifier":[{"id":"85129890719","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34596511","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85117556485","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4f313b27-5841-4631-b9d8-83475f005e2b"],"keyword":["Aged","Delivery of Health Care","Humans","Incidence","Neoplasms/therapy","Palliative Care"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","m