":"1975889","status":"p","title":"OncoImmunology","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115686622"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e952365f-1be1-4447-9467-b742aa5fe5ed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An immunogenic first-in-human immune modulatory vaccine with PD-L1 and PD-L2 peptides is feasible and shows early signs of efficacy in follicular lymphoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532780","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"According to the literature, avoidant personality disorder (APD) is often overlooked in research on personality disorders. In the present study, patients with APD were compared to patients with borderline personality disorder (BPD) with respect to emotional dysfunction. Emotional dysfunction was operationalized through the Affect Integration Inventory. Sixty-one patients receiving treatment at specialized outpatient hospital facilities for either BPD (n = 25) or APD (n = 36) (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, fifth edition) were included in a cross-sectional study. Supporting our expectations of no difference in the global capacity for affect integration between groups, the estimated difference was 0.00 (95% confidence interval [CI] [−0.53, 0.53]). On the other hand, the expected increased dysfunction in APD regarding Expression could not be confirmed. Furthermore, problems with specific affects distinguished the groups; integration of Interest was worse in APD (p = 0.01), whereas integration of Jealousy was worse in BPD (p = 0.04). In terms of prototypical modes of experiencing affects, APD was characterized by decreased access to the motivational properties of Interest (p < 0.01), while BPD was more driven by Interest (p < 0.01), Anger (p < 0.01), and Jealousy (p = 0.01). In conclusion, even though the two disorders are characterized by similar overall levels of emotional dysfunction, they differ systematically and predictably regarding specific affects and modes of experiencing. These findings carry implications for the understanding of emotional dysfunction in APD and BPD, suggesting specific areas of emotional dysfunction that could be targeted in tailored psychotherapeutic interventions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Christina","Solbakken, Ole André","Licht, Rasmus W","Jørgensen, Carsten René","Rodrigo-Domingo, Maria","Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Christina"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Affect Integration Inventory","Affect integration","Avoidant personality disorder","Borderline personality disorder","Emotional dysfunction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"emotional dysfunction in avoidant personality disorder and borderline personality disorder a cross sectional comparative study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sjop.12771","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009259","identifier":[{"id":"34523729","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85115102974","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9291737","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-c00f8ad5-5d4d-4043-b240-64ab485b7c66","au-840bbb2f-e165-4780-a74b-c31a84bbd268"],"keyword":["Affect integration","affect integration inventory","avoidant personality disorder","borderline personality disorder","emotional dysfunction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3443C76917E6860D71F84F41530BF9DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sjop.12771","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/456165043/Frederiksen_et_al._2021_Emotional_dysfunction_in_avoidant_personality_disorder_and_borderline_personality_disorder.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/227081520/sjop.12771_Publisher_PDF.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Psychiatry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"9f676fc7-28d7-462f-b271-84ed8e836389","name":"Frederiksen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole André","key":"solbakkenpau","last":"Solbakken","name":"Solbakken, Ole André","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus W.","key":"lichtpau","last":"Licht","locid":"bf0037e5-e6f9-48b0-91bf-bfd4ec420fb8","name":"Licht, Rasmus W","name_org":"Licht, Rasmus W.","orcid":"0000-0001-8095-3490","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"rodrigodomingopau","last":"Rodrigo-Domingo","locid":"fff908cd-728d-480b-9534-0cd7176b7dfc","name":"Rodrigo-Domingo, Maria","orcid":"0000-0001-7661-7195","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gry","key":"kjaersdamtelléuspau","last":"Kjaersdam Telléus","locid":"156daec5-475f-48d0-aee8-4bfcf2cb7941","name":"Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam","name_org":"Kjaersdam Telléus, Gry","orcid":"0000-0003-2329-3988","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34523729"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sjop.12771","issn":["00365564","14679450"],"issn_org":["00365564"],"issue":"6","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Psychology","pages":"878-886","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Psychology","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115102974"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c00f8ad5-5d4d-4043-b240-64ab485b7c66","au-840bbb2f-e165-4780-a74b-c31a84bbd268"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Emotional dysfunction in avoidant personality disorder and borderline personality disorder : A cross-sectional comparative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009259","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The trans-membrane protease serine 2 (TMPRSS2) is essential for severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) cell entry and infection. Efficacy and safety of TMPRSS2 inhibitors in patients with coronavirus disease 2019 (Covid-19) have not been evaluated in randomized trials. Methods: We conducted an investigator-initiated, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled multicenter trial in patients hospitalized with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection from April 4, to December 31, 2020. Within 48 h of admission, participants were randomly assigned in a 2:1 ratio to receive the TMPRSS2 inhibitor camostat mesilate 200 mg three times daily for 5 days or placebo. The primary outcome was time to discharge or clinical improvement measured as ≥2 points improvement on a 7-point ordinal scale. Other outcomes included 30-day mortality, safety and change in oropharyngeal viral load. Findings: 137 patients were assigned to receive camostat mesilate and 68 to placebo. Median time to clinical improvement was 5 days (interquartile range [IQR], 3 to 7) in the camostat group and 5 days (IQR, 2 to 10) in the placebo group ( P = 0·31). The hazard ratio for 30-day mortality in the camostat compared with the placebo group was 0·82 (95% confidence interval [CI], 0·24 to 2·79; P = 0·75). The frequency of adverse events was similar in the two groups. Median change in viral load from baseline to day 5 in the camostat group was -0·22 log 10 copies/mL ( p <0·05) and -0·82 log 10 in the placebo group ( P <0·05). Interpretation: Under this protocol, camostat mesilate treatment was not associated with increased adverse events during hospitalization for Covid-19 and did not affect time to clinical improvement, progression to ICU admission or mortality. ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT04321096. EudraCT Number: 2020-001200-42.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Gunst, Jesper Damsgaard","Stærke, Nina Breinholt","Pahus, Marie Høst","Kristensen, Lena Hagelskjær","Bodilsen, Jacob","Lohse, Nicolai","Dalgaard, Lars Skov","Brønnum, Dorthe","Frøbert, Ole","Hønge, Bo","Johansen, Isik Somuncu","Hansen, Ida Preetzmann Monrad","Erikstrup, Christian","Rosendal, Regitze","Vilstrup, Emil","Mariager, Theis","Bove, Dorthe G.","Offersen, Rasmus","Shakar, Shakil Ahmad","Cajander, Sara","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Sritharan, Sajitha Sophia","Breining, Peter","Jespersen, Søren","Mortensen, Klaus Leth","Jensen, Mads L.","Kolte, Lilian Østergaard","Frattari, Giamoco S.","Larsen, Carsten S","Storgaard, Merete","Nielsen, Lars P","Tolstrup, Martin","Sædder, Eva Aggerholm","Østergaard, Lars","Ngo, Hien T. T.","Jensen, Morten Hasselstrøm","Højen, Jesper Falkesgaard","Kjolby, Mads","Søgaard, Ole S."],"cuid":["S04-097.69-011732"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kjolby, Mads","Søgaard, Ole S.","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Dundee","Örebro University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy of the tmprss000000000002 inhibitor camostat mesilate in patients hospitalized with covid 000000000019 a double blind randomized controlled trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2021.100849","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The lundbeck foundation. Data are not available for download due to privacy/ethical restrictions under the EU GDPR. Specific requests for access to the trial data may be sent to olesoega@rm.dk and access may be provided to a named individual in agreement with the rules and regulations of the Danish Data Protection agency and the National Committee on Health Research Ethics. JDG, MK and OSS developed the design. JDG, NBS, LHK, JB, NL, LSD, DB, OF, BH, ISJ, EM, TM, DGB, RO, SS, SC, NPJ, SSS, SJ, KLM, MLJ, LK, GSF, CSL, MS, L?, JFH and OSS did the clinical visits. MHP, CE, RR, PB, LPN, MT, EAS and HTTN did the laboratory assays. JDG, MHJ, MK and OSS analyzed data. JDG, MK and OSS drafted the manuscript. All authors critically revised the manuscript for important intellectual content."],"id":"S04-097.69-011732","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8060682","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33903855","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85106067590","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f564aca6-b85f-4099-bccc-f39d6c74edec","au-a311d568-2cf8-44fb-91a7-9c7ac33a916c","ku-0d50080d-6146-4eaa-b8f7-a8cb41eca99e","sdu-e5e75a34-0785-4748-b191-de7b37eeaf66"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-FAA1C45B32E46CD434F1891943DC1CD3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/185098857/1_s2.0_S2589537021001292_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/413504791/Gunst_et_al._2021_Efficacy_of_the_TMPRSS2_Inhibitor_Camostat_Mesilate_in_Patients_Hospitalized_with_Covid_19_a_Double_blind_Randomized_Controlled_Trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275994912/PIIS2589537021001292.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2021.100849","version":"Published Version"}],"oai"