":"Descriptive analysis of long COVID sequelae identified in a multidisciplinary clinic serving hospitalised and non-hospitalised patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466532","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background. Arterial calcification is associated with cardiovascular mortality in dialysis patients. Active matrix Gla protein (MGP) is a vitamin K-dependent inhibitor of arterial calcification. Elevated plasma concentrations of inactive MGP, i.e. dephosphorylated-uncarboxylated MGP (dp-ucMGP), are prevalent in dialysis patients. MGP inactivity might contribute to arterial calcification. We investigated whether vitamin K supplementation had an effect on arterial calcification in chronic dialysis patients. Methods. In a 2-year, double-blind, placebo-controlled intervention trial, 48 dialysis patients were randomized to vitamin K [menaquinone-7 (MK-7), 360 mu g daily] or placebo. MK-7 in serum and dp-ucMGP in plasma were used to assess vitamin K status. Carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity (cfPWV) and scores of coronary arterial calcification (CAC) and abdominal aortic calcification (AAC) were used to assess arterial calcification. Results. Thirty-seven participants completed Year 1, and 21 completed Year 2. At Year 2, serum MK-7 was 40-fold higher, and plasma dp-ucMGP 40% lower after vitamin K supplementation compared with placebo {mean dp-ucMGP difference: -1380 pmol/L [95% confidence interval (CI) -2029 to -730]}. There was no significant effect of vitamin K supplementation on cfPWV [mean difference at Year 2: 1.2 m/s (95% CI -0.1 to 2.4)]. CAC Agatston score increased significantly in vitamin K supplemented participants, but was not significantly different from placebo [mean difference at Year 2: 664 (95% CI -554 to 1881)]. AAC scores increased in both groups, significantly so within the placebo group at Year 1, but with no significant between-group differences. Conclusions. Vitamin K supplementation improved vitamin K status, but did not hinder or modify the progression of arterial calcification in dialysis patients.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Levy-Schousboe, Karin","Frimodt-Møller, Marie","Hansen, Ditte","Peters, Christian Daugaard","Kjærgaard, Krista Dybtved","Jensen, Jens Dam","Strandhave, Charlotte","Elming, Hanne","Larsen, Carsten Toftager","Sandstrøm, Hanne","Brasen, Claus Lohman","Schmedes, Anne","Madsen, Jonna Skov","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Frandsen, Niels Erik","Petersen, Inge","Marckmann, Peter"],"cuid":["S04-094.06-008770"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Marckmann, Peter"],"keyword":["Calcium","Cardiovascular disease","Chronic kidney disease","Hemodialysis patients","Matrix Gla protein","Mortality","Progression","Pulse wave velocity","Stiffness","Vascular Calcification","coronary arterial calcification","menaquinone 7","prognostic significance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vitamin k supplementation and arterial calcification in dialysis results of the double blind randomized placebo controlled renakvit trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ckj/sfab017","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-094.06-008770","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8406073","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34476095","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000695754500015","type":"wos"},{"id":"85111501468","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b5b781f6-2db8-494f-8e98-9f7b088f3452","au-2bae2a97-1437-459c-8686-1572ab227a4c","ku-a50cb989-6975-48b2-a411-12312212fae4","sdu-1b962b04-d682-4045-ab8a-7bc8d1cb6bf0"],"keyword":["CALCIUM","CARDIOVASCULAR-DISEASE","HEMODIALYSIS-PATIENTS","MATRIX GLA PROTEIN","MORTALITY","PROGNOSTIC-SIGNIFICANCE","PROGRESSION","STIFFNESS","VASCULAR CALCIFICATION","chronic kidney disease","coronary arterial calcification","menaquinone-7","pulse wave velocity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-DB5157498D1323706BB3AA3D146244EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ckj/sfab017","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191354211/sfab017.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/281653134/sfab017.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/446943888/Levy_Schousboe_et_al._2021_Vitamin_K_supplementation_and_arterial_calcification_in_dialysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273674098/sfab017.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["De