","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8d7e909e-a6b5-4af1-8b0f-b6ac72f8461d","ku-4170971f-18d9-4346-b046-045623c077ee","sdu-9fe70bbe-3071-40ce-a6ba-c6f881af9655"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Protein-coding variants implicate novel genes related to lipid homeostasis contributing to body-fat distribution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-084.50-803748","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this review it is discussed if acute stress can be fatal. The review is based on literature searches on PubMed, PsycINFO as well as Web of Science. Literature concerning the conditions excited delirium syndrome (ExDS), malignant catatonia, takotsubo cardiomyopathy (TCM), and capture myopathy (CM) is reviewed and compared. The aim of the article is to identify and discuss a possible fatalness as well as a common pathophysiology behind these conditions. This includes a deregulated autonomic nervous system, neurocardiac reasons for myocardial damage, and rhabdomyolysis. We conclude that these conditions could be different manifestations of the same pathophysiological phenomenon. In addition, we suggest that it is possible to die from acute stress, but that it requires a prior sensitization, as seen in cocaine abusers and certain psychiatric patients, to render individuals disposed to an extreme autonomic nerve reaction. Lay summary This article compares different conditions in humans and in other animals, where it appears as if the human or animal dies with no other reason than being submitted to an extreme condition of mental stress. The conditions examined via a literature search are excited delirium syndrome, malignant catatonia and takotsubo cardiomyopathy in humans, and a capture myopathy in different mammals. The article theoretically suggests that one can die solely from acute stress, but that different forms sensitization probably goes ahead of such a fatal stress reaction. E.g. in cocaine addicts, some psychiatric patients, and in wild animals formerly subjected to stress an extreme sympathetic stress response might be immediately fatal. The article also theorizes that excited delirium syndrome, malignant catatonia, and capture myopathy could be more severe and acute variants of the temporary condition seen in takotsubo patients, also known as patients with broken heart syndrome.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Baltzer Nielsen, Solveig","Stanislaus, Sharleny","Saunamäki, Kari","Grøndahl, Carsten","Banner, Jytte","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-509658"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute stress","Capture myopathy","Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy","excited delirium syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can acute stress be fatal a systematic cross disciplinary review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85065169029&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-509658","identifier":[{"id":"85065169029","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30767612","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c2af1436-abd9-4366-bf42-506bffd96c77"],"keyword":["Acute stress","capture myopathy","excited delirium syndrome","fatal stress","malignant catatonia","neuro-cardiac connection","takotsubo cardiomyopathy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-002905389E65F6EE89B56923B937CBE1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – Nykøbing F,"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Section of Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Solveig","key":"baltzernielsenpau","last":"Baltzer Nielsen","name":"Baltzer Nielsen, Solveig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sharleny","key":"stanislauspau","last":"Stanislaus","name":"Stanislaus, Sharleny","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kari","key":"saunamäkipau","last":"Saunamäki","name":"Saunamäki, Kari","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten","key":"grøndahlpau","last":"Grøndahl","name":"Grøndahl, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jytte","key":"bannerpau","last":"Banner","locid":"de232254-f016-4135-9a31-ed55db6d92a7","name":"Banner, Jytte","orcid":"0000-0002-7559-1285","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Martin Balslev","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"dfc70acd-d15d-44f9-891e-6a7646d1727d","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30767612"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/10253890.2018.1561847","issn":["10253890","16078888"],"issn_org":["10253890"],"issue":"3","journal":"Stress: The International Journal on the Biology of Stress","pages":"286-294","status":"p","title":"Stress: The International Journal on the Biology of Stress","title_org":"Stress","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065169029"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c2af1436-abd9-4366-bf42-506bffd96c77"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Can acute stress be fatal? A systematic cross-disciplinary review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509658","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is associated with increased healthcare use and work absenteeism. We aimed to investigate long-term use of healthcare services and social benefits across IBS symptom groups. Additionally, we estimated excess healthcare costs. Methods: A longitudinal population-based study comprising two 5-year follow-up studies: The Danish part of the Multinational Monitoring of Trends and Determinants in Cardiovascular Disease (Dan-MONICA) 1 (1982–1987) and Inter99 (1999–2004) recruited from the western part of Copenhagen County. The total study population (n = 7278) was divided into symptom groups according to degree of IBS definition fulfillment at baseline and/or 5-year follow-up and was followed until 31 December 2013 in Danish central registries. Poisson regression was used for the analyses adjusting for age, sex, length of education, comorbidity, cohort membership and mental vulnerability. Results: IBS symptom groups compared to no IBS symptoms were associated with an increased number of contacts with primary and secondary healthcare, as well as weeks on sickness and disability benefits. Accounting for mental vulnerability decreased the estimates and all but two associations between IBS symptom groups and outcomes remained statistically significant. The two associations that became insignificant were contacts with psychiatric hospitals and weeks on disability pension. The excess unadjusted healthcare costs for IBS were 680 Euros per year and the overall association between symptom groups and total healthcare costs were statistically significant. Conclusions: IBS symptoms influence the long-term use and costs of healthcare, as well as the use of social benefits in the general population. Mental vulnerability explained some, but not all, of the use of healthcare and social benefits.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Poulsen, Charlotte H.","Eplov, Lene F.","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Hastrup, Lene H.","Eliasen, Marie","Dantoft, Thomas M.","Schröder, Andreas","Jørgensen, Torben"],"cuid":["S03-090.60-007783"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Healthcare costs","Irritable bowel syndrome","Prognosis","Sick Leave"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"irritable bowel symptoms use of healthcare costs sickness and disability pension benefits a long term population based study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85047404275&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-090.60-007783","identifier":[{"id":"85047404275","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29762084","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a0f26a94-9bf9-410f-8e56-1dc1c64615f6","au-798bf33b-581e-4f30-827a-445a2ad2d9e1","ku-b38db4f9-f232-4116-9a95-cc8cc314ac46"],"keyword":["Irritable bowel syndrome","healthcare costs","prognosis","sick leave"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-6D82B6BF83EA93B96F855A14038CD510"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Capital Region of Denmark","Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Psychiatric Unit, Region Sjælland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Chalotte H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Chalotte H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene F.","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthøjpau","last":"Hjorthøj","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene H","key":"hastruppau","last":"Hastrup","name":"Hastrup, Lene H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"eliasenpau","last":"Eliasen","name":"Eliasen, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas M.","key":"dantoftpau","last":"Dantoft","name":"Dantoft, Thomas M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","locid":"200c6dd9-43cd-41da-8c27-ce8adb073e24","name":"Schröder, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"a5d9b7f4-413e-465f-a6f2-1f53e2b34186","name":"Jørgensen, Torben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29762084"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1403494818776168","issn":["14034948","16511905"],"issn_org":["14034948"],"issue":"8","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health","pages":"1403494818776168","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047404275"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a0f26a94-9bf9-410f-8e56-1dc1c64615f6","au-798bf33b-581e-4f30-827a-445a2ad2d9e1","ku-b38db4f9-f232-4116-9a95-cc8cc314ac46"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Irritable bowel symptoms, use of healthcare, costs, sickness and disability pension benefits : A long-term population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-090.60-007783","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Patients with borderline personality disorder (BPD) display disturbances in self and other understanding, which is also evident when they narrate events from their own and significant others' lives. In a recent study, we found that patients described both their own and their parents' life stories as more negative and with fewer themes of agency and communion fulfillment. Hence, we examined whether 12 months of psychotherapy would change how patients described their own and their parents' life stories. At baseline, 30 BPD patients and 30 matched control participants described and answered questions about their personal and their parents' life stories. At follow-up, 23 patients and 23 control participants repeated the same procedure after patients had completed 12 months of psychotherapy. At both baseline and follow-up, the life stories were coded for complexity and themes of agency, communion, communion fulfillment, and self-other confusion. BPD patients' personal life stories increased significantly in agency from baseline to follow-up compared with the control group, whereas other aspects of personal and parents' life stories did not change significantly after therapy. Development of agency through the reconstruction of personal life stories may be a crucial mechanism in psychotherapy with BPD patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lind, Majse","Jørgensen, Carsten René","Heinskou, Torben","Simonsen, Sebastian","Bøye, Rikke","Thomsen, Dorthe Kirkegaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-142695"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agency","Autobiographical memories","Borderline personality disorder","Dialectical behavior therapy","Life stories","Meaning making","Mentalization","Narrative identity","PSYCHIATRIC CLASSIFICATION","SELF","Self and other understanding","TRIAL","Therapeutic change"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients with borderline personality disorder show increased agency in life stories after 000000000012 months of psychotherapy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/136062427/Patients_with_borderline_personality_disorder_show_increased_agency_in_life_stories_after_12_months_of_psychotherapy_Accepted_manuscript_2018.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-142695","identifier":[{"id":"85051397450","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000469513900011","type":"wos"},{"id":"30113186","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-17296431-e781-44e9-be42-160a170c918d"],"keyword":["AUTOBIOGRAPHICAL MEMORIES","Agency","BORDERLINE PERSONALITY","Borderline personality disorder","DIALECTICAL BEHAVIOR-THERAPY","Life stories","MEANING-MAKING","MENTALIZATION","NARRATIVE IDENTITY","PSYCHIATRIC CLASSIFICATION","SELF","Self and other understanding","TRANSFERENCE-FOCUSED PSYCHOTHERAPY","TRIAL","Therapeutic change"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9660631968BB632916BC2FAD5D87CB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/136062427/Patients_with_borderline_personality_disorder_show_increased_agency_in_life_stories_after_12_months_of_psychotherapy_Accepted_manuscript_2018.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences","Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - CON AMORE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Majse","key":"lindpau","last":"Lind","locid":"8d869f6e-e52a-4f15-85fd-e20627d55e29","name":"Lind, Majse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"heinskoupau","last":"Heinskou","name":"Heinskou, Torben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bøyepau","last":"Bøye","locid":"c816211a-6dc5-4594-ba92-a5d3aa050cde","name":"Bøye, Rikke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Kirkegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"535c247b-d576-4abf-adb0-3dba6fd5f6eb","name":"Thomsen, Dorthe Kirkegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-5161-6911","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30113186"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1037/pst0000184","issn":["00333204","19391536"],"issn_org":["00333204"],"issue":"2","journal":"Psychotherapy","pages":"274-284","publisher":"American Psychological Association","status":"p","title":"Psychotherapy","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051397450"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-17296431-e781-44e9-be42-160a170c918d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Patients with borderline personality disorder show increased agency in life stories after 12 months of psychotherapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-142695","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Between 1761 and 1776, Christian Horrebow made regular observations of sunspots from Rundetårn in Copenhagen. Based on these observations he writes in 1775 that “it appears that after the course of a certain number of years, the appearance of the Sun repeats itself with respect to the number and size of the spots”. Thus, Horrebow hypothesized the idea of a cyclic Sun several decades before Heinrich Schwabe discovered the solar cycle and estimated its period. This proves the ability of Horrebow as a sunspot observer. In this article, we present a general overview of the work of Christian Horrebow, including a brief biography and a complete bibliography. We also present a translation from Danish to English of his writings on sunspots in the Dansk Historisk Almanak. These writings include tables of daily sunspot measurements of which we discuss the completeness.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten Sønderskov","Karoff, Christoffer","Senthamizh Pavai, V.","Arlt, Rainer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-160147"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Karoff, Christoffer"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Institute for Astrophysics Potsdam"],"keyword":["Solar cycle observations","Sunspots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"christian horrebow s sunspot observations i life and published writings","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.10884.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-160147","identifier":[{"id":"85067248429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-35e88010-fa06-4a8e-a5ce-2382c24889d9"],"keyword":["Solar cycle, observations","Sunspots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FA9093D8827E3519C65D5FE27740074"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.10884.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for astrophysics potsdam","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Astrophysics Potsdam","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Sønderskov","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9bcfa0f7-ade7-4627-adf6-56adab418d7c","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten Sønderskov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"karoffpau","last":"Karoff","locid":"b71daf07-cedf-42bb-bd7c-b0af441e57cd","name":"Karoff, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0003-2009-7965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"senthamizhpavaipau","last":"Senthamizh Pavai","name":"Senthamizh Pavai, V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rainer","key":"arltpau","last":"Arlt","name":"Arlt, Rainer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11207-019-1465-z","issn":["00380938","1573093X"],"issn_org":["00380938"],"issue":"6","journal":"Solar Physics","paperid":"77","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Solar Physics","volume":"294"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067248429"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-35e88010-fa06-4a8e-a5ce-2382c24889d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Christian Horrebow’s Sunspot Observations – I. : Life and Published Writings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-160147","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Ischial tuberosity fractures and complications may be an under recognized diagnosis in adolescent athletes. Operative interventions differ and may include anchor re-fixations, resections and osteostimulating drilling and partial hamstring releases. This case report illustrates a novel and less invasive management of a non-union following a proximal ischial tuberosity avulsion. This approach has to our knowledge not previously been described. PRESENTATION OF CASE: The patient, a 14 years old female athlete, was complaining of sharp pain in the right side of the groin region, after an acute injury during a handball game. The pain was concentrated at the insertion of the adductor muscle group to the superior pubic ramus and the pubic symphysis. She was referred to our orthopaedic sports clinic after 6 months of unsuccessful conservative treatment. An MRI scan showed an ischial tuberosity non-union with a displacement less than 10 mm. Nine months after injury a surgical procedure was performed with the patient under general anaesthesia. An ultrasound guided fenestration of the non-union of the ischial tuberosity with a 1.6 mm Kirshner wire was performed. The enthesis was fenestrated 10 times, using a 1.2 mm syringe. Finally, a 5 ml local anaesthetic was injected in the area. 17 months after the trauma and 8 months postoperatively the patient had a full return to normal day activities including pain free squats and lunges. Radiologically the non-union was healed. CONCLUSION: This novel and less invasive surgical procedure may therefore be seen as a possible treatment option to non-union of the ischial tuberosity with minimal displacement.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jorgensen, Jens Erik","Mølgaard, Carsten","Kristinsson, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-070616"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fenestration","Non union","Sports injury","Trauma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surgical fenestration and rehabilitation of a sports traumatic non union ischial tuberosity fracture case report","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijscr.2018.11.018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-070616","identifier":[{"id":"30472632","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85056849035","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000452767800089","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-46f367df-5e8f-4f0a-a6f1-b45ac1ac7eff"],"keyword":["Adolescent apophyseal injury","Fenestration","Ischial tuberosity avulsion","Non-union","Sports injury","Trauma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8F71A28D503EEC713A7F36055749A3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/291963127/1_s2.0_S221026121830525X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijscr.2018.11.018","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Physiotherapy and Occupational Therapy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Erik","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, Jens Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten M","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"e49f2521-d695-41bf-b1c2-595166292dfd","name":"Mølgaard, Carsten","name_org":"Mølgaard, Carsten M","orcid":"0000-0002-7427-8078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kristinssonpau","last":"Kristinsson","locid":"d279d9c4-5f5e-4d78-a617-a3bde3352dbf","name":"Kristinsson, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30472632"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijscr.2018.11.018","issn":["22102612"],"journal":"International Journal of Surgery Case Reports","pages":"362-366","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Surgery Case Reports","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056849035"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-46f367df-5e8f-4f0a-a6f1-b45ac1ac7eff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Surgical fenestration and rehabilitation of a sports traumatic non-union ischial tuberosity fracture - Case report","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-070616","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
