","key":"gustavsonpau","last":"Gustavson","locid":"1ebbd6c1-641f-40c9-a30f-7652da2113f9","name":"Gustavson, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8242-0276","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn M.","key":"jenssenpau","last":"Jenssen","locid":"bdf2a410-2b73-4fd3-a4d1-5b2a0341d167","name":"Jenssen, Bjørn Munro","name_org":"Jenssen, Bjørn M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anders","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, Anders","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Aqqalu","key":"rosingasvidpau","last":"Rosing-Asvid","name":"Rosing-Asvid, Aqqalu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Carsten","key":"grøndahlpau","last":"Grøndahl","name":"Grøndahl, Carsten","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper B.","key":"mosbacherpau","last":"Mosbacher","locid":"9c13fa64-c01e-45a5-a610-91a95c7c080b","name":"Mosbacher, Jesper Bruun","name_org":"Mosbacher, Jesper B.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ursula","key":"siebertpau","last":"Siebert","name":"Siebert, Ursula","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Morten","key":"trylandpau","last":"Tryland","name":"Tryland, Morten","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Gert","key":"mulvadpau","last":"Mulvad","name":"Mulvad, Gert","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Erik W.","key":"bornpau","last":"Born","name":"Born, Erik W.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 9","first":"Kristin","key":"laidrepau","last":"Laidre","name":"Laidre, Kristin","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Øystein","key":"wiigpau","last":"Wiig","name":"Wiig, Øystein","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rune","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","locid":"86cb72ef-d48d-4395-94ee-b1c0bc3e33b5","name":"Dietz, Rune","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulf","key":"magnussonpau","last":"Magnusson","name":"Magnusson, Ulf","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00300-018-2307-4","issn":["07224060","14322056"],"issn_org":["14322056"],"issue":"9","journal":"Polar Biology","pages":"1671-1680","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Polar Biology","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044097852"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e7a9973e-7207-4086-9c55-0f8daec22f36","ku-c0f2a601-7601-4196-ad59-1d14dce49e91"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence of antibodies against <i>Brucella spp.</i> in West Greenland polar bears (<i>Ursus maritimus</i>) and East Greenland muskoxen (<i>Ovibos moschatus</i>)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-029453","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Activation of energy expenditure in thermogenic fat is a promising strategy to improve metabolic health, yet the dynamic processes that evoke this response are poorly understood. Here we show that synthesis of the mitochondrial phospholipid cardiolipin is indispensable for stimulating and sustaining thermogenic fat function. Cardiolipin biosynthesis is robustly induced in brown and beige adipose upon cold exposure. Mimicking this response through overexpression of cardiolipin synthase (Crls1) enhances energy consumption in mouse and human adipocytes. Crls1 deficiency in thermogenic adipocytes diminishes inducible mitochondrial uncoupling and elicits a nuclear transcriptional response through endoplasmic reticulum stress-mediated retrograde communication. Cardiolipin depletion in brown and beige fat abolishes adipose thermogenesis and glucose uptake, which renders animals insulin resistant. We further identify a rare human CRLS1 variant associated with insulin resistance and show that adipose CRLS1 levels positively correlate with insulin sensitivity. Thus, adipose cardiolipin has a powerful impact on organismal energy homeostasis through thermogenic fat bioenergetics. Sustarsic et al. reveal that synthesis of the mitochondrial phospholipid cardiolipin is a hallmark of brown and beige fat activation by cold temperature. This single lipid species in thermogenic fat not only shapes adipose mitochondrial bioenergetics but also exerts profound control over whole-body insulin sensitivity and metabolic flexibility.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Sustarsic, Elahu G","Ma, Tao","Lynes, Matthew D","Larsen, Michael","Karavaeva, Iuliia","Havelund, Jesper F","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Jedrychowski, Mark P","Moreno-Torres, Marta","Lundh, Morten","Plucińska, Kaja","Jespersen, Naja Z","Grevengoed, Trisha J.","Kramar, Barbara","Peics, Julia","Hansen, Jakob Bondo","Shamsi, Farnaz","Forss, Isabel","Neess, Ditte","Keipert, Susanne","Wang, Jianing","Stohlmann, Katharina","Brandslund, Ivan","Christensen, Cramer","Jørgensen, Marit E","Linneberg, Allan","Pedersen, Oluf","Kiebish, Michael A","Qvortrup, Klaus","Han, Xianlin","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Jastroch, Martin","Mandrup, Susanne","Kjaer, Andreas","Gygi, Steven P","Hansen, Torben","Gillum, Matthew P.","Grarup, Niels","Emanuelli, Brice","Nielsen, Søren","Scheele, Camilla","Tseng, Yu-Hua","Færgeman, Nils J","Gerhart-Hines, Zachary"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-043882"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gerhart-Hines, Zachary"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BERG Health","Harvard Medical School","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","The University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio"],"keyword":["Cardiolipin","Insulin Resistance","Lipid Metabolism","Mitochondria","Phospholipids","Thermogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiolipin synthesis in brown and beige fat mitochondria is essential for systemic energy homeostasis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmet.2018.05.003","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank members of the Gerhart-Hines and Tseng labs for discussions. We are grateful to Genoway for assistance in the design and generation of Crls1 floxed mice. We thank Dr. Miao Wang for technical assistance with targeted brown fat lipidomics. The Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx) Project was supported by the Common Fund of the Office of the Director of the NIH , and by NCI , NHGRI , NHLBI , NIDA , NIMH , and NINDS . The Core Facility for Integrated Microscopy (CFIM) is acknowledged for access to electron microscopes. This work was supported by funding from NIDDK grants R01DK077097 and R01DK102898 (Y.H.-T.), F32DK102320 (M.D.L.), 30DK036836 (Joslin Diabetes Center's Diabetes Research Center), the Danish Diabetes Academy (M.M.-T. and N.Z.J.), the Novo Nordisk Foundation (T.H., M.P.G., B.E., N.G., C.S., and Z.G.-H.), and the Danish Council for Independent Research-Medical Sciences (M. Lundh, N.J.F.), including Sapere Aude Starting grant 4002-00024 (Z.G.-H). In addition, this project has received funding from the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation Programme (grant agreement no. 639382 ). The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research is an independent Research Center at the University of Copenhagen partially funded by an unrestricted donation from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( http://cbmr.ku.dk/ )."],"id":"S02-097.78-043882","identifier":[{"id":"29861389","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85047218679","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6038052","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8028fe7f-422a-440b-b5d5-c67606aa09aa","sdu-ac1be669-d852-4f0c-8624-0ba53d73a566"],"keyword":["CHOP-10","CRLS1","beige adipose","brown adipose","cardiolipin","insulin resistance","lipid metabolism","mitochondria","phospholipids","thermogenesis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AC1D7BB68A365502788AC6F9609A5E78"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/199881781/1_s2.0_S1550413118303103_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141723640/1_s2.0_S1550413118303103_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa",