{"abstract":"Roux-en-Y Gastric bypass surgery (RYGB) is emerging as a powerful tool for treatment of obesity and may also cause remission of type 2 diabetes. However, the molecular mechanism of RYGB leading to diabetes remission independent of weight loss remains elusive. In this study, we profiled plasma metabolites and proteins of 10 normal glucose-tolerant obese (NO) and 9 diabetic obese (DO) patients before and 1-week, 3-months, 1-year after RYGB. 146 proteins and 128 metabolites from both NO and DO groups at all four stages were selected for further analysis. By analyzing a set of bi-molecular associations among the corresponding network of the subjects with our newly developed computational method, we defined the represented physiological states (called the edge-states that reflect the interactions among the bio-molecules), and the related molecular networks of NO and DO patients, respectively. The principal component analyses (PCA) revealed that the edge states of the post-RYGB NO subjects were significantly different from those of the post-RYGB DO patients. Particularly, the time-dependent changes of the molecular hub-networks differed between DO and NO groups after RYGB. In conclusion, by developing molecular network-based systems signatures, we for the first time reveal that RYGB generates a unique path for diabetes remission independent of weight loss.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Li, Qing-Run","Wang, Zi-Ming","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Wang, Dan-Dan","Su, Zhi-Duan","Gao, Xian-Fu","Wu, Qing-Qing","Zhang, Hui-Ping","Zhu, Li","Li, Rong-Xia","Jacobsen, Siv H","Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","Dirksen, Carsten","Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","Petersen, Jacob S.","Madsbad, Sten","Clausen, Trine R.","Diderichsen, Børge","Chen, Luo-Nan","Holst, Jens Juul","Zeng, Rong","Wu, Jia-Rui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395080"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blood Proteins metabolism","Diabetes","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 blood","Gastric Bypass","Gastric bypass surgery","Gene Regulatory Networks","Humans","Journal Article","Metabolome","Network","Obesity genetics","Principal component analysis","Systems biology","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systems signatures reveal unique remission path of type 000000000002 diabetes following roux en y gastric bypass surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2018.01.018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-395080","identifier":[{"id":"29422288","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5835566","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85044854928","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-02afc2e8-4e62-4a8f-a3e6-5b0e26127bae"],"keyword":["Blood Proteins/metabolism","Diabetes","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/blood","Gastric Bypass","Gastric bypass surgery","Gene Regulatory Networks","Humans","Journal Article","Metabolome","Network","Network biomarker","Obesity/genetics","Principal Component Analysis","Systems Biology","Weight Loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCD41AB431FDEDC03688C5ED3747CFB3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2018.01.018","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209546068/1_s2.0_S2352396418300227_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Translational Metabolic Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Qing-Run","key":"liqingrunpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qing-Run","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zi-Ming","key":"wangzimingpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zi-Ming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai Jacob Wewer","key":"weweralbrechtsennicolaijpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","name_org":"Albrechtsen, Nicolai Jacob Wewer","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan-Dan","key":"wangdandanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dan-Dan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhi-Duan","key":"suzhiduanpau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Zhi-Duan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xian-Fu","key":"gaoxianfupau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Xian-Fu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qing-Qing","key":"wuqingqingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Qing-Qing","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hui-Ping","key":"zhanghuipingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hui-Ping","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"zhulipau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Li","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rong-Xia","key":"lirongxiapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Rong-Xia","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"SivHesse","key":"jacobsensivhpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"9258b6d4-2bc2-4170-93e9-56b995a9601d","name":"Jacobsen, Siv H","name_org":"Jacobsen, SivHesse","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils Bruun","key":"jørgensennilsbruunpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"a0a7317b-bb0a-42c1-9853-a086b51dff67","name":"Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksencarstenpau","last":"Dirksen","locid":"b2fdf354-7974-4c22-8fb5-1753eeea4728","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine N.","key":"bojsenmollerkirstinenpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"0c7b0831-8bcd-4ed4-84d6-565f8424f3e9","name":"Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","name_org":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob S.","key":"petersenjacobspau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jacob S.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadstenpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Trine R.","key":"clausentrinerpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Trine R.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Børge","key":"diderichsenbørgepau","last":"Diderichsen","name":"Diderichsen, Børge","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Luo-Nan","key":"chenluonanpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Luo-Nan","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rong","key":"zengrongpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Rong","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jia-Rui","key":"wujiaruipau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Jia-Rui","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29422288"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ebiom.2018.01.018","issn":["23523964"],"journal":"EBioMedicine","pages":"234-240","status":"p","title":"EBioMedicine","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044854928"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-02afc2e8-4e62-4a8f-a3e6-5b0e26127bae"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systems signatures reveal unique remission-path of Type 2 diabetes following Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395080","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Gastric bypass surgery leads to profound changes in the secretion of gut hormones with effects on metabolism, appetite, and food intake. Here, we discuss their contributions to the improvement in glucose tolerance and the weight loss that results from the operations. We find that the improved glucose tolerance is due the following events: a negative energy balance and resulting weight loss, which improve first hepatic and later peripheral insulin sensitivity, in combination with increased postprandial insulin secretion elicited particularly by exaggerated glucagon-like peptide-1 responses. The weight loss is due to loss of appetite resulting in reduced energy intake, and we find it probable that this process is driven by exaggerated secretion of appetite-regulating gut hormones including, but probably not limited to, glucagon-like peptide-1 and peptide-YY. The increased secretion is due to an accelerated exposure to and absorption of nutrients in the small intestine. This places the weight loss and the gut hormones in key positions with respect to the metabolic improvements after bypass surgery.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","Svane, Maria S.","Jørgensen, Nils B","Dirksen, Carsten","Martinussen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415994"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Appetite physiology","Bariatric surgery","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 surgery","Dietary Carbohydrates metabolism","Dietary Proteins metabolism","Digestion physiology","Eating physiology","Gastric Bypass","Glucagon Like Peptide 1 physiology","Humans","Insulin Resistance physiology","Intestinal Absorption physiology","Nutrients metabolism","Obesity Morbid complications","Weight Loss physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mechanisms in bariatric surgery gut hormones diabetes resolution and weight loss","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soard.2018.03.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-415994","identifier":[{"id":"85047021783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29776493","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5974695","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-25c14ae7-9fe6-405b-98b7-cc0e64996b51"],"keyword":["Appetite/physiology","Bariatric Surgery","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/surgery","Dietary Carbohydrates/metabolism","Dietary Proteins/metabolism","Digestion/physiology","Eating/physiology","Gastric Bypass","Gastrointestinal Hormones/physiology","Glucagon-Like Peptide 1/physiology","Humans","Insulin Resistance/physiology","Intestinal Absorption/physiology","Nutrients/metabolism","Obesity, Morbid/complications","Peptide YY/physiology","Weight Loss/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-40560510C65FED4BF50AF9BB56D726CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soard.2018.03.003","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/214405140/1_s2.0_S1550728918301242_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"0c7b0831-8bcd-4ed4-84d6-565f8424f3e9","name":"Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","name_org":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Saur","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"4cc109fb-b416-4327-a1bd-c980486fa717","name":"Svane, Maria S.","name_org":"Svane, Maria Saur","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils Bruun","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"694893d0-af33-4f21-ad66-945a1522de37","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","name_org":"Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","locid":"b2fdf354-7974-4c22-8fb5-1753eeea4728","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoffer","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","name":"Martinussen, Christoffer","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29776493"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.soard.2018.03.003","issn":["15507289"],"issue":"5","journal":"Surgery for Obesity and Related Diseases","pages":"708-714","status":"p","title":"Surgery for Obesity and Related Diseases","title_org":"Surgery for obesity and related diseases : official journal of the American Society for Bariatric Surgery","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047021783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-25c14ae7-9fe6-405b-98b7-cc0e64996b51"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mechanisms in bariatric surgery : Gut hormones, diabetes resolution, and weight loss","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415994","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Hypoglycaemia remains the main limiting factor in type 1 diabetes management. We developed an insulin-dependent glucagon dosing regimen for treatment of mild hypoglycaemia based on simulations. A validated glucose-insulin-glucagon model was used to describe seven virtual patients with insulin pump-treated type 1 diabetes. In each simulation, one of ten different and individualized subcutaneous insulin boluses was administered to decrease plasma glucose (PG) from 7.0 to ≤3.9 mmol/l. Insulin levels were estimated as ratio of actual to baseline serum insulin concentration (se/ba-insulin), insulin on board (IOB) or percentage of IOB to total daily insulin dose (IOB/TDD). Insulin bolus sizes were chosen to provide pre-defined insulin levels when PG reached 3.9 mmol/l, where one of 17 subcutaneous glucagon boluses was administered. Optimum glucagon bolus to treat mild hypoglycaemia at varying insulin levels was the lowest dose that in most patients caused PG peak between 5.0 and 10.0 mmol/l and sustained PG ≥ 3.9 mmol/l for 2 hr after the bolus. PG response to glucagon declined with increasing insulin levels. The glucagon dose to optimally treat mild hypoglycaemia depended exponentially on insulin levels, regardless of how insulin was estimated. A 125-μg glucagon dose was needed to optimally treat mild hypoglycaemia when insulin levels were equal to baseline levels. In contrast, glucagon doses >500 μg were needed when se/ba-insulin >2.5, IOB >2.0 U or IOB/TDD >6%. Although the proposed model-based glucagon regimen needs confirmation in clinical trials, this is the first attempt to develop an insulin-dependent glucagon dosing regimen for treatment of insulin-induced mild hypoglycaemia in patients with type 1 diabetes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ranjan, Ajenthen","Wendt, Sabrina L","Schmidt, Signe","Madsbad, Sten","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsen, Henrik","Knudsen, Carsten B","Jørgensen, John B","Nørgaard, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527162"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relationship between optimum mini doses of glucagon and insulin levels when treating mild hypoglycaemia in patients with type 000000000001 diabetes a simulation study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527162","identifier":[{"id":"85031093686","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28922582","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dfd9155b-c879-4625-beff-55d6f4e1dc22"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-954EE7D3E22EC5ACCA13DEAEE4ECCC79"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"zealand pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ZEA","l3nl":"Zealand Pharma A/S","l3nn":"Zealand Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Zealand Pharma","namevar":["Zealand Pharma A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ajenthen","key":"ranjanpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sabrina L","key":"wendtpau","last":"Wendt","name":"Wendt, Sabrina L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Signe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten B","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Carsten B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, John B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28922582"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.12907","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"3","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"322-330","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031093686"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dfd9155b-c879-4625-beff-55d6f4e1dc22"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Relationship between Optimum Mini‐doses of Glucagon and Insulin Levels when Treating Mild Hypoglycaemia in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes : A Simulation Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527162","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Common CCR5-∆32 and HLA alleles only explain a minority of the HIV long-term non-progressor (LTNP) and elite controller (EC) phenotypes. To identify rare genetic variants contributing to the slow disease progression phenotypes, we performed whole exome sequencing (WES) on seven LTNPs and four ECs. HLA and CCR5 allele status, total HIV DNA reservoir size, as well as variant-related functional differences between the ECs, LTNPs, and eleven age- and gender-matched HIV-infected non-controllers on antiretroviral therapy (NCARTs) were investigated. Several rare variants were identified in genes involved in innate immune sensing, CD4-dependent infectivity, HIV trafficking, and HIV transcription mainly within the LTNP group. ECs and LTNPs had a significantly lower HIV reservoir compared to NCARTs. Furthermore, three LTNPs with variants affecting HIV nuclear import showed integrated HIV DNA levels below detection limit after in vitro infection. HIV slow progressors with variants in the TLR and NOD2 pathways showed reduced pro-inflammatory responses compared to matched controls. Low-range plasma levels of fibronectin was observed in a LTNP harboring two FN1 variants. Taken together, this study identified rare variants in LTNPs as well as in one EC, which may contribute to understanding of HIV pathogenesis and these slow progressor phenotypes, especially in individuals without protecting CCR5-∆32 and HLA alleles.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nissen, Sara Konstantin","Christiansen, Mette","Helleberg, Marie","Kjær, Kathrine","Jørgensen, Sofie Eg","Gerstoft, Jan","Katzenstein, Terese L","Benfield, Thomas","Kronborg, Gitte","Larsen, Carsten S","Laursen, Alex","Pedersen, Gitte","Jakobsen, Martin R","Tolstrup, Martin","Mogensen, Trine H"],"cuid":["S03-098.84-007460"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"lev