7ae-52f680bd2edf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Identitetsdannelse","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-214434","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Der er almindelige og sjældne og næsten usandsynlige stormfloder. Vandstandene i den vestlige Østersø nåede nærmest vanvittige højder under stormfloden den 12.-13.november 1872 og forårsagede oversvømmelser langs mange danske kyster. Selvom det er længe siden, og der gennem tiden er skrevet meget om netop denne stormflod, har den stadig stor betydning. For hvad vil en tilsvarende stormflod have af konsekvenser i dag, og hvor stor er sandsynligheden for, at den indtræffer? Hvis stormflodens sandsynlighed ganges med dens konsekvenser, kan vi tale om en oversvømmelsesrisiko;en risiko, der kan opgøres økonomisk ud fra de skader, den forvolder tillige med fx tab af menneskeliv, som vi ikke i Danmark har tradition for at værdisætte. Når vi som kystsamfund, lokalt eller nationalt, vælger at beskytte os mod fremtidige stormfloder til et vist niveau, træffer vi også et valg om ”at løbe en risiko”. Vi oplevede det under Egon, under Bodil, 1.-2. November 2006 og ved andre lejligheder, at huse og heleboligkvarterer blev oversvømmet. Det vil ske igen. Mens vandstandene under de nævnte hændelser tilsyneladende var ekstreme i flere af de berørte områder, viser historien også, at skaderne selvfølgelig langt hen ad vejen forårsages af, at vi har valgt at bo og leve i lavtliggende kystområder. I forhold til enkeltejendomme er det måske de almindelige og halvsjældne stormfloder, der skal ydes beskyttelse imod, mens der i forhold til større byområder og infrastruktur som motorveje, jernbaner og metrolinjerbør gøres helt andre overvejelser om konsekvenserne af de næsten usandsynligestormfloder. Og hvor usandsynlig eller sjælden var 1872 stormfloden egentlig? Me dudgangspunkt i 1872 stormfloden diskuteres, hvordan vi – ikke mindst set i lyset af klimaændringer og havstigninger, kan øge videngrundlaget forud for de næste næstenusandsynlige hændelser og håndtere denne udfordring.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Carlo Sass","Sørensen, Per","Jürgensen, Carsten","Jørgensen, Niels-Erik","Jebens, Martin","Knudsen, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-338276"],"event":{"end":"2017-01-27","place":"Helsingør, dk","start":"2017-01-25","title":"19. Danske Havforskermøde","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Coastal Authority"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000001872","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128586462/PROGRAM_OG_ABSTRACT_BOG.PDF","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-338276","ids":["dtu-70f13352-a60c-4cf0-8ac1-8381b276365a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D05D59B8471C530A11D21E65CD8BAB69"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128586462/PROGRAM_OG_ABSTRACT_BOG.PDF","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodesy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Coastal Authority"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carlo Sass","key":"sørensencarlosasspau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"bcf14797-1194-4a3c-998b-ccaef0e178b2","name":"Sørensen, Carlo Sass","orcid":"0000-0001-5754-6440","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"sørensenperpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Per","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"jürgensencarstenpau","last":"Jürgensen","name":"Jürgensen, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels-Erik","key":"jørgensennielserikpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Niels-Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"jebensmartinpau","last":"Jebens","name":"Jebens, Martin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"knudsenperpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"ed19967f-42c8-4114-b94d-7f6f43f931bb","name":"Knudsen, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-4640-6746","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"108","status":"p","title":"19. Danske Havforskermøde. Program &amp; præsentationer"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-70f13352-a60c-4cf0-8ac1-8381b276365a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"1872","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-338276","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Liver toxicity is frequently seen in relation to allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT), but pathogenesis and the risk factors are poorly understood. The purpose of this study was to investigate associations between liver toxicity, gastrointestinal toxicity, and levels of immune-regulating cytokines during the early post-transplantation period. We prospectively included 81 children and adults undergoing HSCT after myeloablative conditioning. Alanine aminotransferase (ALT), total bilirubin levels, and international normalized ratio were measured longitudinally until 3 months after the transplantation and related to levels of inflammatory markers (C-reactive protein [CRP], IL-6, and IL-10) and to plasma citrulline as a marker of intestinal toxicity during the first 3 weeks after HSCT. The majority of patients experienced ALT levels above the normal range (45 U/L) with significant increases at 3 months after HSCT. Increased levels of total bilirubin were observed in 26% during the 3-month period. Citrulline levels decreased significantly to a nadir at day 7 (B = .23; 95% confidence interval [CI], .12 to .35; P < .0001), but citrulline levels at nadir were not associated with parameters of liver toxicity. However, a faster reconstitution of mucosa with higher citrulline levels at day +21 correlated with lower bilirubin levels 3 months after HSCT (r = -.26, P = .034) and increased overall survival (hazard ratio, .88; 95% CI, .79 to .97; P = .008) Increased levels of CRP and IL-6 at day 7 after HSCT correlated positively with ALT and bilirubin, and in the multivariate analysis, IL-6 at day 7 appeared to be the only predicting risk factor for increased mean bilirubin during the early post-transplantation phase (B = .01; 95% CI, .01 to .02; P = .001) as well as maximum levels of bilirubin (B = .3; 95% CI, .12 to .48; P= .001) and occurrence of sinusoidal obstruction syndrome during the first 3 months after HSCT (odds ratio, 1.003; 95% CI, 1.001 to 1.005; P = .002). The results of this study indicate that liver toxicity after HSCT is associated with an increased inflammatory response mounted during the phase of maximal gastrointestinal toxicity in the early phase after transplantation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jordan, Karina","Pontoppidan, Peter Erik Lotko","Uhlving, Hilde Hylland","Kielsen, Katrine","Burrin, Douglas G.","Weischendorff, Sarah","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Jørgensen, Marianne H.","Heilmann, Carsten","Sengeløv, Henrik","Müller, Klaus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415392"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine"],"keyword":["Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Hepatotoxicity","Inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gastrointestinal toxicity systemic inflammation and liver biochemistry in allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-415392","identifier":[{"id":"85019031104","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28344059","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-24ca2713-9f23-4e92-9177-4dcae917a3ba"],"keyword":["Hematopoietic stem cell transplantation","Hepatotoxicity","Inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A26A6B3EC50F572120710B7648C91B5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"baylor college of medicine","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Baylor College of Medicine","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Clinical and Experimental Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Karina","key":"jordanpau","last":"Jordan","name":"Jordan, Karina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter","key":"pontoppidanpau","last":"Pontoppidan","locid":"5ee6fd90-dccc-4956-a943-40dc71a17c0c","name":"Pontoppidan, Peter Erik Lotko","name_org":"Pontoppidan, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hilde Hylland","key":"uhlvingpau","last":"Uhlving","name":"Uhlving, Hilde Hylland","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine","key":"kielsenpau","last":"Kielsen","name":"Kielsen, Katrine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Douglas G.","key":"burrinpau","last":"Burrin","name":"Burrin, Douglas G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"weischendorffpau","last":"Weischendorff","name":"Weischendorff, Sarah","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ib J","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b8f0594e-4a73-4cf7-9117-a9eb69323873","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","name_org":"Christensen, Ib J","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne H.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Marianne H.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"heilmannpau","last":"Heilmann","name":"Heilmann, Carsten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"sengeløvpau","last":"Sengeløv","locid":"ff0cb82b-deb8-4d4e-b871-8f70d359af15","name":"Sengeløv, Henrik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Klaus","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"b909f13e-79e3-4363-aaff-e5a5ecbdf7ce","name":"Müller, Klaus","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28344059"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbmt.2017.03.021","issn":["10838791","15236536"],"issn_org":["10838791"],"issue":"7","journal":"Biology of Blood and Marrow Transplantation","pages":"1170-1176","status":"p","title":"Biology of Blood and Marrow Transplantation","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019031104"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-24ca2713-9f23-4e92-9177-4dcae917a3ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gastrointestinal toxicity, systemic inflammation, and liver biochemistry in allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415392","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Positron emission tomography (PET) can, when used with appropriate radioligands, non-invasively generate temporal and spatial information about acute changes in brain neurotransmitter systems. We for the first time evaluate the novel 5-HT2A receptor agonist PET radioligand, [11C]Cimbi-36, for its sensitivity to detect changes in endogenous cerebral 5-HT levels, as induced by different pharmacological challenges. To enable a direct translation of PET imaging data to changes in brain 5-HT levels, we calibrated the [11C]Cimbi-36 PET signal in the pig brain by simultaneous measurements of extracellular 5-HT levels with microdialysis and [11C]Cimbi-36 PET after various acute interventions (saline, citalopram, citalopram þ pindolol, fenfluramine). In a subset of pigs, para-chlorophenylalanine pretreatment was given to deplete cerebral 5-HT. The interventions increased the cerebral extracellular 5-HT levels to 2–11 times baseline, with fenfluramine being the most potent pharmacological enhancer of 5-HT release, and induced a varying degree of decline in[11C]Cimbi-36 binding in the brain, consistent with the occupancy competition model. The observed correlation between changes in the extracellular 5-HT level in the pig brain and the 5-HT2A receptor occupancy indicates that [11C]Cimbi-36 binding is sensitive to changes in endogenous 5-HT levels, although only detectable with PET when the 5- HT release is sufficiently high.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Louise M","Weikop, Pia","Villadsen, Jonas","Visnapuu, Tanel","Ettrup, Anders","Hansen, Hanne D","Baandrup, Anders O","Andersen, Flemming L","Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","Thomsen, Carsten","Jespersen, Bo","Knudsen, Gitte M"],"cuid":["S02-095.34-001691"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Estonia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Tartu"],"keyword":["5 HT","Brain imaging","Kinetic modelling","Neurosurgery","Positron Emission Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cerebral 000000000005 ht release correlates with 000000000011c cimbi000000000036 pet measures of 000000000005 ht000000000002a receptor occupancy in the pig brain","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5381441/pdf/10.1177_0271678X16629483.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.34-001691","identifier":[{"id":"26825776","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5381441","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000393903900004","type":"wos"},{"id":"85009840456","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-217dc64a-ba94-4cf7-bf9e-04a36cff4bec","ku-9d1b7355-7e57-4ff2-9b76-1753c18b86b5"],"keyword":["5-HT","Positron emission tomography","brain imaging","kinetic modelling","neurosurgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C43864354DE4AE92BE8A9DB35B084CCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5381441?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5381441/pdf/10.1177_0271678X16629483.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","nam