"Visnapuu","name":"Visnapuu, Tanel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","name":"Ettrup, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne D.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Hanne D.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders O","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","name":"Baandrup, Anders O","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Flemming L.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","name_org":"Andersen, Flemming L.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten R","key":"bjarkampau","last":"Bjarkam","locid":"a05346d7-147b-4c78-8bc5-1f6c771af2c6","name":"Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","name_org":"Bjarkam, Carsten R","orcid":"0000-0002-0164-9595","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Carsten","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"3df25ea7-9eb3-4b95-9aca-5171b7d5870f","name":"Thomsen, Carsten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","name":"Jespersen, Bo","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gitte M.","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"f02aee9e-69cf-491a-9765-ff062f734db8","name":"Knudsen, Gitte Moos","name_org":"Knudsen, Gitte M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1508-6866","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26825776"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0271678x16629483","issn":["0271678X","15597016"],"issn_org":["0271678X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Cerebral Blood Flow and Metabolism","pages":"425-434","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cerebral Blood Flow and Metabolism","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009840456"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-217dc64a-ba94-4cf7-bf9e-04a36cff4bec","ku-9d1b7355-7e57-4ff2-9b76-1753c18b86b5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cerebral 5-HT release correlates with [11C]Cimbi36 PET measures of 5-HT2A receptor occupancy in the pig brain","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.34-001691","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Currently, no consensus exists on a model describing endogenous glucose production (EGP) as a function of glucagon concentrations. Reliable simulations to determine the glucagon dose preventing or treating hypoglycemia or to tune a dual-hormone artificial pancreas control algorithm need a validated glucoregulatory model including the effect of glucagon. Methods: Eight type 1 diabetes (T1D) patients each received a subcutaneous (SC) bolus of insulin on four study days to induce mild hypoglycemia followed by a SC bolus of saline or 100, 200, or 300 µg of glucagon. Blood samples were analyzed for concentrations of glucagon, insulin, and glucose. We fitted pharmacokinetic (PK) models to insulin and glucagon data using maximum likelihood and maximum a posteriori estimation methods. Similarly, we fitted a pharmacodynamic (PD) model to glucose data. The PD model included multiplicative effects of insulin and glucagon on EGP. Bias and precision of PD model test fits were assessed by mean predictive error (MPE) and mean absolute predictive error (MAPE). Results: Assuming constant variables in a subject across nonoutlier visits and using thresholds of ±15% MPE and 20% MAPE, we accepted at least one and at most three PD model test fits in each of the seven subjects. Thus, we successfully validated the PD model by leave-one-out cross-validation in seven out of eight T1D patients. Conclusions: The PD model accurately simulates glucose excursions based on plasma insulin and glucagon concentrations. The reported PK/PD model including equations and fitted parameters allows for in silico experiments that may help improve diabetes treatment involving glucagon for prevention of hypoglycemia.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","Ranjan, Ajenthen","Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","Schmidt, Signe","Boye Knudsen, Carsten","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Madsbad, Sten","Madsen, Henrik","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Jørgensen, John Bagterp"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-033507"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cross validation","Glucagon","Glucoregulatory model","Parameter estimation","Simulation model","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cross validation of a glucose insulin glucagon pharmacodynamics model for simulation using data from patients with type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1932296817693254","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.78-033507","identifier":[{"id":"28654314","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5951032","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85032819571","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2980a238-2312-475a-9fad-8b0741588ac0","ku-c411a33f-7b07-4063-8982-702f43d2e805"],"keyword":["Cross-validation","Glucagon","Glucoregulatory model","Parameter Estimation","Simulation model","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B5DC4634E4CAF29C6559397E6A3ED778"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5951032?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1932296817693254","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/130315209/WENDT_manuscript_2_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Scientific Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"zealand pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ZEA","l3nl":"Zealand Pharma A/S","l3nn":"Zealand Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Zealand Pharma","namevar":["Zealand Pharma A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sabrina Lyngbye","key":"wendtsabrinalyngbyepau","last":"Wendt","locid":"053fcca6-8b59-439b-ad9a-4abe1507ae4f","name":"Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","orcid":"0000-0002-1520-0254","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ajenthen","key":"ranjanajenthenpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Kloppenborg","key":"møllerjankloppenborgpau","last":"Møller","locid":"06a667bd-2e4d-493d-ada6-191296446a2e","name":"Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","orcid":"0000-0002-6100-043X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"schmidtsignepau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Signe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"boyeknudsencarstenpau","last":"Boye Knudsen","name":"Boye Knudsen, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten Boye","key":"knudsencarstenboyepau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Carsten Boye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadstenpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"madsenhenrikpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardkirstenpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenjohnbagterppau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d2bc6de4-a5c6-43f7-8712-606bd02a88e9","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","orcid":"0000-0001-9799-2808","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28654314"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1932296817693254","issn":["19322968"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Diabetes Science and Technology","pages":"1101-1111","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Diabetes Science and Technology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032819571"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2980a238-2312-475a-9fad-8b0741588ac0","ku-c411a33f-7b07-4063-8982-702f43d2e805"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cross-Validation of a Glucose-Insulin-Glucagon Pharmacodynamics Model for Simulation Using Data From Patients With Type 1 Diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-033507","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Responsiveness of a clinical test is highly relevant in order to evaluate the effect of a given intervention. However, the responsiveness of clinical tests for people with neck pain has not been adequately evaluated. The objective of the present study was to examine the responsiveness of four clinical tests which are low cost and easy to perform in a clinical setting, including the craniocervical flexion test, cervical active range of movement, test for the cervical extensors and pressure pain threshold testing. METHODS: This study is a secondary analysis of data collected in a previously published randomised controlled trial. Participants were randomized to either physical training, exercises and pain education combined or pain education only. Participants were tested on the clinical tests at baseline and at 4-month follow-up. An anchor-based approach using Receiver Operator Characteristics (ROC) curves was used to evaluate responsiveness of the clinical tests. The Neck Disability Index was used to discriminate between those who had improved and those who were unchanged at the 4-month follow-up. Minimum Clinically Important Difference (MCID), together with sensitivity, specificity, positive and negative predictive values, in addition to positive and negative likelihood ratios were calculated. RESULTS: In total, 164 participants completed the 4 month follow up. One-hundred forty four participants were classified as unchanged whereas 20 patients were considered to be improved. Twenty-six participants didn't complete all of the clinical tests, leaving a total of 138 to be included for analyses. Area Under Curve (AUC) ranged from 0.50-0.62 for the clinical tests, and were all below an acceptable level. MCID was generally large, and the corresponding sensitivity and specificity was low with sensitivity ranging from 20 to 60%, and specificity from 54 to 86%. LR+ (0.8-2.07) and LR- (0.7-1.1) showed low diagnostic value for all variables, with PPV ranging from 12.1 to 26.1 and NPV ranging from 84.7 to 89.2. CONCLUSION: Responsiveness of the included clinical tests was generally low when using change in NDI score as the anchor from baseline to the 4-month follow up. Further investigations of responsiveness are warranted, possibly using other anchors, which to a higher degree resemble similar dimensions as the clinical tests.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jørgensen, René","Ris, Inge","Juhl, Carsten Bogh","Falla, Deborah","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit"],"cuid":["S02-097.96-048555"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georg-August-Universität Göttingen","University of Birmingham"],"keyword":["Journal Article","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCS"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"responsiveness of clinical tests for people with neck pain","src":["sdu","ucsyd"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-017-1918-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.96-048555","identifier":[{"id":"29282073","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040187407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5745670","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-104551c2-7e13-48cb-82d8-c3877e0a63ca","ucsyd-313dbbb0-1883-44de-8077-8927990d5007"],"keyword":["Journal Article","disease, health science and nursing","nakkesmerter, målemetoder"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DA5926E2F2CD35D3791E1277C6CE2F5C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","t