{"abstract":"The narrative structure and episodic richness of self-generated past and future events were examined in patients diagnosed with borderline personality disorder (BPD), eating disorder (ED), and obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD), respectively, and compared with a nonclinical control group. The 3 patient groups generated fewer events characterized by a classic narrative structure, with the event narrative building up to a high point followed by an evaluation. The narrative structures demonstrated by the BPD and ED groups were most deviant from the control group in terms of more frequently involving an impoverished narrative structure for past events and in terms of generating fewer future events with specific episodic contents. These deficits were more marked in the BPD group. The findings show that the ability to construct coherent past and future events is compromised across clinical diagnoses, but more so in patients diagnosed with BPD.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anne Scharling","Jørgensen, Carsten René","O'Connor, Maja","Bennedsen, Birgit","Godt, Kristine D.","Bøye, Rikke","Berntsen, Dorthe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-202039"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Borderline personality disorder","Identity disturbance","Narrative structure","Overgeneral memory"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the structure of past and future events in borderline personality disorder eating disorder and obsessive compulsive disorder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/120732640/The_structure_of_past_and_future_events_Accepted_manuscript_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-202039","identifier":[{"id":"85038834796","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7f10df7a-c2f5-40bf-8a96-20fe1ba57774"],"keyword":["Borderline personality disorder","Identity disturbance","Identity-related past and future events","Narrative structure","Overgeneral memory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C4F74E073906B7680C1A9A5597514930"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/120732640/The_structure_of_past_and_future_events_Accepted_manuscript_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - CON AMORE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Scharling","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"b7723e07-5e65-4a2d-a159-5b963d34e1b8","name":"Rasmussen, Anne Scharling","orcid":"0000-0002-7853-9271","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"oconnorpau","last":"O Connor","locid":"1173473f-f95b-473d-bc15-f8b8c026b6b9","name":"O'Connor, Maja","name_org":"O Connor, Maja","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-8633","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit","key":"bennedsenpau","last":"Bennedsen","locid":"89892e48-fc01-4f99-9c84-754de8c3c9dc","name":"Bennedsen, Birgit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine D.","key":"godtpau","last":"Godt","locid":"48696379-cf26-4c80-9c41-72d99689bf4c","name":"Godt, Kristine D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bøyepau","last":"Bøye","locid":"c816211a-6dc5-4594-ba92-a5d3aa050cde","name":"Bøye, Rikke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe","key":"berntsenpau","last":"Berntsen","locid":"2a5c3e80-973a-4b35-883d-a7de4143885c","name":"Berntsen, Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0001-5941-314X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1037/cns0000109","issn":["23265523","23265531"],"issn_org":["23265523"],"issue":"2","journal":"Psychology of Consciousness: Theory, Research, and Practice","pages":"190-210","publisher":"American Psychological Association","status":"p","title":"Psychology of Consciousness: Theory, Research, and Practice","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038834796"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7f10df7a-c2f5-40bf-8a96-20fe1ba57774"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The structure of past and future events in borderline personality disorder, eating disorder and obsessive compulsive disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-202039","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this report we use a validated model of the glucoregulatory system including effects of insulin and glucagon for simulation studies in seven type 1 diabetes patients. Using simulations, we replicate the results from a clinical study investigating the effect of micro-doses of glucagon on glucose metabolism at varying ambient insulin levels. The report compares in vivo and in silico results head-to-head, and discusses similarities and differences. We design and simulate simple studies to emphasize the implications of some glucoregulatory dynamics which are ignored in most previous clinical studies: the effect of discontinuing insulin and glucose infusions prior to glucagon administration, the delayed effect of insulin, timing of data sampling, and carryover effects from multiple subcutaneous doses of glucagon. We also use simulations to discuss two hypotheses of how insulin and glucagon might interact in influencing the glucose response. Following the simulations we propose a study design that potentially could explore if the hypotheses are true or false.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","Ranjan, Ajenthen","Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","Boye Knudsen, Carsten","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Madsen, Henrik","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Jørgensen, John Bagterp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-317515"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Glucagon","Glucose","Insulin","Simulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulating clinical studies of the glucoregulatory system i in vivo i meets i in silico i","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":