ology & Toxicology","pages":"322-330","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","title_org":"Basic and Clinical Pharmacology and Toxicology","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031093686"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9ee86e14-a38f-460b-a5e4-9d550ede1810"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Relationship between Optimum Mini-doses of Glucagon and Insulin Levels when Treating Mild Hypoglycaemia in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes - A Simulation Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351976","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB) induces weight loss and improves insulin sensitivity when evaluated by the hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp (HEC). Surrogate indices of insulin sensitivity calculated from insulin and glucose concentrations at fasting or after an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) are frequently used, but have not been validated after RYGB. Our aim was to evaluate whether surrogate indices reliably estimate changes in insulin sensitivity after RYGB. Four fasting (inverse-HOMA-IR, HOMA2-%S, QUICKI, revised-QUICKI) and three OGTT-derived surrogates (Matsuda, Gutt, OGIS) were compared with HEC-estimated peripheral insulin sensitivity (Rd or Rd/I, depending on how the index was originally validated) and the tracer-determined hepatic insulin sensitivity index (HISI) in patients with preoperative type 2 diabetes (n=10) and normal glucose tolerance (n=10) 1 week, 3 months and 1 year postoperatively. Post-RYGB changes in inverse-HOMA-IR and HOMA2-%S did not correlate with changes in Rd at any visit, but were comparable to changes in HISI at 1 week. Changes in QUICKI and revised-QUICKI correlated with Rd/I after surgery. Changes in Matsuda and Gutt did not correlate with changes in Rd/I and Rd, respectively, whereas OGIS-changes correlated with Rd-changes at 1 year post-RYGB. In conclusion, surrogate measures of insulin sensitivity may not reflect results obtained with gold standard methodology after RYGB, underscoring the importance of critical reflection when surrogate endpoints are used. Fasting surrogate indices may be particularly affected by post-RYGB changes in insulin clearance, whereas the validity of OGTT-derived surrogates may be compromised by the surgical rearrangements of the gut.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","Dirksen, Carsten","Svane, Maria Saur","Jørgensen, Nils B","Holst, Jens Juul","Richter, Erik A.","Madsbad, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-427978"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bariatric surgery","HOMA IR","Hepatic insulin sensitivity","Matsuda"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variable reliability of surrogate measures of insulin sensitivity after roux en y gastric bypass","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-427978","identifier":[{"id":"85019996039","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28202439","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3a03cbe4-1cee-4c0b-9b2b-ee05fab67fea"],"keyword":["Bariatric surgery","HOMA-IR","Hepatic insulin sensitivity","Matsuda","OGIS","Peripheral insulin sensitivity","QUICKI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EF3D14F9B57592E8A8323C9099044F4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Saur","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Maria Saur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik A.","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28202439"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpregu.00291.2016","issn":["03636119","15221490"],"issn_org":["03636119"],"issue":"5","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Regulatory, Integrative and Comparative Physiology","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Regulatory, Integrative and Comparative Physiology","volume":"312"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019996039"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3a03cbe4-1cee-4c0b-9b2b-ee05fab67fea"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Variable reliability of surrogate measures of insulin sensitivity after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-427978","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate normal human placental growth longitudinally throughout the second and third trimesters using MRI. METHODS: Twenty normal, first-time singleton pregnancies were scanned 7 times between the 14th and 38th week of gestation, at 4-week intervals, using MRI. Placental volumes were measured in both sagittal and transversal slices. All placentas were weighed after delivery to make a comparative study. RESULTS: Sixteen of the 20 women had increasing placental volumes from the 14th to 38th week of gestation. The 6th and 7th scan showed that 4 women had placentas of the same size. The mean placental volume increases linearly from the 14th till the 38th week of gestation, with a constant mean growth rate of 29.97 ml/week. The median placental volume extrapolated to delivery was to 856 ml (range 602-1,050 ml). The median weight of the exsanguinated placenta after delivery was 640 g (range 500-787 g). All pregnancies were carried to term, resulting in the delivery of healthy infants with good correlation between placental size and birth weight (R = 0.56, p = 0.009). CONCLUSION: Placental growth was measured systematically in a longitudinal study through the second and third trimesters using MRI. MRI provides a safe and feasible method to measure placental growth. The mean placental growth was linear throughout the second and third trimesters.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Langhoff, Lasse","Grønbeck, Lene","von Huth, Sebastian","Axelsson, Anna","Jørgensen, Connie","Thomsen, Carsten","Vejlstrup, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527242"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"placental growth during normal pregnancy a magnetic resonance imaging study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527242","identifier":[{"id":"85006257595","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27960180","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dff4869a-b1f1-43c6-9bdb-6ae3558f7df0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5C0ED61D6D8E63955CC70142951AD25C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lasse","key":"langhoffpau","last":"Langhoff","name":"Langhoff, Lasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"grønbeckpau","last":"Grønbeck","name":"Grønbeck, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian","key":"vonhuthpau","last":"von Huth","name":"von Huth, Sebastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"axelssonpau","last":"Axelsson","name":"Axelsson, Anna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Connie","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Connie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"3df25ea7-9eb3-4b95-9aca-5171b7d5870f","name":"Thomsen, Carsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27960180"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000452661","issn":["03787346","1423002X"],"issn_org":["03787346"],"issue":"5","journal":"Gynecologic and Obstetric Investigation","pages":"462-467","status":"p","title":"Gynecologic and Obstetric Investigation","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006257595"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dff4869a-b1f1-43c6-9bdb-6ae3558f7df0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Placental Growth during Normal Pregnancy - A Magnetic Resonance Imaging Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527242","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
