{"abstract":"The ability to fabricate nanoscale domains of uniform size in two-dimensional materials could potentially enable new applications in nanoelectronics and the development of innovative metamaterials. However, achieving even minimal control over the growth of two-dimensional lateral heterostructures at such extreme dimensions has proven exceptionally challenging. Here we show the spontaneous formation of ordered arrays of graphene nano-domains (dots), epitaxially embedded in a two-dimensional boron-carbon-nitrogen alloy. These dots exhibit a strikingly uniform size of 1.6 ± 0.2 nm and strong ordering, and the array periodicity can be tuned by adjusting the growth conditions. We explain this behaviour with a model incorporating dot-boundary energy, a moiré-modulated substrate interaction and a long-range repulsion between dots. This new two-dimensional material, which theory predicts to be an ordered composite of uniform-size semiconducting graphene quantum dots laterally integrated within a larger-bandgap matrix, holds promise for novel electronic and optoelectronic properties, with a variety of potential device applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Camilli, Luca","Jørgensen, Jakob Holm","Tersoff, Jerry","Stoot, Adam C.","Balog, Richard","Cassidy, Andrew","Sadowski, Jerzy T.","Boggild, Peter","Hornekær, Liv"],"cuid":["S02-092.63-014829"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Camilli, Luca"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brookhaven National Laboratory","IBM Research","Pacific Northwest National Laboratory"],"keyword":["ATOMIC LAYERS","Carbon","GROWTH","Heterostructures","Hexagonal boron nitride","IR 111","Interface","Nitrogen","Transition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self assembly of ordered graphene nanodot arrays","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00042-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.63-014829","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5491516","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000404333000006","type":"wos"},{"id":"28663540","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85021642592","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1ebe9fec-9ab6-446c-a5ed-cf798727ab6c","dtu-ced9865a-dfa9-4cd8-ad49-f07aa0e1d9c9"],"keyword":["ATOMIC LAYERS","B-C-N","CARBON","GROWTH","HETEROSTRUCTURES","HEXAGONAL BORON-NITRIDE","INTERFACE","IR(111)","NITROGEN","TRANSITION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C3519A038D8FD2B8D2B8FF8DCC687198"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00042-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/133702887/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/191032111/2017_Camilli_NatureComm_8_47.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Nanocarbon"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus u