{"abstract":"Common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) is a heterogeneous primary immunodeficiency disease, leading to recurrent bacterial airway infections and often also autoimmune complications. To shed light on the regulatory lymphocytes from these patients, we analyzed the levels of regulatory B (pro-B10) cell and regulatory T (Treg) cell subpopulations in PBMCs from twenty-six patients diagnosed with CVID using multi-color flowcytometry. Pro-B10 cells were induced by 48h in vitro stimulation prior to analysis. Suppressor function was measured on a subset of patients with splenomegaly and autoimmune complications. The levels of regulatory B and T cells were correlated to clinical manifestations, including autoimmunity, splenomegaly and CVID EUROclass subgroups. We demonstrate a significant association between elevated levels of pro-B10 cells, decreased levels of Tregs and autoimmune phenomena in CVID patients. The finding of marked abnormalities in regulatory lymphocyte populations contribute to our understanding of the pathogenesis of CVID and potentially be valuable in the clinical management and treatment of patients.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kofod-Olsen, Emil","Jørgensen, Sofie Eg","Nissen, Sara Konstantin","Westh, Lena","Møller, Bjarne K.","Østergaard, Lars","Larsen, Carsten S.","Mogensen, Trine H."],"cuid":["S02-095.65-006584"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["International Center for Immunodeficiency Diseases"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altered fraction of regulatory b and t cells is correlated with autoimmune phenomena and splenomegaly in patients with cvid","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84947602571","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.65-006584","identifier":[{"id":"000368970000007","type":"wos"},{"id":"84947602571","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26586095","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8839d086-da55-4337-9850-295ba95134fe","au-b1ce4edd-3046-4b03-b50f-25f9ec35e061"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E72ACFD6B204E66CFEB4E028F1F263A1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory of Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["International Center for Immunodeficiency Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"