{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Carsten René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238978"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eu undergraver tryghed og identitet","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.information.dk/debat/2016/07/eu-undergraver-tryghed-identitet","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-238978","ids":["au-c021bc58-a2a6-4f1d-bad7-53109b5d389a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-78BADD3E12A16674985ED92E939F7299"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3763a4db-6ce1-4e54-ac67-524a9604e1ce","name":"Jørgensen, Carsten René","orcid":"0000-0002-7324-1628","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16022572"],"newspaper":"Information","pages":"14-15","publisher":"Dagbladet Information","status":"p","title":"Information","title_org":"Dagbladet Information","volume":"Section 1, Debat"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c021bc58-a2a6-4f1d-bad7-53109b5d389a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"EU undergraver tryghed og identitet","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-238978","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objective We aim to develop a simulation model of the complex glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics based on physiology and data. Furthermore, we compare pharmacokinetic (PK) and pharmacodynamic (PD) characteristics of marketed reconstituted glucagon with a stable liquid glucagon analogue invented by Zealand Pharma A/S. Research Design and Methods We expanded a physiological model of endogenous glucose production with multiplicative effects of insulin and glucagon and combined it with the Hovorka glucoregulatory model. We used a Bayesian framework to perform multidimensional MAP estimation of model parameters given priors reported in the literature. We used profile likelihood analysis to investigate parameter identifiability and reduce the number of model variables. We estimated model parameters in pre-clinical data from one cross-over study with a total of 20 experiments in five dogs. The dogs received two subcutaneous (SC) bolus injections of low and high doses of glucagon and ZP-GA-1 (20 and 120 nmol/kg). Results We report posterior probability distributions and correlations for all identifiable model parameters. Based on visual inspection and residual analysis, the PD model described data satisfactorily for both glucagon and the analogue. Parameter estimates of the PD model were not significantly different between the two compounds. Conclusions The new PK/PD model enables simulations of the glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics after a SC bolus of glucagon or glucagon analogue. The novel glucagon analogue by Zealand Pharma A/S shows PK and PD characteristics similar to marketed glucagon.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","Boye Knudsen, Carsten","Madsen, Henrik","Haidar, Ahmad","Jørgensen, John Bagterp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-322651"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","McGill University"],"keyword":["Glucagon","Glucose","Insulin","MAP","Modeling","Modelling","PD","PK","Pharmacodynamics","Pharmacokinetics","Profile likelihood","Simulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pk pd modelling of glucose insulin glucagon dynamics in healthy dogs after a subcutaneous bolus administration of native glucagon or a novel glucagon analogue","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123443377/tr16_02_Wendt_SL.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-322651","ids":["dtu-3cb81b95-2819-46b6-a471-967dc98ece34"],"keyword":["Glucagon","Glucagon analogue","Glucoregulatory","Glucose","Insulin","MAP","Modeling","Modelling","ODE","PD","PK","Pharmacodynamics","Pharmacokinetics","Profile likelihood","SDE","Simulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3D6D697E8D522E4509DD0269C0F526C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123443377/tr16_02_Wendt_SL.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Scientific Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"zealand pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ZEA","l3nl":"Zealand Pharma A/S","l3nn":"Zealand Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Zealand Pharma","namevar":["Zealand Pharma A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sabrina Lyngbye","key":"wendtpau","last":"Wendt","locid":"053fcca6-8b59-439b-ad9a-4abe1507ae4f","name":"Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","orcid":"0000-0002-1520-0254","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Kloppenborg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"06a667bd-2e4d-493d-ada6-191296446a2e","name":"Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","orcid":"0000-0002-6100-043X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"boyeknudsenpau","last":"Boye Knudsen","name":"Boye Knudsen, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad","key":"haidarpau","last":"Haidar","name":"Haidar, Ahmad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d2bc6de4-a5c6-43f7-8712-606bd02a88e9","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","orcid":"0000-0001-9799-2808","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16012321"],"issue":"2","pages":"54","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","repno":"DTU Compute Technical Report-2016, No. 2","series":"DTU Compute Technical Report","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3cb81b95-2819-46b6-a471-967dc98ece34"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"PK/PD modelling of glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics in healthy dogs after a subcutaneous bolus administration of native glucagon or a novel glucagon analogue","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-322651","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In healthy individuals, insulin and glucagon work in a complex fashion to maintain blood glucose levels within a narrow range. This regulation is distorted in patients with diabetes. The hepatic glucose response due to an elevated glucagon level depends on the current insulin concentration and thus endogenous glucose production (EGP) can not be modelled without knowledge of the concentration of both hormones in plasma. Furthermore, literature suggests an upper limit to EGP irrespective of glucagon levels. We build a simulation model of the glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics in man including saturation effect of EGP. Ten healthy subjects received a 1 mg subcutaneous (SC) glucagon bolus (GlucaGen®). Plasma samples were collected until 300 minutes post dose and analyzed for glucagon, insulin, and glucose concentrations. All observations were used to fit a physiological model of the glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics using the Hovorka model with a novel multiplicative description of the effects of insulin and of glucagon on EGP. Bayesian estimation by Maximum a Posteriori using prior knowledge reported in literature was used to estimate the model parameters for each subject. Profile likelihood plots were used to investigate parameter identifiability. Unidentifiable parameters were fixed at their prior mean values. The new model enables simulations of the glucose-insulin-glucagon dynamics in humans at both low and high glucagon concentrations (180-8000 pg/mL) and physiologic insulin concentrations (1.2-81.9 mIU/L). The model can be used for simulation of glucagon bolus strategies for treatment of hypoglycemia and for in silico simulation of dual-hormone artificial pancreas algorithms.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","Haidar, Ahmad","Bysted, Britta Væver","Knudsen, Carsten Boye","Madsen, Henrik","Jørgensen, John Bagterp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360707"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-14","place":"New Orleans, Louisiana, us","start":"2016-06-10","title":"The American Diabetes Association's 76th Scientific Sessions (ADA 2016)","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","McGill University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model of the glucose insulin glucagon dynamics after subcutaneous administration of a glucagon rescue bolus in healthy humans","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124207434/abstract_ada16_slw_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360707","ids":["dtu-bbce4766-5453-4bc7-ae9c-23cc75e80d91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-39AF918326F08ADF53007933CABF0D05"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124207434/abstract_ada16_slw_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Scientific Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"zealand pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ZEA","l3nl":"Zealand Pharma A/S","l3nn":"Zealand Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Zealand Pharma","namevar":["Zealand Pharma A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sabrina Lyngbye","key":"wendtpau","last":"Wendt","locid":"053fcca6-8b59-439b-ad9a-4abe1507ae4f","name":"Wendt, Sabrina Lyngbye","orcid":"0000-0002-1520-0254","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Kloppenborg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"06a667bd-2e4d-493d-ada6-191296446a2e","name":"Møller, Jan Kloppenborg","orcid":"0000-0002-6100-043X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad","key":"haidarpau","last":"Haidar","name":"Haidar, Ahmad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Britta Væver","key":"bystedpau","last":"Bysted","name":"Bysted, Britta Væver","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Boye","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Carsten Boye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"458e950b-adfd-4f2d-8d0d-ef39dee24bea","name":"Madsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0690-3713","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d2bc6de4-a5c6-43f7-8712-606bd02a88e9","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","orcid":"0000-0001-9799-2808","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bbce4766-5453-4bc7-ae9c-23cc75e80d91"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Model of the Glucose-Insulin-Glucagon Dynamics after Subcutaneous Administration of a Glucagon Rescue Bolus in Healthy Humans","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360707","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Exaggerated secretion of glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) is important for postprandial glucose tolerance after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB), whereas the role of glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) remains to be resolved. We aimed to explore the relative importance of endogenously secreted GLP-1 and GIP on glucose tolerance and beta-cell function after RYGB. We used DPP-4 inhibition to enhance concentrations of intact GIP and GLP-1 and the GLP-1 receptor antagonist exendin 9-39 (Ex-9) for specific blockage of GLP-1 actions. Twelve glucose tolerant patients were studied after RYGB in a randomized, placebo-controlled, four-day, cross-over study with standard mixed meal tests and concurrent administration of: placebo, oral sitagliptin, Ex-9 infusion or combined Ex-9/sitagliptin. GLP-1 receptor antagonism increased glucose excursions, clearly attenuated beta-cell function and aggravated postprandial hyperglucagonaemia compared with placebo, whereas sitagliptin had no effect despite 2-3-fold increased concentrations of intact GLP-1 and GIP. Similarly, sitagliptin did not affect glucose tolerance or beta-cell function during GLP-1R blockage. This study confirms the importance of GLP-1 for glucose tolerance after RYGB via increased insulin and attenuated glucagon secretion in the postprandial state, whereas amplification of the GIP signal (or other DPP-4 sensitive glucose lowering mechanisms) did not appear to contribute to the improved glucose tolerance seen after RYGB.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Svane, Maria S.","Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N","Nielsen, Signe Ledou","Jørgensen, Nils B","Dirksen, Carsten","Bendtsen, Flemming","Kristiansen, Viggo B","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535813"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of endogenous glp 000000000001 and gip on glucose tolerance after roux en y gastric bypass surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-535813","identifier":[{"id":"84983028408","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26786780","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ee872285-6791-4449-a37a-1f163b723fc5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9657A39BD8ADDF95AC9D3461EFA18CFE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria S","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"4cc109fb-b416-4327-a1bd-c980486fa717","name":"Svane, Maria S.","name_org":"Svane, Maria S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmollerpau","last":"Bojsen-Moller","name":"Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"48a7d837-0860-4ccc-9fc3-0bd30339bfe6","name":"Nielsen, Signe Ledou","name_org":"Nielsen, Signe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nils B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"bendtsenpau","last":"Bendtsen","locid":"18608d49-a3d5-4de9-8053-3edef5ba12f9","name":"Bendtsen, Flemming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viggo B","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Viggo B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26786780"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpendo.00471.2015","issn":["01931849","15221555"],"issn_org":["01931849"],"issue":"7","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"310"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983028408"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee872285-6791-4449-a37a-1f163b723fc5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of endogenous GLP-1 and GIP on glucose tolerance after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535813","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Hvordan har de danske unge det? Og hvad ved vi om dem? Svarene på disse spørgsmål – og meget mere – kan du finde i dette temanummer om unge. Vi har valgt at sætte fokus på en række problemstillinger i temanummeret: De unges overgang fra skole til uddannelse og betydningen af dette; deres erfaringer med seksuelle relationer og forventninger til familie og fremtid; deres kendskab til alkohol og hash og betydningen af dette – og selvfølgelig stiller vi skarpt på de af dem, der er særligt udsatte. Meget af materialet i temahæftet stammer fra SFI’s Forløbsundersøgelse af børn født i 1995. Det er en unik undersøgelse, fordi vi har fulgt de samme 6.000 børn og deres familier siden 1995, med seneste dataindsamling i 18-årsalderen. Deltagerne kommer fra hele landet og fra alle sociale lag. Den viden, vi får ved at følge de samme børn og deres familier over tid, er ganske speciel, fordi forløbsundersøgelsen kan vise, hvordan forhold i barndommen og under opvæksten påvirker deltagerne som unge – og senere som voksne. Vi får altså information om nogle af de betingelser, der har betydning for en god opvækst – og en dårlig! Det vil kunne bidrage til at styrke både udviklingen af de relevante faglige indsatser og vores videre forskning. Det giver ny viden til fx kommunale beslutningstagere og praktikere, når vi endnu mere præcist kan udpege de særligt sårbare grupper. Det gælder fx de unge, der har vedvarende symptomer på depression, idet denne gruppe af unge er ekstremt udsat og mange har allerede i teenagealderen selvmordsforsøg bag sig. Og det giver viden til beslutningstagerne i Folketinget, når undersøgelsens data peger på, at en stor andel af frafaldet på ungdomsskolerne ikke alene skyldes forhold på selve uddannelsen, men i høj grad også er knyttet til den unges opvækst og familiebaggrund. For det betyder jo, at det ikke er tilstrækkeligt at ændre på uddannelserne – vi er også nødt til at forholde os til, hvad der sker tidligere i skolen og i familien, hvis vi ønsker at give børn og unge lige muligheder for uddannelse og øge den sociale mobilitet. Er vi så færdige nu med at kigge på ’95-årgangen? Nej – faktisk ikke. Lige som fx det engelske National Child Development Study, som blev påbegyndt med årgang 1958, er vores ambition at føre Forløbsundersøgelsen af årgang ’95 videre, så vi kan få mere viden om det tidlige voksenliv, og senere hen familiedannelsen. Hvem ender med at få videregående uddannelser og hvorfor? Hvilke faktorer i det tidlige børneliv bidrager til et dårligt helbred i voksenlivet – og hvordan kan vi imødegå det fremover? Hvem får et nogenlunde stabilt forhold til arbejdsmarkedet, og hvad er med til at fremme det? Kan vi tidligt spotte dem, der kommer til at leve af overførselsindkomst? Hvad betyder en opvækst med økonomisk fattigdom og materielle afsavn på lang sigt? Hvem nøjedes med at feste igennem med både røg og alkohol i ungdommen – og hvem tog alt for mange rusmidler med sig ind i vokselivet? Både beslutningstagere, praktikere og mange forskere i Danmark og internationalt har stor glæde af disse data fra Forløbsundersøgelsen af årgang ’95. Og alle har adgang til resultaterne. Alt hvad SFI publicerer ligger således offentligt tilgængeligs på vores hjemmeside sfi.dk.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Trine","Wulff, Carsten","Underbjerg, Anne Marie","Høg, Mads Andersen","Haahr, Ulla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-663028"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social forskning 000000002016 000000000001 portræt unge i danmark","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/492074/SF_2016_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-663028","ids":["vive-40c04a0b-caeb-4398-bfdb-14d9474b1e08"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1405D58EE6A92C6B6443287B317F642E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/492074/SF_2016_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Ledelsessekretariat"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"4b417f79-c334-4856-8b9f-711c8d0a15cb","name":"Jørgensen, Trine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"wulffpau","last":"Wulff","locid":"cd62074e-697c-4c07-b82c-af85d394b325","name":"Wulff, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Marie","key":"underbjergpau","last":"Underbjerg","locid":"e69c5d62-028e-4c93-8551-0e7d856ca8a3","name":"Underbjerg, Anne Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Andersen","key":"høgpau","last":"Høg","locid":"d4447e99-9e72-4c23-acab-8da444b90914","name":"Høg, Mads Andersen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla","key":"haahrpau","last":"Haahr","locid":"a993b36f-8f5b-4e05-a59c-a2bd3308b013","name":"Haahr, Ulla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09037537"],"issue":"2016:1","journal":"Social Forskning.","publisher":"SFI - Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Velfærd","status":"p","title":"Social Forskning.","title_org":"social forskning"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-40c04a0b-caeb-4398-bfdb-14d9474b1e08"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Social Forskning 2016:1 : Portræt: Unge i danmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-663028","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objective Functional gastrointestinal (GI) symptoms can develop into persistent states often categorised as the irritable bowel syndrome (IBS). In the severe end of the GI symptom continuum, other coexisting symptoms are common. We aimed to investigate the GI symptom continuum in relation to mortality and development of GI diseases, and to examine if coexisting symptoms had an influence on the outcomes. Material and methods A longitudinal population-based study comprising two 5-year follow-up studies: Dan-Monica1 (1982-1987) and Inter99 (1999-2004). IBS was defined according to a population-based IBS definition. The pooled cohort (n = 7278) was followed until December 2013 in Central Registries. Results Fifty-one percent had no GI symptoms, 39% had GI symptoms but never fulfilled the IBS definition, 8% had fluctuating IBS and 2% had persisting IBS. There was no significant association between symptom groups and mortality (p = 0.47). IBS and GI symptoms with abdominal pain were significantly associated with development of GI diseases. Only GI symptoms with abdominal pain were associated with development of severe GI diseases (HR: 1.38; 95% CI: [1.06-1.79]). There were no statistically significant interactions between symptom groups and coexisting symptoms in relation to the two outcomes. Conclusions GI diseases were seen more frequently, but IBS was not associated with severe GI diseases or increased mortality. Clinicians should be more aware when patients do not fulfil the IBS definition, but continue to report frequent abdominal pain. Coexisting symptoms did not influence mortality and development of GI diseases.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Heinsvig Poulsen, Chalotte","Falgaard Eplov, Lene","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Eliasen, Marie","Frost Ebstrup, Jeanette","Skovbjerg, Sine","Schröder, Andreas","Jørgensen, Torben"],"cuid":["S03-092.00-009391"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Gastrointestinal Diseases","Irritable bowel syndrome","Mortality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gastrointestinal symptoms related to the irritable bowel syndrome a longitudinal population based register study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84955194770","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-092.00-009391","identifier":[{"id":"26635123","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000368696900005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84955194770","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c335f4c4-2b0d-407d-bf21-e2721fc26178","au-c959457c-7c2f-4681-81ef-d7d1dc39b5c8","ku-33f01fc5-aa87-48be-9f70-b402f48beda9"],"keyword":["Gastrointestinal diseases","irritable bowel syndrome","mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D2C909F1B14853095AF6F05D8A81102E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Chalotte","key":"heinsvigpoulsenpau","last":"Heinsvig Poulsen","name":"Heinsvig Poulsen, Chalotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chalotte Heinsvig","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Chalotte Heinsvig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"falgaardeplovpau","last":"Falgaard Eplov","name":"Falgaard Eplov, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthojpau","last":"Hjorthoj","locid":"d4b636e3-7c21-48a0-b812-de219ca78a9e","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","name_org":"Hjorthoj, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthøjpau","last":"Hjorthøj","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"eliasenpau","last":"Eliasen","name":"Eliasen, Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"frostebstruppau","last":"Frost Ebstrup","name":"Frost Ebstrup, Jeanette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeanette Frost","key":"ebstruppau","last":"Ebstrup","name":"Ebstrup, Jeanette Frost","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine","key":"skovbjergpau","last":"Skovbjerg","name":"Skovbjerg, Sine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","locid":"200c6dd9-43cd-41da-8c27-ce8adb073e24","name":"Schröder, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"schroderpau","last":"Schroder","name":"Schroder, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"a5d9b7f4-413e-465f-a6f2-1f53e2b34186","name":"Jørgensen, Torben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26635123"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365521.2015.1117652","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00365521"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"420-426","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84955194770"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c335f4c4-2b0d-407d-bf21-e2721fc26178","au-c959457c-7c2f-4681-81ef-d7d1dc39b5c8","ku-33f01fc5-aa87-48be-9f70-b402f48beda9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gastrointestinal symptoms related to the irritable bowel syndrome : a longitudinal population-based register study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.00-009391","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The project aims to develop the next generation of energy cost-efficient artificial lighting control that enables greenhouse growers to adapt their use of artificial lighting dynamically to fluctuations in the price of electricity. This is a necessity as fluctuations in the price of electricity can be so large that it directly affects the production costs. The project results show that the newly developed lighting control software, DynaLight NG, allows greenhouse growers to adapt their use of artificial lighting to market variations in electricity prices without negative impacts on plant quality or production time. The electricity savings that DynaLight NG can achieve depends on the installed lamp type. When used together with conventional SON-T lamps DynaLight NG can achieve an electricity savings of 25% compared to traditional artificial lighting control. The project results also show that shifting from SON-T to LED lamps can result in a further reduction of 50% reduction in electricity consumption.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Bo Nørregaard","Ottosen, Carl-Otto","Dam-Hansen, Carsten","Rosenqvist, Eva","Pedersen, Ivan Kristian","Sørensen, Jan Corfixen","Kjær, Katrine Heinsvig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353659"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynalight next generation smart grid ready energy efficient lighting system for green house horticulture","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128123505/EUDP_FinalReport_SmartGridReady.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353659","ids":["dtu-a470316f-35fc-4f3a-91ba-17ddf80e8b28"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C1A046F4CFF8DC839E9CE14ACA27CEC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128123505/EUDP_FinalReport_SmartGridReady.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Diode Lasers and LED Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["Ørsted A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo Nørregaard","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Bo Nørregaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl-Otto","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","name":"Ottosen, Carl-Otto","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"damhansenpau","last":"Dam-Hansen","locid":"9560dc41-73f3-41fd-aa1d-cbf953325027","name":"Dam-Hansen, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-7518-4025","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rosenqvistpau","last":"Rosenqvist","name":"Rosenqvist, Eva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan Kristian","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ivan Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Corfixen","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jan Corfixen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Heinsvig","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Katrine Heinsvig","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"59","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a470316f-35fc-4f3a-91ba-17ddf80e8b28"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynalight Next Generation : Smart Grid Ready Energy Efficient Lighting System for Green House Horticulture.","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353659","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Maternal vitamin D deficiency is proposed as a risk factor for preeclampsia in humans. We tested the hypothesis that vitamin D depletion aggravates and high supplementation ameliorates the preeclampsia phenotype in an established transgenic rat model of human renin-angiotensin system-mediated preeclampsia. Adult rat dams, transgenic for human angiotensinogen (hAGT) and mated with male rats transgenic for human renin (hREN), were fed either vitamin D-depleted chow (VDd) or enriched chow (VDh) 2 weeks before mating and during pregnancy. Mean blood pressure was recorded by tail-cuff, and 24-hour urine samples were collected in metabolic cages at days 6 and 18 of gestation. Rats were sacrificed at day 21 of gestation. Depleted dams (VDd) had negligible serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D2+3 levels (mean ± SEM; 2.95 ± 0.45 nmol/l vs. VDh 26.20 ± 2.88 nmol/l, P = .01), but in both groups, levels of 1,25(OH)2D3 remained below detection level of 25 pmol/l. Dietary vitamin D depletion did not aggravate hypertension (mean ± SEM BP, day 20 of gestation: 151.38 ± 5.65 mmHg VDd vs. 152.00 ± 4.10 mmHg VDh) or proteinuria. Fetal anthropometrics were similar between the groups, whereas VDd displayed lower placental:fetal weight ratios (0.15 vs. 0.16 g/g, P = .01) and increased sFlt-1/PlGF ratio. Expression of hREN was lower in placenta of VDd dams (0.82 ± 0.44 AU vs. 1.52 ± 0.15 AU, P = .04). Expression of key vitamin D metabolizing enzymes was unchanged. Dietary vitamin D intervention did not alter key aspects of the preeclampsia phenotype using the transgenic rodent model of human renin-angiotensin system-mediated pre-eclampsia, plausibly due to altered vitamin D metabolism or excretion in the transgenic rats.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Andersen, Louise Bjørkholt","Golic, Michaela","Przybyl, Lukasz","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Jørgensen, Jan Stener","Fruekilde, Palle Bach Nielsen","von Versen-Höynck, Frauke","Herse, Florian","Højskov, Carsten Schriver","Dechend, Ralf","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Haase, Nadine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Berlin Institute of Health","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","HELIOS Klinikum Berlin","Hannover Medical School","Max-Delbrück-Center for Molecular Medicine (MDC), Berlin-Buch, Germany, Germany."],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vitamin d depletion does not affect key aspects of the preeclamptic phenotype in a transgenic rodent model for preeclampsia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84991225582","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606227","identifier":[{"id":"84991225582","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27450577","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-736432a6-7d92-4dcc-8237-89cea769e6c2"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7A55F8FCEEA2AC5C9DDA953C8543A32"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"charité university m