{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Riis, Marianne","Bergstedt, Palle","Rasmussen, Carsten Lund","Jørgensen, Claus Bo","Koch, Hans Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-081.82-039380"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-13","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2015-06-11","title":"Nordyrk konferencen 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Informations og kommunikationsteknologi og e læring","Læring pædagogik og undervisning"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ikt som transfermedierende værktøj mellem forskellige kontekster fokus på grænsekrydsninger mellem skole og praktik","src":["kp","pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-081.82-039380","ids":["kp-c2da0ea9-0367-40b9-a7e9-f557e1454019","pha-e6b9d449-8dc5-4832-ac14-a9a48dadade5"],"keyword":["Informations- og kommunikationsteknologi, og e-læring","Læring, pædagogik og undervisning"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-511EC2B305225C157711AA0112A73468"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Nationalt center for Erhvervspædagogik, Nationalt center for Erhvervspædagogik"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Absalon - Forskningsprogram for Digital teknologi, læring og design","Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Center for Skole og Læring - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"bf6f17db-5187-481d-af30-839922786263","name":"Riis, Marianne","orcid":"0009-0005-2181-8148","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Palle","key":"bergstedtpau","last":"Bergstedt","locid":"39917d20-a3b9-4b83-8e82-df4f165e2a1d","name":"Bergstedt, Palle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"d0364b63-ec70-4a5b-882f-80ae68506ea0","name":"Rasmussen, Carsten Lund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Bo","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7f3e7e6c-a79a-4412-8f3c-72804b4d1017","name":"Jørgensen, Claus Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Henrik","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","locid":"8c4294fe-9e1c-4868-bc6d-d466413b5617","name":"Koch, Hans Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-c2da0ea9-0367-40b9-a7e9-f557e1454019","pha-e6b9d449-8dc5-4832-ac14-a9a48dadade5"],"src":["AB University College Absalon","KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Ikt som transfermedierende værktøj mellem forskellige kontekster : fokus på grænsekrydsninger mellem skole og praktik","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.82-039380","year":"2015","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Exposure to perfluorinated alkylate substances (PFASs) is associated with immune suppression in animal models, and serum concentrations of specific antibodies against certain childhood vaccines tend to decrease at higher exposures. As such, we investigated the immunotoxic impacts of the three major PFASs in a Faroese birth cohort. METHODS: A total of 464 children contributed blood samples collected at age 7 years. PFAS concentrations and concentrations of antibodies against diphtheria and tetanus were assessed in serum at age 7 years, and results were available from samples collected at age 5. In addition to standard regressions, structural equation models were generated to determine the association between three major PFASs measured at the two points in time and the two antibody concentrations. RESULTS: Concentrations of all three 7-year PFAS concentrations were individually associated with a decrease in concentrations of antibodies, however, it was not possible to attribute causality to any single PFAS concentration. Hence, the three 7-year concentrations were combined and showed that a 2-fold increase in PFAS was associated with a decrease by 54.4 % (95 % CI: 22.0 %, 73.3 %) in the antibody concentration. If considering both the age-5 and age-7 concentrations of the three major PFASs, the exposure showed a slightly greater loss. CONCLUSIONS: These analyses strengthen the evidence of human PFAS immunotoxicity at current exposure levels and reflect the usefulness of structural equation models to adjust for imprecision in the exposure variables.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mogensen, Ulla Brasch","Grandjean, Philippe","Heilmann, Carsten","Nielsen, Flemming","Weihe, Pal","Budtz-Jørgensen, Esben"],"cuid":["S02-088.80-042630"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"country":["Faroe Islands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Faroese Hospital System"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural equation modeling of immunotoxicity associated with exposure to sperfluorinated alkylates","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12940-015-0032-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.80-042630","identifier":[{"id":"84933512586","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26041029","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4488050","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-58cecfae-9d7d-472a-b086-b92246a5ed92","sdu-c85a1634-7132-4f9f-ad36-8c3da0bf460c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B43F9BE2FB3BFC17E38093733BF64523"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129611978/Structural_equation_modeling_of_immunotoxicity_associated_with_exposure_to_perfluorinated_alkylates.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12940-015-0032-9","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fo","key":"faroese hospital system","loc":["Faroe Islands","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"name":"Faroese Hospital System","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ulla B","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"7db8dc3f-3821-4155-b8f4-7df37d15b892","name":"Mogensen, Ulla Brasch","name_org":"Mogensen, Ulla B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Philippe","key":"grandjeanpau","last":"Grandjean","locid":"6fe207c8-8ce6-41b9-8503-bc15b6cf3ea1","name":"Grandjean, Philippe","orcid":"0000-0003-4046-9658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"heilmannpau","last":"Heilmann","name":"Heilmann, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a3417ee2-84f4-4f19-ab48-919e04e98666","name":"Nielsen, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0002-5657-405X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pál","key":"weihepau","last":"Weihe","name":"Weihe, Pál","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esben","key":"budtzjørgensenpau","last":"Budtz-Jørgensen","locid":"c4ebc45c-df67-437e-a5e9-bdaa629d7caa","name":"Budtz-Jørgensen, Esben","orcid":"0000-0002-5551-0724","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26041029"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12940-015-0032-9","issn":["1476069X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Environmental Health","paperid":"47","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84933512586"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-58cecfae-9d7d-472a-b086-b92246a5ed92","sdu-c85a1634-7132-4f9f-ad36-8c3da0bf460c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Structural equation modeling of immunotoxicity associated with exposure to sperfluorinated alkylates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.80-042630","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Context: Bile acids and fibroblast growth factor 19 (FGF19) have been suggested as key mediators of the improvements in glucose metabolism after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB). Objective: To describe fasting and postprandial state total bile acid (TBA) and FGF19 concentrations before and after RYGB and relate them to parameters of glucose metabolism, glucagon-like peptide-1, cholecystokinin, and cholesterol fractions. Design and Setting: A prospective descriptive study was performed at the Department of Endocrinology, Hvidovre Hospital, Hvidovre, Denmark. Patients: Thirteen type 2 diabetic (T2D) patients and 12 normal glucose tolerant (NGT) subjects participated in the study. Intervention: A 4-hour liquid meal test was performed before and 1 week, 3 months, and 1 year after RYGB. Main Outcome Measures: We measured fasting and postprandial TBA and FGF19 concentrations. Results: Fasting TBA concentrations decreased in NGT subjects (P < .001) and were unchanged in T2D patients 1 week after surgery, but then increased gradually in both groups with time from surgery (ANOVA Ptime < .001). Area under the curve (AUC) TBA was decreased in NGT subjects 1 week after RYGB (before surgery, 567 mmol * min/L [interquartile range, 481–826]; 1 wk, 419 [381–508]; P = .009) and was unchanged in T2D patients (894 [573–1002]; 695 [349–1147]; P = .97) but then increased with time from surgery in both groups (Ptime < .001). Fasting FGF19 concentrations were unchanged acutely after RYGB (NGT, 140 pg/mL [100–162], 134 [119–204], P = .42; T2D, 162 [130–196], 154 [104–164], P = .68) and remained unchanged throughout the follow-up period. AUC FGF19 increased gradually with time after surgery (Ptime < .001), resembling the changes seen with AUC TBA. One week after RYGB, glucose metabolism improved, low-density lipoprotein-cholesterol and high-density lipoprotein-cholesterol decreased, and cholecystokinin and glucagon-like peptide-1 secretion increased, whereas FFA concentrations were unchanged. Conclusion: TBA and FGF19 do not explain acute changes in glucose metabolism, cholesterol fractions, and gut hormone secretion after RYGB.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Nils B","Dirksen, Carsten","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","Kristiansen, Viggo B","Wulff, Birgitte S","Rainteau, Dominique","Humbert, Lydie","Rehfeld, Jens F.","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Clausen, Trine R"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417241"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improvements in glucose metabolism early after gastric bypass surgery are not explained by increases in total bile acids and fibroblast growth factor 000000000019 concentrations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-417241","identifier":[{"id":"25536209","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84924985110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-27c8d46f-d339-4abd-b879-bde9779b2a61"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C9164D2AF9785C9E9087005D6720A24"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Teaching"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nils B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"694893d0-af33-4f21-ad66-945a1522de37","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viggo B","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Viggo B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte S","key":"wulffpau","last":"Wulff","name":"Wulff, Birgitte S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dominique","key":"rainteaupau","last":"Rainteau","name":"Rainteau, Dominique","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lydie","key":"humbertpau","last":"Humbert","name":"Humbert, Lydie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens F","key":"rehfeldpau","last":"Rehfeld","locid":"eaf0b29a-7fae-4c52-947e-9324996a4830","name":"Rehfeld, Jens F.","name_org":"Rehfeld, Jens F","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trine R","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Trine R","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25536209"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2014-1658","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of clinical endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"100"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924985110"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-27c8d46f-d339-4abd-b879-bde9779b2a61"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improvements in glucose metabolism early after gastric bypass surgery are not explained by increases in total bile acids and fibroblast growth factor 19 concentrations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-417241","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB) involves exclusion of major parts of the stomach and changes in admixture of gastro-pancreatic enzymes, which could have a major impact on protein digestion and amino acid absorption. OBJECTIVE: We investigated the effect of RYGB on amino acid appearance in the systemic circulation from orally ingested protein and from endogenous release. DESIGN: Nine obese glucose-tolerant subjects, with a mean body mass index (in kg/m(2)) of 39.2 (95% CI: 35.2, 43.3) and mean glycated hemoglobin of 5.3% (95% CI: 4.9%, 5.6%), were studied before and 3 mo after RYGB. Leucine and phenylalanine kinetics were determined under basal conditions and during 4 postprandial hours by intravenous infusions of [3,3,3-(2)H3]-leucine and [ring-(2)D5]-phenylalanine combined with ingestion of [1-(13)C]-leucine intrinsically labeled caseinate as the sole protein source of the meal. Changes in body composition were assessed by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. RESULTS: After RYGB, basal plasma leucine concentration did not change, but marked changes were seen postprandially with 1.7-fold increased peak concentrations (before—mean: 217 μmol/L; 95% CI: 191, 243 μmol/L; 3 mo—mean: 377 μmol/L; 95% CI: 252, 502 μmol/L; P = 0.012) and 2-fold increased incremental AUC (before-mean: 4.1 mmol ∙ min/L; 95% CI: 2.7, 5.5 mmol ∙ min/L; 3 mo-mean: 9.5 mmol ∙ min/L; 95% CI: 4.9, 14.2 mmol ∙ min/L; P = 0.032). However, the postprandial hyperleucinemia was transient, and concentrations were below basal concentrations in the fourth postprandial hour. These concentration differences were mainly caused by changes in leucine appearance rate from orally ingested caseinate: peak rate increased nearly 3-fold [before—mean: 0.5 μmol/(kg fat-free mass ∙ min); 95% CI: 0.4, 0.5 μmol/(kg fat-free mass ∙ min); 3 mo—mean 1.4 μmol/(kg fat-free mass ∙ min); 95% CI: 0.8, 1.9 μmol/(kg fat-free mass ∙ min); P = 0.002], and time to peak was much shorter (before—mean: 173 min; 95% CI: 137, 209 min; 3 mo—mean: 65 min; 95% CI: 46, 84 min; P < 0.001). Only minor changes were seen in endogenous leucine release after RYGB. CONCLUSIONS: RYGB accelerates caseinate digestion and amino acid absorption, resulting in faster and higher but more transient postprandial elevation of plasma amino acids. Changes are likely mediated by accelerated intestinal nutrient entry and clearly demonstrate that protein digestion is not impaired after RYGB. This trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov as NCT01559792.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bojsen-Møller, Anna Kirstine","Jacobsen, Siv H","Dirksen, Carsten","Jørgensen, Nils B","Reitelseder, Søren","Jensen, Jens-Erik B","Kristiansen, Viggo B","Holst, Jens Juul","van Hall, Gerrit","Madsbad, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505539"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accelerated protein digestion and amino acid absorption after roux en y gastric bypass","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-505539","identifier":[{"id":"84941656594","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26245808","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-bbd41bc8-ce1a-4e80-9e39-397f16860f71"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-432B79AD963AF5E4258506E180593CF8"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anna Kirstine","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Anna Kirstine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Siv H","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Siv H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nils B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Søren","key":"reitelsederpau","last":"Reitelseder","locid":"a025a25f-6413-49d5-a5f0-72729ec0a20a","name":"Reitelseder, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens-Erik B","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens-Erik B","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viggo B","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Viggo B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gerrit","key":"vanhallpau","last":"van Hall","locid":"55a9b111-6dbb-4a42-a9ab-d5f3785fbdae","name":"van Hall, Gerrit","orcid":"0000-0002-2519-8127","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26245808"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3945/ajcn.115.109298","issn":["00029165","19383207"],"issn_org":["00029165"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"600-7","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","title_org":"The American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941656594"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bbd41bc8-ce1a-4e80-9e39-397f16860f71"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accelerated protein digestion and amino acid absorption after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505539","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"X chromosomes are unusual in many regards, not least of which is their nonrandom gene content. The causes of this bias are commonly discussed in the context of sexual antagonism and the avoidance of activity in the male germline. Here, we examine the notion that, at least in some taxa, functionally biased gene content may more profoundly be shaped by limits imposed on gene expression owing to haploid expression of the X chromosome. Notably, if the X, as in primates, is transcribed at rates comparable to the ancestral rate (per promoter) prior to the X chromosome formation, then the X is not a tolerable environment for genes with very high maximal net levels of expression, owing to transcriptional traffic jams. We test this hypothesis using The Encyclopedia of DNA Elements (ENCODE) and data from the Functional Annotation of the Mammalian Genome (FANTOM5) project. As predicted, the maximal expression of human X-linked genes is much lower than that of genes on autosomes: on average, maximal expression is three times lower on the X chromosome than on autosomes. Similarly, autosome-to-X retroposition events are associated with lower maximal expression of retrogenes on the X than seen for X-to-autosome retrogenes on autosomes. Also as expected, X-linked genes have a lesser degree of increase in gene expression than autosomal ones (compared to the human/Chimpanzee common ancestor) if highly expressed, but not if lowly expressed. The traffic jam model also explains the known lower breadth of expression for genes on the X (and the Z of birds), as genes with broad expression are, on average, those with high maximal expression. As then further predicted, highly expressed tissue-specific genes are also rare on the X and broadly expressed genes on the X tend to be lowly expressed, both indicating that the trend is shaped by the maximal expression level not the breadth of expression per se. Importantly, a limit to the maximal expression level explains biased tissue of expression profiles of X-linked genes. Tissues whose tissue-specific genes are very highly expressed (e.g., secretory tissues, tissues abundant in structural proteins) are also tissues in which gene expression is relatively rare on the X chromosome. These trends cannot be fully accounted for in terms of alternative models of biased expression. In conclusion, the notion that it is hard for genes on the Therian X to be highly expressed, owing to transcriptional traffic jams, provides a simple yet robustly supported rationale of many peculiar features of X’s gene content, gene expression, and evolution.","author_count":262,"contributors":["Hurst, Laurence D.","Ghanbarian, Avazeh T.","Forrest, Alistair R R","Huminiecki, Lukasz","Rehli, Michael","Kenneth Baillie, J.","de Hoon, Michiel J L","Haberle, Vanja","Lassmann, Timo","Kulakovskiy, Ivan V.","Lizio, Marina","Itoh, Masayoshi","Andersson, Robin","Mungall, Christopher J.","Meehan, Terrence F.","Schmeier, Sebastian","Bertin, Nicolas","Jørgensen, Mette","Dimont, Emmanuel","Arner, Erik","Schmidl, Christian","Schaefer, Ulf","Medvedeva, Yulia A.","Plessy, Charles","Vitezic, Morana","Severin, Jessica","Semple, Colin A.","Ishizu, Yuri","Young, Robert S.","Francescatto, Margherita","Alam, Intikhab","Albanese, Davide","Altschuler, Gabriel M.","Arakawa, Takahiro","Archer, John A C","Arner, Peter","Babina, Magda","Baker, Sarah","Balwierz, Piotr J.","Beckhouse, Anthony G.","Pradhan, Swati Bhatt","Blake, Judith A.","Blumenthal, Antje","Bodega, Beatrice","Bonetti, Alessandro","Briggs, James","Brombacher, Frank","Maxwell Burroughs, A.","Califano, Andrea","Cannistraci, Carlo V.","Carbajo, Daniel","Chen, Yun","Chierici, Marco","Ciani, Yari","Clevers, Hans C.","Dalla, Emiliano","Davis, Carrie A.","Detmar, Michael","Diehl, Alexander D.","Dohi, Taeko","Drabløs, Finn","Edge, Albert S B","Edinger, Matthias","Ekwall, Karl","Endoh, Mitsuhiro","Enomoto, Hideki","Fagiolini, Michela","Fairbairn, Lynsey","Fang, Hai","Farach-Carson, Mary C.","Fau