{"abstract":"Petroleum reservoirs are subsurface formations of porous rocks with hydrocarbons trapped in the pores. Initially, the reservoir pressure may be sufficiently large to push the fluids to the production facilities. However, as the fluids are produced the pressure declines and production reduces over time. When the natural pressure becomes insufficient, the pressure must be maintained artificially by injection of water. Conventional technologies for recovery leaves more than 50% of the oil in the reservoir. Wells with adjustable downhole flow control devices coupled with modern control technology offer the potential to increase the oil recovery significantly. In optimal control of smart wells, downhole sensor equipment and remotely controlled valves are used in combination with large-scale subsurface flow models and gradient based optimization methods in a Nonlinear Model Predictive Control framework to increase the production and economic value of an oil reservoir. Wether the objective is to maximize recovery or some financial measure like Net Present Value, the increased production is achieved by manipulation of the well rates and bottom-hole pressures of the injection and production wells. The optimal water injection rates and production well bottom-hole pressures are computed by solution of a large-scale constrained optimal control problem. The objective is to maximize production by manipulating the well rates and bottom hole pressures of injection and production wells. Optimal control settings of injection and production wells are computed by solution of a large scale constrained optimal control problem. We describe a gradient based method to compute the optimal control strategy of the water flooding process. An explicit singly diagonally implicit Runge-Kutta (ESDIRK) method with adaptive stepsize control is used for computationally efficient solution of the model. The gradients are computed by the adjoint method. The adjoint equations associated with the ESDIRK method are solved by integrating backwards in time. The necessary information for the adjoint computation is calculated and stored during the forward solution of the model. The backward adjoint computation then only requires the assembly of this information to compute the gradients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Völcker, Carsten","Jørgensen, John Bagterp","Thomsen, Per Grove","Stenby, Erling Halfdan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311439"],"event":{"end":"2012-01-27","place":"Kongens Lyngby, dk","start":"2012-01-25","title":"17th Nordic Process Control Workshop","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"production optimization for two phase flow in an oil reservoir","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6596784/IMM08.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311439","ids":["dtu-16d23e04-f754-479f-b57a-be269ca45b1b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-34EF1E3D1E97A930B2FFF7EABE412041"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6596784/IMM08.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://npcw17.imm.dtu.dk/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Energy Resources Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling, Scientific Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"völckerpau","last":"Völcker","locid":"c3f83288-e76c-48d8-bb93-cedc1ae0d972","name":"Völcker, Carsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d2bc6de4-a5c6-43f7-8712-606bd02a88e9","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","orcid":"0000-0001-9799-2808","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Grove","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"86ccc604-cc59-4554-9525-868f11c75311","name":"Thomsen, Per Grove","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erling Halfdan","key":"stenbypau","last":"Stenby","locid":"08d1917e-6211-4ea5-8ac3-7959d122b86a","name":"Stenby, Erling Halfdan","orcid":"0000-0002-2296-069X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenpedh","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Kjøbsted","key":"huusompedh","last":"Huusom","name":"Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gürkan","key":"sinpedh","last":"Sin","name":"Sin, Gürkan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788764309461"],"pages":"198","place":"Kogens Lyngby","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th Nordic Process Control Workshop"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-16d23e04-f754-479f-b57a-be269ca45b1b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Production Optimization for Two-Phase Flow in an Oil Reservoir","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311439","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Perfluorinated compounds (PFCs) have emerged as important food contaminants. They cause immune suppression in a rodent model at serum concentrations similar to those occurring in the US population, but adverse health effects of PFC exposure are poorly understood.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Grandjean, Philippe","Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","Budtz-Jørgensen, Esben","Nielsen, Flemming","Mølbak, Kåre","Weihe, Pal","Heilmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477563"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibody Formation","Child","Child Preschool","Denmark","Diphtheria Toxoid","Environmental Exposure","Female","Fluorocarbons","Food Contamination","Humans","Immune Tolerance","Immunity Humoral","Immunization","Male","Maternal Exposure","Milk Human","Odds Ratio","Polychlorinated biphenyls","Pregnancy","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects","Prospective Studies","Seafood","Tetanus Toxoid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"serum vaccine antibody concentrations in children exposed to perfluorinated compounds","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.2011.2034","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477563","identifier":[{"id":"22274686","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84856182161","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4402650","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8cac4966-8ef9-4872-b5b0-4814e7f39de3"],"keyword":["Antibody Formation","Child","Child, Preschool","Denmark","Diphtheria Toxoid","Environmental Exposure","Female","Fluorocarbons","Food Contamination","Humans","Immune Tolerance","Immunity, Humoral","Immunization","Male","Maternal Exposure","Milk, Human","Odds Ratio","Polychlorinated Biphenyls","Pregnancy","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects","Prospective Studies","Seafood","Tetanus Toxoid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-43DB945B313454F7FA39EECC2DBBC1F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.2011.2034","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Medical Genetics Program","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Philippe","key":"grandjeanpau","last":"Grandjean","name":"Grandjean, Philippe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth Wreford","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Esben","key":"budtzjørgensenpau","last":"Budtz-Jørgensen","locid":"c4ebc45c-df67-437e-a5e9-bdaa629d7caa","name":"Budtz-Jørgensen, Esben","orcid":"0000-0002-5551-0724","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Flemming","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kåre","key":"mølbakpau","last":"Mølbak","name":"Mølbak, Kåre","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pal","key":"weihepau","last":"Weihe","name":"Weihe, Pal","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"heilmannpau","last":"Heilmann","locid":"22b3139f-7d03-4690-8102-0b40a11bc60d","name":"Heilmann, Carsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22274686"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jama.2011.2034","issn":["00987484","15383598"],"issue":"4","journal":"JAMA","pages":"391-7","status":"p","title":"JAMA","title_org":"JAMA : the journal of the American Medical Association","volume":"307"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84856182161"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8cac4966-8ef9-4872-b5b0-4814e7f39de3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Serum vaccine antibody concentrations in children exposed to perfluorinated compounds","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477563","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Baagrund: Effekten af fysisk aktivitet og ikke mindst inaktivitet er veldokumenteret og har banet vejen frem mod ideen om det fysisk aktive sygehus, som også Aalborg sygehus arbejder aktivt med. Når ældre og svage patienter taber funktionniveau under indlæggelse er der stor risiko for at de aldrig genvinder disse igen.(1) Der er desuden god dokumentation for at også ældre patienter med demens kan forbedre funktionsniveau ved træning.(2) Særligt styrketræning af underekstremiteterne med høj intensitet, har vist sig at være effektivt. Hvilket blandt andet har kunnet registreres med ”Timed up and go” testen. Monitoreringen af patienternes fysiske aktivitet er i højere grad blevet muligt med den teknologiske udvikling af bl.a. acellerometre, GPS, skridttællere, gyro, pulsmålere og kombinationer af disse. Sammenlignet med øvrige afdelinger i Danmark, ser der ud til at være et potentiale for forbedring af Bartehl scoren under indlæggelse på aalborg sygehus.(3) Årsagerne til den beskedne fremgang kan skyldes den manglende fysiske aktivitet hos de indlagte patienter. Formålet med dette projekt er således: 1. At beskrive den tid (gennemsnitligt pr dag) patienterne er stående/gående fra indlæggelse til udskrivelse? 2. At undersøge hvilken betydning tiden stående/gående har for ændringen i Barthel Index under indlæggelsen. Metode: Undersøgelsen gennemføres som et observationssstudie af aktivitetsniveau fra indlæggelse til udskrivelse for patienter indlagt på geriatrisk afdeling Aalborg sygehus. Timed up and Go (TUG), rejse-sætte sig testen og Barthel score registreres for alle patienter ved indlæggelse og udskrivelse. Øvrige oplysninger vedrørende alder, køn, vægt, højde, demens, depression, årsag til indlæggelse, boligform, og pårørende indhentes fra journalen. Primær outcome for undersøgelsen er den samlede daglige tid patienten er helholdvis stående og gående. Inklusionskriterier: Mindst indlagt på geriatrisk afd. i 48 timer og henvist til fysio og/eller ergoterapi. Eksklusionskriterier: Døende. Fjerner ActivPal accellorometer fra lårets forside. Kontraindikationer, som forhindrer mobilisering til stående/gående under den første uge af indlæggelsen. Patientens ønsker ikke at deltage Analyse plan: 1. Deskriptiv analyse af den samlede tid stående/gående under indlæggelse, tid stående/gående i indlæggelsens første døgn, udskrivelsens sidste døgn og ændringen fra indlæggelse til udskrivelse. 2. Andel af patienterne som ikke bliver mere stående/gående under indlæggelsen. 3. Er der en sammenhæng mellem gennemsnitlig daglig tid gående/stående og indlæggelsestiden justeret for Barthel score ved indlæggelse. Etiske overvejelser: Projektet er godkendt af Videnskabsetisk komite Nordjylland til at køre som et kvalitetssikrringsprojekt. Reference List (1) Covinsky KE, Palmer RM, Fortinsky RH, Counsell SR, Stewart AL, Kresevic D, et al. Loss of independence in activities of daily living in older adults hospitalized with medical illnesses: increased vulnerability with age. J Am Geriatr Soc 2003 Apr;51(4):451-8. (2) Potter R, Ellard D, Rees K, Thorogood M. A systematic review of the effects of physical activity on physical functioning, quality of life and depression in older people with dementia. Int J Geriatr Psychiatry 2011 Oct;26(10):1000-11. (3) Årsrapport 2010 - DEN LANDSDÆKKENDE KVALITETSDATABASE FOR GERIATRI. Kompetencecenter for Landsdækkende Kliniske kvalitetsdatabaser (øst); 2011.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Villumsen, Morten","Jørgensen, Martin Grønbech","Andreasen, Jane","Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","Mølgaard, Carsten"],"cuid":["S02-099.29-025989"],"event":{"end":"2012-11-28","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2012-11-28","title":"Forsknings- og Udviklingssymposium for Fysioterapeuter, Region Nordjylland","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Fysioterapi","Fysisk aktivitet","Geriatri","Monitering"],"level":"sc